"Session 1 Retrieval Quiz"},"id":"week2-session1-retrieval-title","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"heading","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"correctOptionId":"b","feedback":{"correct":"Cyber security is the protection of systems, networks and data from threats that could affect confidentiality, integrity or availability.","incorrect":"Cyber security is the protection of systems, networks and data from threats that could affect confidentiality, integrity or availability."},"formative":true,"options":[{"id":"a","label":"Installing every software update on the same day it is released"},{"id":"b","label":"Protecting systems, networks and data from unauthorised access, damage or disruption"},{"id":"c","label":"Blocking all external email to remove phishing risk"},{"id":"d","label":"Using social media policies to control staff behaviour"}],"prompt":"Which statement best describes cyber security?","questionId":"week2-session1-retrieval:s1-q1","sourceQuestionId":"s1-q1","sourceType":"single"},"id":"week2-session1-retrieval-q-1-s1-q1","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"single-choice","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"correctOptionId":"b","feedback":{"correct":"Confidentiality means only authorised people can view or obtain the information.","incorrect":"Confidentiality means only authorised people can view or obtain the information."},"formative":true,"options":[{"id":"a","label":"Information is available whenever authorised users need it"},{"id":"b","label":"Information can only be accessed by people who are authorised to see it"},{"id":"c","label":"Information is never changed once it has been saved"},{"id":"d","label":"Information is backed up to an off-site location"}],"prompt":"What does confidentiality mean in the CIA triad?","questionId":"week2-session1-retrieval:s1-q2","sourceQuestionId":"s1-q2","sourceType":"single"},"id":"week2-session1-retrieval-q-2-s1-q2","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"single-choice","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"correctOptionId":"a","feedback":{"correct":"Integrity means information remains complete, accurate and trustworthy.","incorrect":"Integrity means information remains complete, accurate and trustworthy."},"formative":true,"options":[{"id":"a","label":"Information is accurate and has not been altered without authorisation"},{"id":"b","label":"Information is encrypted while it travels across a network"},{"id":"c","label":"Information is deleted after a set retention period"},{"id":"d","label":"Information is shared only inside the organisation"}],"prompt":"What does integrity mean in the CIA triad?","questionId":"week2-session1-retrieval:s1-q3","sourceQuestionId":"s1-q3","sourceType":"single"},"id":"week2-session1-retrieval-q-3-s1-q3","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"single-choice","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"correctOptionId":"b","feedback":{"correct":"Availability means authorised users can access systems and data when required.","incorrect":"Availability means authorised users can access systems and data when required."},"formative":true,"options":[{"id":"a","label":"Information is hidden from everyone except senior managers"},{"id":"b","label":"Authorised users can access systems and information when they need them"},{"id":"c","label":"Information is copied to paper records for legal reasons"},{"id":"d","label":"Information is never stored on portable devices"}],"prompt":"What does availability mean in the CIA triad?","questionId":"week2-session1-retrieval:s1-q4","sourceQuestionId":"s1-q4","sourceType":"single"},"id":"week2-session1-retrieval-q-4-s1-q4","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"single-choice","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"correctOptionId":"b","feedback":{"correct":"Unauthorised access is a cyber security incident because it threatens confidentiality of sensitive data.","incorrect":"Unauthorised access is a cyber security incident because it threatens confidentiality of sensitive data."},"formative":true,"options":[{"id":"a","label":"A planned staff training day"},{"id":"b","label":"Unauthorised access to patient records"},{"id":"c","label":"Ordering new networked printers"},{"id":"d","label":"Updating a meeting room booking"}],"prompt":"Which of the following is a type of cyber security incident?","questionId":"week2-session1-retrieval:s1-q5","sourceQuestionId":"s1-q5","sourceType":"single"},"id":"week2-session1-retrieval-q-5-s1-q5","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"single-choice","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"correctOptionId":"b","feedback":{"correct":"Personal data must be protected to reduce harm to individuals and to meet legal and ethical duties.","incorrect":"Personal data must be protected to reduce harm to individuals and to meet legal and ethical duties."},"formative":true,"options":[{"id":"a","label":"Because personal data is never useful to an attacker"},{"id":"b","label":"Because loss or misuse can harm individuals and may breach data protection law"},{"id":"c","label":"Because personal data is always encrypted automatically"},{"id":"d","label":"Because personal data only exists on paper forms"}],"prompt":"Why must personal data be protected?","questionId":"week2-session1-retrieval:s1-q6","sourceQuestionId":"s1-q6","sourceType":"single"},"id":"week2-session1-retrieval-q-6-s1-q6","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"single-choice","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"correctOptionId":"b","feedback":{"correct":"Organisational data supports services and decision-making; compromise can halt operations and damage trust.","incorrect":"Organisational data supports services and decision-making; compromise can halt operations and damage trust."},"formative":true,"options":[{"id":"a","label":"Organisational data has no commercial or operational value"},{"id":"b","label":"Loss or alteration can disrupt services, damage reputation and create financial cost"},{"id":"c","label":"Organisational data is always publicly available"},{"id":"d","label":"Only personal data can be involved in an incident"}],"prompt":"Why must organisational data be protected?","questionId":"week2-session1-retrieval:s1-q7","sourceQuestionId":"s1-q7","sourceType":"single"},"id":"week2-session1-retrieval-q-7-s1-q7","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"single-choice","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"correctOptionId":"b","feedback":{"correct":"State and critical public-sector information can affect security and public safety if exposed or disrupted.","incorrect":"State and critical public-sector information can affect security and public safety if exposed or disrupted."},"formative":true,"options":[{"id":"a","label":"State information is only used for marketing campaigns"},{"id":"b","label":"Compromise can affect national security, critical services or public safety"},{"id":"c","label":"State information is never connected to digital systems"},{"id":"d","label":"State information is less sensitive than social media posts"}],"prompt":"Why must state information be protected?","questionId":"week2-session1-retrieval:s1-q8","sourceQuestionId":"s1-q8","sourceType":"single"},"id":"week2-session1-retrieval-q-8-s1-q8","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"single-choice","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"correctOptionId":"c","feedback":{"correct":"If staff cannot open records when needed, availability is affected. Confidentiality may also be at risk in some ransomware cases, but the clearest evidence here is loss of access.","incorrect":"If staff cannot open records when needed, availability is affected. Confidentiality may also be at risk in some ransomware cases, but the clearest evidence here is loss of access."},"formative":true,"options":[{"id":"a","label":"Confidentiality only"},{"id":"b","label":"Integrity only"},{"id":"c","label":"Availability"},{"id":"d","label":"None of the CIA aims"}],"prompt":"At Northbank, which CIA aim is mainly affected if appointment records become unreadable after ransomware?","questionId":"week2-session1-retrieval:s1-q9","sourceQuestionId":"s1-q9","sourceType":"single"},"id":"week2-session1-retrieval-q-9-s1-q9","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"single-choice","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"correctOptionId":"b","feedback":{"correct":"Incidents can arise from many causes and may affect confidentiality, integrity, availability or a combination.","incorrect":"Incidents can arise from many causes and may affect confidentiality, integrity, availability or a combination."},"formative":true,"options":[{"id":"a","label":"They only happen when malware is involved"},{"id":"b","label":"They can involve people, processes or technology and may affect one or more CIA aims"},{"id":"c","label":"They always destroy data permanently"},{"id":"d","label":"They only matter if personal data is stolen"}],"prompt":"Which statement is true about cyber security incidents?","questionId":"week2-session1-retrieval:s1-q10","sourceQuestionId":"s1-q10","sourceType":"single"},"id":"week2-session1-retrieval-q-10-s1-q10","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"single-choice","version":"0.1.0"}],"id":"week2-session1-retrieval","metadata":{"activityType":"Retrieval quiz","href":null,"runtimeGlobal":"Week2Session1Retrieval","status":"available","summary":"Session 1 Retrieval Quiz","title":"Session 1 Retrieval Quiz"},"relationships":{"assets":[],"assignment":"formative-practice","learningOutcomes":["LO1"],"questions":[]},"schema":"lp.content.activity","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","version":"1.0.0"},{"blocks":[{"content":{"level":2,"text":"Threats and Vulnerabilities Learning"},"id":"week2-threat-vulnerability-learning-title","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"heading","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"correctOptionId":"b","feedback":{"correct":"The key relationship: a threat exploits a vulnerability, which leads to a cyber security incident.","incorrect":"The key relationship: a threat exploits a vulnerability, which leads to a cyber security incident."},"formative":true,"options":[{"id":"a","label":"A vulnerability creates a threat automatically"},{"id":"b","label":"A threat exploits a vulnerability to cause an incident"},{"id":"c","label":"Threats and vulnerabilities are interchangeable terms"},{"id":"d","label":"An incident happens only when hardware fails"}],"prompt":"Which statement best describes the relationship between threats and vulnerabilities?","questionId":"week2-threat-vulnerability-learning:tv-q1","sourceQuestionId":"tv-q1","sourceType":"single"},"id":"week2-threat-vulnerability-learning-q-1-tv-q1","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"single-choice","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"correctOptionId":"b","feedback":{"correct":"The phisher is the threat \u2014 the actor attempting to cause harm. Trusting the email is the vulnerability.","incorrect":"The phisher is the threat \u2014 the actor attempting to cause harm. Trusting the email is the vulnerability."},"formative":true,"options":[{"id":"a","label":"Staff who trust emails without checking"},{"id":"b","label":"The phisher sending a convincing fake email"},{"id":"c","label":"Stolen login credentials"},{"id":"d","label":"The email filtering software"}],"prompt":"In the Northbank phishing example, what is the threat?","questionId":"week2-threat-vulnerability-learning:tv-q2","sourceQuestionId":"tv-q2","sourceType":"single"},"id":"week2-threat-vulnerability-learning-q-2-tv-q2","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"single-choice","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"correctOptionId":"b","feedback":{"correct":"Human behaviour \u2014 trusting a message without verification \u2014 is the weakness the threat exploits.","incorrect":"Human behaviour \u2014 trusting a message without verification \u2014 is the weakness the threat exploits."},"formative":true,"options":[{"id":"a","label":"The phisher sending a convincing fake email"},{"id":"b","label":"A staff member trusting the email without verifying the sender"},{"id":"c","label":"The cyber security incident report form"},{"id":"d","label":"The organisation's brand logo"}],"prompt":"In the Northbank phishing example, what is the vulnerability?","questionId":"week2-threat-vulnerability-learning:tv-q3","sourceQuestionId":"tv-q3","sourceType":"single"},"id":"week2-threat-vulnerability-learning-q-3-tv-q3","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"single-choice","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"correctOptionId":"b","feedback":{"correct":"Missing patches leave a known weakness that malware or attackers can exploit. That is a vulnerability.","incorrect":"Missing patches leave a known weakness that malware or attackers can exploit. That is a vulnerability."},"formative":true,"options":[{"id":"a","label":"A threat"},{"id":"b","label":"A vulnerability"},{"id":"c","label":"An incident"},{"id":"d","label":"A control"}],"prompt":"Unpatched software on a server is best classified as\u2026","questionId":"week2-threat-vulnerability-learning:tv-q4","sourceQuestionId":"tv-q4","sourceType":"single"},"id":"week2-threat-vulnerability-learning-q-4-tv-q4","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"single-choice","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"correctOptionId":"b","feedback":{"correct":"A ransomware operator is a threat actor. The other options describe weaknesses that could be exploited.","incorrect":"A ransomware operator is a threat actor. The other options describe weaknesses that could be exploited."},"formative":true,"options":[{"id":"a","label":"An unlocked server room cabinet"},{"id":"b","label":"A ransomware operator"},{"id":"c","label":"Weak password policy"},{"id":"d","label":"Out-of-date antivirus definitions"}],"prompt":"Which of the following is a threat rather than a vulnerability?","questionId":"week2-threat-vulnerability-learning:tv-q5","sourceQuestionId":"tv-q5","sourceType":"single"},"id":"week2-threat-vulnerability-learning-q-5-tv-q5","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"single-choice","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"correctOptionId":"c","feedback":{"correct":"The incident is the harmful outcome: compromised systems and disrupted services. Malware is the threat; the unpatched flaw is the vulnerability.","incorrect":"The incident is the harmful outcome: compromised systems and disrupted services. Malware is the threat; the unpatched flaw is the vulnerability."},"formative":true,"options":[{"id":"a","label":"The malware itself"},{"id":"b","label":"The missing patch"},{"id":"c","label":"Systems are compromised and services may be disrupted"},{"id":"d","label":"The vendor who released the patch"}],"prompt":"Systems compromised after malware exploits an unpatched flaw \u2014 what is the incident outcome?","questionId":"week2-threat-vulnerability-learning:tv-q6","sourceQuestionId":"tv-q6","sourceType":"single"},"id":"week2-threat-vulnerability-learning-q-6-tv-q6","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"single-choice","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"format":"application/json","text":"```json\n{\n  \"formula\": \"A threat exploits a vulnerability to cause a cyber security incident.\",\n  \"definitions\": {\n    \"threat\": {\n      \"term\": \"Threat\",\n      \"text\": \"A threat is a person, group or event that could deliberately or accidentally harm systems, networks or data. Threats include cyber criminals, malicious insiders, ransomware operators and social engineers.\"\n    },\n    \"vulnerability\": {\n      \"term\": \"Vulnerability\",\n      \"text\": \"A vulnerability is a weakness in a system, process or behaviour that a threat could use. Examples include weak passwords, missing software patches, unlocked doors and staff who trust phishing emails without checking.\"\n    },\n    \"incident\": {\n      \"term\": \"Cyber security incident\",\n      \"text\": \"An incident is the harmful outcome when a threat successfully exploits a vulnerability. It may affect confidentiality, integrity, availability or a combination of CIA aims.\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"workedExamples\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"ex-phishing\",\n      \"title\": \"Phishing at Northbank\",\n      \"threat\": \"A phisher sends a convincing fake email.\",\n      \"vulnerability\": \"A staff member trusts the email and does not verify the sender.\",\n      \"incident\": \"Login credentials are stolen and an attacker accesses internal systems.\",\n      \"ciaNote\": \"Confidentiality is affected when unauthorised people obtain account access.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"ex-malware\",\n      \"title\": \"Malware through unpatched software\",\n      \"threat\": \"Malware designed to spread across a network.\",\n      \"vulnerability\": \"A server runs software that has not been patched against a known flaw.\",\n      \"incident\": \"Systems are compromised and services become unavailable.\",\n      \"ciaNote\": \"Availability and integrity may both be affected depending on what the malware does.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"misconceptions\": [\n    {\n      \"myth\": \"A threat and a vulnerability are the same thing.\",\n      \"reality\": \"A threat is the danger source; a vulnerability is the weakness that can be exploited. Both must be present for an incident to occur.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"myth\": \"Technology alone causes incidents.\",\n      \"reality\": \"People and processes matter too. Poor training, weak policies and human error are common vulnerabilities.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"myth\": \"If you have a firewall, you have no vulnerabilities.\",\n      \"reality\": \"Controls reduce risk but do not remove every weakness. Misconfigured rules, unpatched software and social engineering can still succeed.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"comparisonPoints\": [\n    {\n      \"aspect\": \"What it is\",\n      \"threat\": \"The potential cause of harm (who or what might attack)\",\n      \"vulnerability\": \"The weakness that could be exploited (what is unprotected or flawed)\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"aspect\": \"Example at Northbank\",\n      \"threat\": \"A scammer calling reception pretending to be IT support\",\n      \"vulnerability\": \"Staff have not been trained to verify unexpected support calls\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"aspect\": \"Can you remove it completely?\",\n      \"threat\": \"You cannot eliminate all threats, but you can reduce exposure\",\n      \"vulnerability\": \"You can fix or reduce many vulnerabilities through controls and training\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"aspect\": \"OCR exam focus\",\n      \"threat\": \"Name the actor or attack method clearly\",\n      \"vulnerability\": \"Identify the specific weakness \u2014 technical, physical or human\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```"},"id":"week2-threat-vulnerability-learning-source-remainder","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"markdown","version":"0.1.0"}],"id":"week2-threat-vulnerability-learning","metadata":{"activityType":"Guided learning","href":null,"runtimeGlobal":"Week2ThreatVulnerabilityLearning","status":"available","summary":"Threats and Vulnerabilities Learning","title":"Threats and Vulnerabilities Learning"},"relationships":{"assets":[],"assignment":"formative-practice","learningOutcomes":["LO1"],"questions":[]},"schema":"lp.content.activity","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","version":"1.0.0"},{"blocks":[{"content":{"level":2,"text":"Malware Categories and Symptoms"},"id":"week2-malware-symptoms-title","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"heading","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"correctOptionId":"b","feedback":{"correct":"Worms spread automatically across networks. Viruses usually need a file to be opened.","incorrect":"Worms spread automatically across networks. Viruses usually need a file to be opened."},"formative":true,"options":[{"id":"a","label":"Virus"},{"id":"b","label":"Worm"},{"id":"c","label":"Trojan"},{"id":"d","label":"Adware"}],"prompt":"Which malware type self-replicates across a network without a user opening a host file?","questionId":"week2-malware-symptoms:mw-q1","sourceQuestionId":"mw-q1","sourceType":"single"},"id":"week2-malware-symptoms-q-1-mw-q1","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"single-choice","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"correctOptionId":"b","feedback":{"correct":"Encryption plus a ransom demand is characteristic of ransomware.","incorrect":"Encryption plus a ransom demand is characteristic of ransomware."},"formative":true,"options":[{"id":"a","label":"Spyware"},{"id":"b","label":"Ransomware"},{"id":"c","label":"Adware"},{"id":"d","label":"Rootkit"}],"prompt":"Files are encrypted and a payment demand appears on screen. Which category fits best?","questionId":"week2-malware-symptoms:mw-q2","sourceQuestionId":"mw-q2","sourceType":"single"},"id":"week2-malware-symptoms-q-2-mw-q2","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"single-choice","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"correctOptionId":"b","feedback":{"correct":"Trojans trick users into installing harmful software that looks legitimate.","incorrect":"Trojans trick users into installing harmful software that looks legitimate."},"formative":true,"options":[{"id":"a","label":"Worm"},{"id":"b","label":"Trojan"},{"id":"c","label":"Virus"},{"id":"d","label":"Botnet malware"}],"prompt":"Software disguised as a helpful tool that creates a back door is called a\u2026","questionId":"week2-malware-symptoms:mw-q3","sourceQuestionId":"mw-q3","sourceType":"single"},"id":"week2-malware-symptoms-q-3-mw-q3","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"single-choice","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"correctOptionId":"a","feedback":{"correct":"Spyware steals private information, which mainly threatens confidentiality.","incorrect":"Spyware steals private information, which mainly threatens confidentiality."},"formative":true,"options":[{"id":"a","label":"Confidentiality"},{"id":"b","label":"Integrity only"},{"id":"c","label":"Availability only"},{"id":"d","label":"None of the CIA aims"}],"prompt":"Keystrokes are captured secretly and sent to an attacker. Which CIA aim is mainly affected?","questionId":"week2-malware-symptoms:mw-q4","sourceQuestionId":"mw-q4","sourceType":"single"},"id":"week2-malware-symptoms-q-4-mw-q4","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"single-choice","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"correctOptionId":"b","feedback":{"correct":"Adware focuses on displaying adverts and may track browsing for targeting.","incorrect":"Adware focuses on displaying adverts and may track browsing for targeting."},"formative":true,"options":[{"id":"a","label":"Ransom note demanding Bitcoin"},{"id":"b","label":"Unwanted advert pop-ups and browser redirects"},{"id":"c","label":"All files renamed with a strange extension"},{"id":"d","label":"Device recruited for a DDoS attack with no visible adverts"}],"prompt":"Which symptom is most associated with adware?","questionId":"week2-malware-symptoms:mw-q5","sourceQuestionId":"mw-q5","sourceType":"single"},"id":"week2-malware-symptoms-q-5-mw-q5","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"single-choice","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"correctOptionId":"b","feedback":{"correct":"Worms and botnet malware spread or operate across many devices, causing network strain.","incorrect":"Worms and botnet malware spread or operate across many devices, causing network strain."},"formative":true,"options":[{"id":"a","label":"Adware"},{"id":"b","label":"Worm or botnet malware"},{"id":"c","label":"Spyware only"},{"id":"d","label":"Rootkit only"}],"prompt":"Many devices on the network slow down simultaneously with high traffic. Which category is most likely?","questionId":"week2-malware-symptoms:mw-q6","sourceQuestionId":"mw-q6","sourceType":"single"},"id":"week2-malware-symptoms-q-6-mw-q6","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"single-choice","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"correctOptionId":"b","feedback":{"correct":"Rootkits hide malicious activity from security tools and administrators.","incorrect":"Rootkits hide malicious activity from security tools and administrators."},"formative":true,"options":[{"id":"a","label":"Virus"},{"id":"b","label":"Rootkit"},{"id":"c","label":"Adware"},{"id":"d","label":"Worm"}],"prompt":"Security software finds nothing, but hidden accounts exist. Which category should you suspect?","questionId":"week2-malware-symptoms:mw-q7","sourceQuestionId":"mw-q7","sourceType":"single"},"id":"week2-malware-symptoms-q-7-mw-q7","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"single-choice","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"correctOptionId":"a","feedback":{"correct":"Viruses corrupt or damage files (integrity) and may stop them working (availability).","incorrect":"Viruses corrupt or damage files (integrity) and may stop them working (availability)."},"formative":true,"options":[{"id":"a","label":"Integrity and availability of files"},{"id":"b","label":"Confidentiality only"},{"id":"c","label":"Physical safety only"},{"id":"d","label":"None \u2014 viruses do not affect CIA aims"}],"prompt":"A virus at Northbank is most likely to affect which CIA aims first?","questionId":"week2-malware-symptoms:mw-q8","sourceQuestionId":"mw-q8","sourceType":"single"},"id":"week2-malware-symptoms-q-8-mw-q8","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"single-choice","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"correctOptionId":"a","feedback":{"correct":"Both often arrive through social engineering such as phishing emails.","incorrect":"Both often arrive through social engineering such as phishing emails."},"formative":true,"options":[{"id":"a","label":"Phishing emails with malicious links or attachments"},{"id":"b","label":"Only physical theft of paper records"},{"id":"c","label":"Scheduled automatic OS updates"},{"id":"d","label":"Staff training sessions"}],"prompt":"Which delivery method is common to both trojans and ransomware?","questionId":"week2-malware-symptoms:mw-q9","sourceQuestionId":"mw-q9","sourceType":"single"},"id":"week2-malware-symptoms-q-9-mw-q9","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"single-choice","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"correctOptionId":"a","feedback":{"correct":"Botnet malware turns devices into remotely controlled bots for tasks such as sending spam.","incorrect":"Botnet malware turns devices into remotely controlled bots for tasks such as sending spam."},"formative":true,"options":[{"id":"a","label":"Botnet malware"},{"id":"b","label":"Adware"},{"id":"c","label":"Virus"},{"id":"d","label":"Spyware"}],"prompt":"A device sends spam emails while idle. Which malware category best explains this?","questionId":"week2-malware-symptoms:mw-q10","sourceQuestionId":"mw-q10","sourceType":"single"},"id":"week2-malware-symptoms-q-10-mw-q10","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"single-choice","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"format":"application/json","text":"```json\n{\n  \"categories\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"virus\",\n      \"name\": \"Virus\",\n      \"does\": \"Attaches to legitimate files or programs and spreads when those files are opened or shared.\",\n      \"delivery\": \"Infected email attachments, USB drives, downloaded files.\",\n      \"symptoms\": [\n        \"Files become corrupted or fail to open\",\n        \"Unexpected pop-ups or error messages\",\n        \"Antivirus alerts after opening a file\"\n      ],\n      \"ciaAims\": [\n        \"Integrity\",\n        \"Availability\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"worm\",\n      \"name\": \"Worm\",\n      \"does\": \"Self-replicates across networks without needing a host file to be opened.\",\n      \"delivery\": \"Network shares, unpatched services, removable media, email links.\",\n      \"symptoms\": [\n        \"Sudden network slowdown\",\n        \"Many devices affected at once\",\n        \"Unusual outbound traffic\"\n      ],\n      \"ciaAims\": [\n        \"Availability\",\n        \"Integrity\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"trojan\",\n      \"name\": \"Trojan\",\n      \"does\": \"Disguises itself as useful software to trick users into installing it, then opens a back door.\",\n      \"delivery\": \"Fake downloads, cracked software, malicious email links.\",\n      \"symptoms\": [\n        \"New unknown programs appear\",\n        \"Remote access or changed settings without explanation\",\n        \"Security software disabled\"\n      ],\n      \"ciaAims\": [\n        \"Confidentiality\",\n        \"Integrity\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"ransomware\",\n      \"name\": \"Ransomware\",\n      \"does\": \"Encrypts files or locks systems and demands payment for recovery.\",\n      \"delivery\": \"Phishing emails, exposed remote desktop, drive-by downloads.\",\n      \"symptoms\": [\n        \"Files renamed or unreadable\",\n        \"Ransom note on screen\",\n        \"Systems unusable until payment is demanded\"\n      ],\n      \"ciaAims\": [\n        \"Availability\",\n        \"Integrity\",\n        \"Confidentiality\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"spyware\",\n      \"name\": \"Spyware\",\n      \"does\": \"Secretly monitors activity, keystrokes or data and sends it to an attacker.\",\n      \"delivery\": \"Bundled with free software, malicious adverts, infected downloads.\",\n      \"symptoms\": [\n        \"Browser homepage changes without consent\",\n        \"Slower performance and unknown processes running\",\n        \"Accounts accessed from unusual locations\"\n      ],\n      \"ciaAims\": [\n        \"Confidentiality\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"adware\",\n      \"name\": \"Adware\",\n      \"does\": \"Displays unwanted adverts and may track browsing habits to target ads.\",\n      \"delivery\": \"Free software bundles, browser extensions, misleading download sites.\",\n      \"symptoms\": [\n        \"Constant advert pop-ups\",\n        \"New toolbars or extensions you did not install\",\n        \"Browser redirects to advert pages\"\n      ],\n      \"ciaAims\": [\n        \"Confidentiality\",\n        \"Integrity\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"botnet\",\n      \"name\": \"Botnet malware\",\n      \"does\": \"Turns infected devices into bots controlled remotely, often for DDoS or spam.\",\n      \"delivery\": \"Trojans, exploit kits, weak credentials on IoT devices.\",\n      \"symptoms\": [\n        \"Device runs slowly when idle\",\n        \"High network use with no clear cause\",\n        \"IP address appears in abuse reports\"\n      ],\n      \"ciaAims\": [\n        \"Availability\",\n        \"Integrity\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"rootkit\",\n      \"name\": \"Rootkit\",\n      \"does\": \"Hides deeply in the operating system to maintain persistent hidden access.\",\n      \"delivery\": \"Privilege escalation exploits, trojan installers, compromised installers.\",\n      \"symptoms\": [\n        \"Security tools fail or report nothing despite odd behaviour\",\n        \"System settings change and cannot be reversed easily\",\n        \"Hidden accounts or services\"\n      ],\n      \"ciaAims\": [\n        \"Confidentiality\",\n        \"Integrity\",\n        \"Availability\"\n      ]\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```"},"id":"week2-malware-symptoms-source-remainder","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"markdown","version":"0.1.0"}],"id":"week2-malware-symptoms","metadata":{"activityType":"Knowledge check","href":null,"runtimeGlobal":"Week2MalwareSymptoms","status":"available","summary":"Malware Categories and Symptoms","title":"Malware Categories and Symptoms"},"relationships":{"assets":[],"assignment":"formative-practice","learningOutcomes":["LO1"],"questions":[]},"schema":"lp.content.activity","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","version":"1.0.0"},{"blocks":[{"content":{"level":2,"text":"Threat or Vulnerability Sort"},"id":"week2-threat-vulnerability-sort-title","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"heading","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"categories":[{"id":"vulnerability","label":"vulnerability"},{"id":"threat","label":"threat"}],"formative":true,"items":[{"ambiguityNote":null,"correctCategoryId":"vulnerability","explanation":"A weak, easily guessed password is a weakness in access control \u2014 a vulnerability.","exploitPair":"sort-02","id":"sort-01","text":"Staff member uses Password123 for their work account."},{"ambiguityNote":null,"correctCategoryId":"threat","explanation":"The phisher is the actor attempting harm \u2014 a threat.","exploitPair":"sort-01","id":"sort-02","text":"A phisher sends a fake payroll email."},{"ambiguityNote":"Some learners may focus on malware; the weakness here is the unprotected system.","correctCategoryId":"vulnerability","explanation":"Unsupported software no longer receives security fixes, leaving known weaknesses unpatched.","exploitPair":"sort-09","id":"sort-03","text":"A PC still runs an unsupported operating system."},{"ambiguityNote":null,"correctCategoryId":"vulnerability","explanation":"Physical access without supervision is a weakness that allows theft or tampering.","exploitPair":"sort-07","id":"sort-04","text":"A laptop is left unlocked and unattended in a public area."},{"ambiguityNote":"The fake email could also be seen as social engineering \u2014 classify the attack method as the threat.","correctCategoryId":"threat","explanation":"The ransomware attack (delivered via a deceptive email) is the threat attempting harm.","exploitPair":"sort-11","id":"sort-05","text":"Ransomware arrives in a fake invoice email."},{"ambiguityNote":null,"correctCategoryId":"vulnerability","explanation":"Misconfiguration is a technical weakness that exposes services to attack.","exploitPair":null,"id":"sort-06","text":"Firewall rules allow unnecessary inbound traffic."},{"ambiguityNote":null,"correctCategoryId":"threat","explanation":"The insider acting with harmful intent is a threat.","exploitPair":"sort-04","id":"sort-07","text":"A malicious insider copies sensitive files."},{"ambiguityNote":null,"correctCategoryId":"vulnerability","explanation":"Poor physical security is a vulnerability that allows unauthorised access.","exploitPair":"sort-07","id":"sort-08","text":"A server room cabinet is left unlocked overnight."},{"ambiguityNote":null,"correctCategoryId":"vulnerability","explanation":"An unpatched known flaw is a classic technical vulnerability.","exploitPair":"sort-03","id":"sort-09","text":"A web application has not been patched against a known flaw."},{"ambiguityNote":null,"correctCategoryId":"threat","explanation":"The scammer is a threat actor using social engineering.","exploitPair":"sort-11","id":"sort-10","text":"A scammer calls claiming to be tech support and asks for remote access."},{"ambiguityNote":null,"correctCategoryId":"vulnerability","explanation":"Lack of training is a human/process weakness that makes phishing more likely to succeed.","exploitPair":"sort-05","id":"sort-11","text":"Staff have had no phishing awareness training."},{"ambiguityNote":"If read as \u201cthe stolen account itself\u201d, learners may call it an incident \u2014 the card describes the missing control.","correctCategoryId":"vulnerability","explanation":"Missing multi-factor authentication is the weakness; credential theft is the incident outcome.","exploitPair":null,"id":"sort-12","text":"An admin account was stolen because MFA was not enabled."}],"prompt":"Threat or Vulnerability Sort","questionId":"week2-threat-vulnerability-sort","sourceQuestionId":"week2-threat-vulnerability-sort"},"id":"week2-threat-vulnerability-sort-classification","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"classification","version":"0.1.0"}],"id":"week2-threat-vulnerability-sort","metadata":{"activityType":"Classification","href":null,"runtimeGlobal":"Week2ThreatVulnerabilitySort","status":"available","summary":"Threat or Vulnerability Sort","title":"Threat or Vulnerability Sort"},"relationships":{"assets":[],"assignment":"formative-practice","learningOutcomes":["LO1"],"questions":[]},"schema":"lp.content.activity","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","version":"1.0.0"},{"blocks":[{"content":{"level":2,"text":"TryHackMe: Vulnerabilities 101"},"id":"week2-vulnerabilities101-reflection-title","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"heading","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"text":"TryHackMe: Vulnerabilities 101"},"id":"week2-vulnerabilities101-reflection-intro","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"paragraph","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"format":"application/json","text":"```json\n{\n  \"description\": \"TryHackMe: Vulnerabilities 101\"\n}\n```"},"id":"week2-vulnerabilities101-reflection-source-remainder","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"markdown","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"formative":true,"prompt":"Complete this activity on the learner hub page, then write a short note to confirm you have finished.","questionId":"week2-vulnerabilities101-reflection:learner-note","sourceQuestionId":"learner-note"},"id":"week2-vulnerabilities101-reflection-learner-note","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"reflection","version":"0.1.0"}],"id":"week2-vulnerabilities101-reflection","metadata":{"activityType":"Reflection","href":null,"runtimeGlobal":null,"status":"available","summary":"TryHackMe: Vulnerabilities 101","title":"TryHackMe: Vulnerabilities 101"},"relationships":{"assets":[],"assignment":"formative-practice","learningOutcomes":["LO1"],"questions":[]},"schema":"lp.content.activity","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","version":"1.0.0"},{"blocks":[{"content":{"level":2,"text":"Session 2 Retrieval Quiz"},"id":"week2-session2-retrieval-title","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"heading","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"correctOptionId":"b","feedback":{"correct":"A threat is the potential source of harm \u2014 who or what might attack or cause damage.","incorrect":"A threat is the potential source of harm \u2014 who or what might attack or cause damage."},"formative":true,"options":[{"id":"a","label":"A weakness in a system that could be exploited"},{"id":"b","label":"A person, group or event that could harm systems, networks or data"},{"id":"c","label":"The harmful outcome after an attack succeeds"},{"id":"d","label":"A control that reduces risk"}],"prompt":"Which statement best defines a threat in cyber security?","questionId":"week2-session2-retrieval:s2-q1","sourceQuestionId":"s2-q1","sourceType":"single"},"id":"week2-session2-retrieval-q-1-s2-q1","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"single-choice","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"correctOptionId":"b","feedback":{"correct":"A vulnerability is a flaw or weakness \u2014 unpatched software, misconfiguration or human error.","incorrect":"A vulnerability is a flaw or weakness \u2014 unpatched software, misconfiguration or human error."},"formative":true,"options":[{"id":"a","label":"A ransomware operator attempting to encrypt files"},{"id":"b","label":"A weakness in technology, configuration or behaviour that a threat could exploit"},{"id":"c","label":"A successful login using stolen credentials"},{"id":"d","label":"An antivirus product scanning email attachments"}],"prompt":"Which statement best defines a vulnerability?","questionId":"week2-session2-retrieval:s2-q2","sourceQuestionId":"s2-q2","sourceType":"single"},"id":"week2-session2-retrieval-q-2-s2-q2","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"single-choice","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"correctOptionId":"c","feedback":{"correct":"Both must be present: a threat exploits a vulnerability, which leads to an incident affecting CIA aims.","incorrect":"Both must be present: a threat exploits a vulnerability, which leads to an incident affecting CIA aims."},"formative":true,"options":[{"id":"a","label":"A vulnerability automatically creates a threat"},{"id":"b","label":"Threats and vulnerabilities mean the same thing in OCR exams"},{"id":"c","label":"A threat exploits a vulnerability to cause a cyber security incident"},{"id":"d","label":"An incident happens only when hardware fails"}],"prompt":"What is the correct relationship between threats and vulnerabilities?","questionId":"week2-session2-retrieval:s2-q3","sourceQuestionId":"s2-q3","sourceType":"single"},"id":"week2-session2-retrieval-q-3-s2-q3","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"single-choice","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"correctOptionId":"a","feedback":{"correct":"Ransomware typically encrypts files and demands payment. Users often cannot open affected documents.","incorrect":"Ransomware typically encrypts files and demands payment. Users often cannot open affected documents."},"formative":true,"options":[{"id":"a","label":"Files become encrypted and a ransom note appears"},{"id":"b","label":"The mouse pointer moves without user input only"},{"id":"c","label":"The printer runs out of toner"},{"id":"d","label":"Email signatures change automatically"}],"prompt":"Which symptom is most commonly associated with ransomware?","questionId":"week2-session2-retrieval:s2-q4","sourceQuestionId":"s2-q4","sourceType":"single"},"id":"week2-session2-retrieval-q-4-s2-q4","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"single-choice","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"correctOptionId":"a","feedback":{"correct":"Unpatched or outdated application code is a software vulnerability \u2014 a weakness in the program itself.","incorrect":"Unpatched or outdated application code is a software vulnerability \u2014 a weakness in the program itself."},"formative":true,"options":[{"id":"a","label":"A software vulnerability"},{"id":"b","label":"A hardware vulnerability"},{"id":"c","label":"A configuration vulnerability"},{"id":"d","label":"A human behaviour vulnerability"}],"prompt":"Out-of-date web server software with a known security flaw is best classified as\u2026","questionId":"week2-session2-retrieval:s2-q5","sourceQuestionId":"s2-q5","sourceType":"single"},"id":"week2-session2-retrieval-q-5-s2-q5","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"single-choice","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"correctOptionId":"b","feedback":{"correct":"Physical access to hardware without proper protection is a hardware (physical) vulnerability.","incorrect":"Physical access to hardware without proper protection is a hardware (physical) vulnerability."},"formative":true,"options":[{"id":"a","label":"A software vulnerability"},{"id":"b","label":"A hardware vulnerability"},{"id":"c","label":"A configuration vulnerability"},{"id":"d","label":"A human behaviour vulnerability"}],"prompt":"An unlocked server room cabinet left overnight is best classified as\u2026","questionId":"week2-session2-retrieval:s2-q6","sourceQuestionId":"s2-q6","sourceType":"single"},"id":"week2-session2-retrieval-q-6-s2-q6","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"single-choice","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"correctOptionId":"c","feedback":{"correct":"Misconfigured security settings \u2014 such as overly permissive firewall rules \u2014 are configuration vulnerabilities.","incorrect":"Misconfigured security settings \u2014 such as overly permissive firewall rules \u2014 are configuration vulnerabilities."},"formative":true,"options":[{"id":"a","label":"A software vulnerability"},{"id":"b","label":"A hardware vulnerability"},{"id":"c","label":"A configuration vulnerability"},{"id":"d","label":"A human behaviour vulnerability"}],"prompt":"A firewall rule that allows unnecessary inbound traffic is best classified as\u2026","questionId":"week2-session2-retrieval:s2-q7","sourceQuestionId":"s2-q7","sourceType":"single"},"id":"week2-session2-retrieval-q-7-s2-q7","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"single-choice","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"correctOptionId":"d","feedback":{"correct":"Untrained or careless behaviour is a human vulnerability that social engineers exploit.","incorrect":"Untrained or careless behaviour is a human vulnerability that social engineers exploit."},"formative":true,"options":[{"id":"a","label":"A software vulnerability"},{"id":"b","label":"A hardware vulnerability"},{"id":"c","label":"A configuration vulnerability"},{"id":"d","label":"A human behaviour vulnerability"}],"prompt":"Staff who trust phishing emails without checking the sender are an example of\u2026","questionId":"week2-session2-retrieval:s2-q8","sourceQuestionId":"s2-q8","sourceType":"single"},"id":"week2-session2-retrieval-q-8-s2-q8","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"single-choice","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"correctOptionId":"b","feedback":{"correct":"The social engineer is the threat. Failing to verify the caller is the human vulnerability.","incorrect":"The social engineer is the threat. Failing to verify the caller is the human vulnerability."},"formative":true,"options":[{"id":"a","label":"Reception staff who do not verify unexpected support calls"},{"id":"b","label":"The social engineer pretending to be IT support"},{"id":"c","label":"The remote-access system itself"},{"id":"d","label":"The incident report form"}],"prompt":"In this scenario, what is the threat?","questionId":"week2-session2-retrieval:s2-q9","scenario":"At Northbank, a caller pretends to be from IT support and asks reception for a remote-access code.","sourceQuestionId":"s2-q9","sourceType":"single"},"id":"week2-session2-retrieval-q-9-s2-q9","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"single-choice","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"correctOptionId":"b","feedback":{"correct":"Unpatched software is the vulnerability. Malware or an attacker targeting the flaw would be the threat.","incorrect":"Unpatched software is the vulnerability. Malware or an attacker targeting the flaw would be the threat."},"formative":true,"options":[{"id":"a","label":"Malware designed to exploit the known flaw"},{"id":"b","label":"The missing software patch leaving a known weakness"},{"id":"c","label":"Patient records stored on the server"},{"id":"d","label":"The cyber security incident response team"}],"prompt":"In this scenario, what is the vulnerability?","questionId":"week2-session2-retrieval:s2-q10","scenario":"At Northbank, appointment software has not been updated despite a vendor security patch being available for three months.","sourceQuestionId":"s2-q10","sourceType":"single"},"id":"week2-session2-retrieval-q-10-s2-q10","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"single-choice","version":"0.1.0"}],"id":"week2-session2-retrieval","metadata":{"activityType":"Retrieval quiz","href":null,"runtimeGlobal":"Week2Session2Retrieval","status":"available","summary":"Session 2 Retrieval Quiz","title":"Session 2 Retrieval Quiz"},"relationships":{"assets":[],"assignment":"formative-practice","learningOutcomes":["LO1"],"questions":[]},"schema":"lp.content.activity","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","version":"1.0.0"},{"blocks":[{"content":{"level":2,"text":"Northbank Vulnerability Analysis"},"id":"week2-northbank-vulnerability-analysis-title","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"heading","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"format":"application/json","text":"```json\n{\n  \"categories\": [\n    \"Software\",\n    \"Hardware\",\n    \"Configuration\",\n    \"Human behaviour\"\n  ],\n  \"ciaOptions\": [\n    \"Confidentiality\",\n    \"Integrity\",\n    \"Availability\"\n  ],\n  \"feedbackChain\": \"Threat \u2192 exploits vulnerability \u2192 causes incident \u2192 produces impact on CIA aims.\",\n  \"scenarios\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"nba-1\",\n      \"title\": \"Unpatched patient portal\",\n      \"text\": \"Northbank's patient appointment portal runs software that has not been updated for six months. A vendor patch fixing a serious flaw was released but never installed.\",\n      \"answers\": {\n        \"vulnerability\": [\n          \"unpatched software\",\n          \"missing patch\",\n          \"out-of-date software\",\n          \"outdated software\",\n          \"not updated\",\n          \"unpatched portal\"\n        ],\n        \"category\": \"Software\",\n        \"threat\": [\n          \"malware\",\n          \"ransomware\",\n          \"attacker\",\n          \"cyber criminal\",\n          \"hacker\",\n          \"exploit\"\n        ],\n        \"likelyIncident\": [\n          \"unauthorised access\",\n          \"data breach\",\n          \"malware infection\",\n          \"system compromise\",\n          \"ransomware\",\n          \"encryption\"\n        ],\n        \"ciaAims\": [\n          \"Confidentiality\",\n          \"Availability\"\n        ],\n        \"justification\": \"Unpatched software is a software vulnerability. Malware or an attacker can exploit the known flaw, leading to compromise of patient data (confidentiality) or disrupted access (availability).\"\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"nba-2\",\n      \"title\": \"Unlocked server room\",\n      \"text\": \"A cleaner props open the server room door overnight so they can move equipment. No one notices until the morning.\",\n      \"answers\": {\n        \"vulnerability\": [\n          \"unlocked door\",\n          \"door propped open\",\n          \"physical access\",\n          \"unsecured server room\",\n          \"open server room\"\n        ],\n        \"category\": \"Hardware\",\n        \"threat\": [\n          \"malicious insider\",\n          \"insider\",\n          \"intruder\",\n          \"thief\",\n          \"unauthorised person\",\n          \"attacker\"\n        ],\n        \"likelyIncident\": [\n          \"unauthorised access\",\n          \"theft\",\n          \"tampering\",\n          \"hardware theft\",\n          \"data theft\",\n          \"physical access\"\n        ],\n        \"ciaAims\": [\n          \"Confidentiality\",\n          \"Integrity\"\n        ],\n        \"justification\": \"Physical access to hardware without protection is a hardware vulnerability. An insider or intruder could access or tamper with equipment, affecting confidentiality and integrity of stored data.\"\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"nba-3\",\n      \"title\": \"Overly permissive firewall\",\n      \"text\": \"Northbank's firewall allows remote desktop (RDP) connections from any IP address on the internet. IT staff set this up for home working but never restricted it.\",\n      \"answers\": {\n        \"vulnerability\": [\n          \"firewall rule\",\n          \"misconfigured firewall\",\n          \"open rdp\",\n          \"permissive rule\",\n          \"misconfiguration\",\n          \"unnecessary inbound\"\n        ],\n        \"category\": \"Configuration\",\n        \"threat\": [\n          \"brute force\",\n          \"attacker\",\n          \"cyber criminal\",\n          \"hacker\",\n          \"automated attack\",\n          \"credential stuffing\"\n        ],\n        \"likelyIncident\": [\n          \"unauthorised login\",\n          \"unauthorised access\",\n          \"account compromise\",\n          \"remote access\",\n          \"system compromise\"\n        ],\n        \"ciaAims\": [\n          \"Confidentiality\"\n        ],\n        \"justification\": \"Allowing unnecessary inbound RDP is a configuration vulnerability. Attackers can attempt brute-force logins, gaining unauthorised access and threatening confidentiality of patient records.\"\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"nba-4\",\n      \"title\": \"Phishing email at reception\",\n      \"text\": \"Reception staff receive an email claiming to be from payroll, asking them to click a link and confirm login details. Several staff members do so without checking the sender.\",\n      \"answers\": {\n        \"vulnerability\": [\n          \"trust phishing\",\n          \"click link\",\n          \"no verification\",\n          \"human error\",\n          \"trust email\",\n          \"staff trust\",\n          \"phishing susceptibility\"\n        ],\n        \"category\": \"Human behaviour\",\n        \"threat\": [\n          \"phisher\",\n          \"phishing\",\n          \"social engineer\",\n          \"scammer\",\n          \"attacker\",\n          \"fake email\"\n        ],\n        \"likelyIncident\": [\n          \"credential theft\",\n          \"stolen credentials\",\n          \"account compromise\",\n          \"unauthorised access\",\n          \"login stolen\"\n        ],\n        \"ciaAims\": [\n          \"Confidentiality\"\n        ],\n        \"justification\": \"Trusting a fake email without verification is a human behaviour vulnerability. The phisher exploits this to steal credentials, leading to unauthorised access and loss of confidentiality.\"\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"nba-5\",\n      \"title\": \"Shared admin password\",\n      \"text\": \"The reception PC uses a single shared administrator password that every shift worker knows. It has not been changed in over a year.\",\n      \"answers\": {\n        \"vulnerability\": [\n          \"shared password\",\n          \"weak password\",\n          \"shared admin\",\n          \"known password\",\n          \"password not changed\"\n        ],\n        \"category\": \"Human behaviour\",\n        \"threat\": [\n          \"malicious insider\",\n          \"insider\",\n          \"former employee\",\n          \"attacker\",\n          \"unauthorised user\"\n        ],\n        \"likelyIncident\": [\n          \"unauthorised changes\",\n          \"unauthorised access\",\n          \"data alteration\",\n          \"account misuse\",\n          \"integrity breach\"\n        ],\n        \"ciaAims\": [\n          \"Integrity\",\n          \"Confidentiality\"\n        ],\n        \"justification\": \"A shared, unchanged admin password is a human/process vulnerability. Anyone with the password \u2014 including a malicious insider \u2014 could alter records (integrity) or access sensitive data (confidentiality).\"\n      }\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```"},"id":"week2-northbank-vulnerability-analysis-source-remainder","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"markdown","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"formative":true,"prompt":"Complete this activity on the learner hub page, then write a short note to confirm you have finished.","questionId":"week2-northbank-vulnerability-analysis:learner-note","sourceQuestionId":"learner-note"},"id":"week2-northbank-vulnerability-analysis-learner-note","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"reflection","version":"0.1.0"}],"id":"week2-northbank-vulnerability-analysis","metadata":{"activityType":"Scenario analysis","href":null,"runtimeGlobal":"Week2NorthbankAnalysis","status":"available","summary":"Northbank Vulnerability Analysis","title":"Northbank Vulnerability Analysis"},"relationships":{"assets":[],"assignment":"formative-practice","learningOutcomes":["LO1"],"questions":[]},"schema":"lp.content.activity","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","version":"1.0.0"},{"blocks":[{"content":{"level":2,"text":"Six-Mark Response Guide"},"id":"week2-six-mark-response-guide-title","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"heading","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"correctOptionId":"b","feedback":{"correct":"Start with a direct point \u2014 name the threat, vulnerability, relationship or incident outcome.","incorrect":"Start with a direct point \u2014 name the threat, vulnerability, relationship or incident outcome."},"formative":true,"options":[{"id":"a","label":"Describe Northbank's location and size"},{"id":"b","label":"State a clear cyber security point that answers the command word"},{"id":"c","label":"List every type of malware"},{"id":"d","label":"Copy the question wording without adding detail"}],"prompt":"In a six-mark explain response, what should the Point (P) do first?","questionId":"week2-six-mark-response-guide:pec-q1","sourceQuestionId":"pec-q1","sourceType":"single"},"id":"week2-six-mark-response-guide-q-1-pec-q1","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"single-choice","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"correctOptionId":"b","feedback":{"correct":"Explanation develops the point \u2014 define, describe the mechanism or show cause and effect.","incorrect":"Explanation develops the point \u2014 define, describe the mechanism or show cause and effect."},"formative":true,"options":[{"id":"a","label":"A bullet list of unrelated acronyms"},{"id":"b","label":"How or why the point is true \u2014 e.g. threat exploits vulnerability"},{"id":"c","label":"Your personal opinion about the NHS"},{"id":"d","label":"A request for the examiner to mark leniently"}],"prompt":"What belongs in the Explanation (E) part of PEC?","questionId":"week2-six-mark-response-guide:pec-q2","sourceQuestionId":"pec-q2","sourceType":"single"},"id":"week2-six-mark-response-guide-q-2-pec-q2","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"single-choice","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"correctOptionId":"b","feedback":{"correct":"OCR expects application \u2014 link your point to Northbank staff, systems or data to show understanding in context.","incorrect":"OCR expects application \u2014 link your point to Northbank staff, systems or data to show understanding in context."},"formative":true,"options":[{"id":"a","label":"It replaces the need to define threats and vulnerabilities"},{"id":"b","label":"It shows you can apply general cyber security knowledge to the organisation in the question"},{"id":"c","label":"It is only needed for two-mark questions"},{"id":"d","label":"It means you can ignore the command word"}],"prompt":"Why is a contextual link essential for full marks at Northbank?","questionId":"week2-six-mark-response-guide:pec-q3","sourceQuestionId":"pec-q3","sourceType":"single"},"id":"week2-six-mark-response-guide-q-3-pec-q3","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"single-choice","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"format":"application/json","text":"```json\n{\n  \"structure\": {\n    \"title\": \"Point \u2013 Explanation \u2013 Contextual link (PEC)\",\n    \"points\": [\n      {\n        \"letter\": \"P\",\n        \"name\": \"Point\",\n        \"description\": \"State a clear cyber security point that directly answers the command word \u2014 name the threat, vulnerability or relationship.\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"letter\": \"E\",\n        \"name\": \"Explanation\",\n        \"description\": \"Explain how or why \u2014 describe the mechanism (threat exploits vulnerability) or define the term accurately.\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"letter\": \"C\",\n        \"name\": \"Contextual link\",\n        \"description\": \"Apply your point to Northbank Community Health Partnership \u2014 use a realistic example from the scenario or organisation.\"\n      }\n    ]\n  },\n  \"examQuestion\": {\n    \"commandWord\": \"Explain\",\n    \"marks\": 6,\n    \"text\": \"Explain how a phishing attack could lead to a cyber security incident at Northbank Community Health Partnership. In your answer, refer to threats, vulnerabilities and the impact on confidentiality. [6 marks]\"\n  },\n  \"weakResponse\": \"Phishing is bad and staff should not click links. Northbank uses computers so they could get hacked.\",\n  \"improvedResponse\": \"A phishing email is a threat because a social engineer attempts to deceive staff. At Northbank, a human vulnerability exists when reception staff trust a fake payroll email without verifying the sender. The phisher exploits this weakness to steal login credentials, causing unauthorised access to internal systems. This affects confidentiality because patient or staff data could be viewed by someone who is not authorised.\",\n  \"modelAnswer\": [\n    {\n      \"part\": \"Point 1\",\n      \"text\": \"Phishing is a threat \u2014 a social engineer sends a deceptive email attempting to obtain credentials.\",\n      \"annotation\": \"P \u2014 names the threat clearly\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"part\": \"Explanation 1\",\n      \"text\": \"The threat exploits a human behaviour vulnerability when staff trust the message and click a link without checking the sender.\",\n      \"annotation\": \"E \u2014 explains threat exploits vulnerability\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"part\": \"Contextual link 1\",\n      \"text\": \"At Northbank, reception staff who confirm login details via a fake payroll email give an attacker access to internal systems.\",\n      \"annotation\": \"C \u2014 applied to Northbank\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"part\": \"Point 2\",\n      \"text\": \"The likely incident is credential theft leading to unauthorised access.\",\n      \"annotation\": \"P \u2014 names the incident outcome\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"part\": \"Explanation 2\",\n      \"text\": \"Unauthorised access means someone without permission can view or obtain sensitive records.\",\n      \"annotation\": \"E \u2014 explains confidentiality impact\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"part\": \"Contextual link 2\",\n      \"text\": \"This affects confidentiality at Northbank because patient appointment or contact details could be exposed.\",\n      \"annotation\": \"C \u2014 Northbank-specific CIA impact\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"sentenceStarters\": [\n    \"A [threat type] is a threat because\u2026\",\n    \"The vulnerability at Northbank is\u2026 because\u2026\",\n    \"The threat exploits this vulnerability by\u2026\",\n    \"This could lead to [incident] which affects [CIA aim] because\u2026\",\n    \"At Northbank, this matters because\u2026\"\n  ]\n}\n```"},"id":"week2-six-mark-response-guide-source-remainder","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"markdown","version":"0.1.0"}],"id":"week2-six-mark-response-guide","metadata":{"activityType":"Exam skills","href":null,"runtimeGlobal":"Week2SixMarkGuide","status":"available","summary":"Six-Mark Response Guide","title":"Six-Mark Response Guide"},"relationships":{"assets":[],"assignment":"formative-practice","learningOutcomes":["LO1"],"questions":[]},"schema":"lp.content.activity","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","version":"1.0.0"},{"blocks":[{"content":{"level":2,"text":"OCR-Style Question Practice"},"id":"week2-ocr-question-practice-title","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"heading","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"commandWord":"Define","correctOptionId":"b","feedback":{"correct":"","incorrect":""},"formative":true,"marks":2,"options":[{"id":"a","label":"A weakness that could be exploited by an attacker"},{"id":"b","label":"A person, group or event that could harm systems, networks or data"},{"id":"c","label":"The outcome when an attack succeeds"},{"id":"d","label":"Software that removes viruses automatically"}],"prompt":"Define the term threat in cyber security.","questionId":"week2-ocr-question-practice:ocr-q1","sourceQuestionId":"ocr-q1","sourceType":"mcq"},"id":"week2-ocr-question-practice-q-1-ocr-q1","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"single-choice","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"commandWord":"Define","correctOptionId":"b","feedback":{"correct":"","incorrect":""},"formative":true,"marks":2,"options":[{"id":"a","label":"A control that blocks malicious traffic"},{"id":"b","label":"A weakness in technology, configuration or behaviour that a threat could exploit"},{"id":"c","label":"An encrypted backup stored off site"},{"id":"d","label":"A person who investigates incidents"}],"prompt":"Define the term vulnerability in cyber security.","questionId":"week2-ocr-question-practice:ocr-q2","sourceQuestionId":"ocr-q2","sourceType":"mcq"},"id":"week2-ocr-question-practice-q-2-ocr-q2","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"single-choice","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"commandWord":"State","correctOptionId":"a","feedback":{"correct":"","incorrect":""},"formative":true,"marks":2,"options":[{"id":"a","label":"Files become encrypted and users see a ransom demand"},{"id":"b","label":"The monitor brightness changes randomly"},{"id":"c","label":"Keyboard keys stick physically"},{"id":"d","label":"Paper documents fade in sunlight"}],"prompt":"Which pair best describes common symptoms of ransomware?","questionId":"week2-ocr-question-practice:ocr-q3","sourceQuestionId":"ocr-q3","sourceType":"mcq"},"id":"week2-ocr-question-practice-q-3-ocr-q3","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"single-choice","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"commandWord":"Identify","correctOptionId":"b","feedback":{"correct":"","incorrect":""},"formative":true,"marks":2,"options":[{"id":"a","label":"Staff who open attachments without checking"},{"id":"b","label":"The scammer sending malicious invoice emails"},{"id":"c","label":"The email server hardware"},{"id":"d","label":"The incident log template"}],"prompt":"Identify the threat in this scenario.","questionId":"week2-ocr-question-practice:ocr-q4","scenario":"At Northbank, a scammer sends fake invoice emails containing malicious attachments.","sourceQuestionId":"ocr-q4","sourceType":"mcq"},"id":"week2-ocr-question-practice-q-4-ocr-q4","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"single-choice","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"commandWord":"Identify","correctOptionId":"b","feedback":{"correct":"","incorrect":""},"formative":true,"marks":2,"options":[{"id":"a","label":"Malware designed to exploit outdated systems"},{"id":"b","label":"The unsupported operating system without security updates"},{"id":"c","label":"The reception desk furniture"},{"id":"d","label":"The organisation's logo on the website"}],"prompt":"Identify the vulnerability in this scenario.","questionId":"week2-ocr-question-practice:ocr-q5","scenario":"At Northbank, a reception PC still runs an operating system that no longer receives security updates.","sourceQuestionId":"ocr-q5","sourceType":"mcq"},"id":"week2-ocr-question-practice-q-5-ocr-q5","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"single-choice","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"commandWord":"Describe","correctOptionId":"b","feedback":{"correct":"","incorrect":""},"formative":true,"marks":2,"options":[{"id":"a","label":"Northbank has no human vulnerabilities because staff are trained once"},{"id":"b","label":"Unpatched software at Northbank is a vulnerability that malware could exploit, disrupting patient services"},{"id":"c","label":"Threats only exist outside the organisation so internal systems are safe"},{"id":"d","label":"Vulnerabilities and threats are the same at Northbank"}],"prompt":"Which statement best applies threat and vulnerability knowledge to Northbank?","questionId":"week2-ocr-question-practice:ocr-q6","sourceQuestionId":"ocr-q6","sourceType":"mcq"},"id":"week2-ocr-question-practice-q-6-ocr-q6","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"single-choice","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"commandWord":"State","correctOptionId":"c","feedback":{"correct":"","incorrect":""},"formative":true,"marks":2,"options":[{"id":"a","label":"Confidentiality only"},{"id":"b","label":"Integrity only"},{"id":"c","label":"Availability"},{"id":"d","label":"None of the CIA aims"}],"prompt":"Which CIA aim is mainly affected?","questionId":"week2-ocr-question-practice:ocr-q7","scenario":"After ransomware encrypts Northbank appointment records, clinicians cannot access schedules for a full day.","sourceQuestionId":"ocr-q7","sourceType":"mcq"},"id":"week2-ocr-question-practice-q-7-ocr-q7","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"single-choice","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"commandWord":"Explain","correctOptionId":"","feedback":{"correct":"","incorrect":""},"formative":true,"marks":6,"options":[],"prompt":"Explain how a phishing attack could lead to a cyber security incident at Northbank Community Health Partnership. In your answer, refer to threats, vulnerabilities and the impact on confidentiality. [6 marks]","questionId":"week2-ocr-question-practice:ocr-q8","sourceQuestionId":"ocr-q8","sourceType":"extended"},"id":"week2-ocr-question-practice-q-8-ocr-q8","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"single-choice","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"format":"application/json","text":"```json\n{\n  \"suggestedMinutes\": 35,\n  \"extendedMinChars\": 80,\n  \"extendedDraftKey\": \"ocrExtendedResponse\"\n}\n```"},"id":"week2-ocr-question-practice-source-remainder","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"markdown","version":"0.1.0"}],"id":"week2-ocr-question-practice","metadata":{"activityType":"Exam skills","href":null,"runtimeGlobal":"Week2OcrPractice","status":"available","summary":"OCR-Style Question Practice","title":"OCR-Style Question Practice"},"relationships":{"assets":[],"assignment":"formative-practice","learningOutcomes":["LO1"],"questions":[]},"schema":"lp.content.activity","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","version":"1.0.0"},{"blocks":[{"content":{"level":2,"text":"Peer Marking and Answer Improvement"},"id":"week2-peer-marking-answer-improvement-title","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"heading","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"format":"application/json","text":"```json\n{\n  \"ocrPracticePath\": \"../ocr-practice/\",\n  \"extendedDraftKey\": \"ocrExtendedResponse\",\n  \"peerDraftKey\": \"peerMarking\",\n  \"question\": {\n    \"commandWord\": \"Explain\",\n    \"marks\": 6,\n    \"text\": \"Explain how a phishing attack could lead to a cyber security incident at Northbank Community Health Partnership. In your answer, refer to threats, vulnerabilities and the impact on confidentiality. [6 marks]\"\n  },\n  \"markScheme\": [\n    \"Threat named clearly (e.g. phishing / social engineer sending deceptive email).\",\n    \"Vulnerability named (e.g. staff trust email without verifying sender).\",\n    \"Relationship explained \u2014 threat exploits vulnerability.\",\n    \"Applied to Northbank (reception, staff, systems or patient data).\",\n    \"Consequence / incident described (e.g. credential theft, unauthorised access).\",\n    \"Confidentiality impact explained with reason.\"\n  ],\n  \"checklist\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"chk-threat\",\n      \"label\": \"Threat named?\",\n      \"description\": \"The response identifies phishing or a social engineer as the threat.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"chk-vulnerability\",\n      \"label\": \"Vulnerability named?\",\n      \"description\": \"The response identifies a human or technical weakness (e.g. trusting emails).\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"chk-relationship\",\n      \"label\": \"Relationship explained?\",\n      \"description\": \"The response explains that the threat exploits the vulnerability.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"chk-northbank\",\n      \"label\": \"Applied to Northbank?\",\n      \"description\": \"The response mentions Northbank staff, systems or data specifically.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"chk-consequence\",\n      \"label\": \"Consequence described?\",\n      \"description\": \"The response describes a likely incident outcome (e.g. stolen credentials).\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"chk-command\",\n      \"label\": \"Answered the command word?\",\n      \"description\": \"The response explains how and why, not just lists terms.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"maxAwardedMarks\": 6\n}\n```"},"id":"week2-peer-marking-answer-improvement-source-remainder","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"markdown","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"formative":true,"prompt":"Complete this activity on the learner hub page, then write a short note to confirm you have finished.","questionId":"week2-peer-marking-answer-improvement:learner-note","sourceQuestionId":"learner-note"},"id":"week2-peer-marking-answer-improvement-learner-note","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"reflection","version":"0.1.0"}],"id":"week2-peer-marking-answer-improvement","metadata":{"activityType":"Reflection","href":null,"runtimeGlobal":"Week2PeerMarking","status":"available","summary":"Peer Marking and Answer Improvement","title":"Peer Marking and Answer Improvement"},"relationships":{"assets":[],"assignment":"formative-practice","learningOutcomes":["LO1"],"questions":[]},"schema":"lp.content.activity","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","version":"1.0.0"},{"blocks":[{"content":{"level":2,"text":"Northbank Vulnerability Register"},"id":"week2-northbank-vulnerability-register-title","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"heading","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"format":"application/json","text":"```json\n{\n  \"entryCount\": 5,\n  \"registerStorageKey\": \"unit3-week2-northbank-vulnerability-register\",\n  \"categories\": [\n    \"Software\",\n    \"Hardware\",\n    \"Configuration\",\n    \"Human behaviour\"\n  ],\n  \"ciaOptions\": [\n    \"Confidentiality\",\n    \"Integrity\",\n    \"Availability\"\n  ],\n  \"week7ReservedFields\": [\n    \"likelihood\",\n    \"impact\",\n    \"riskScore\",\n    \"mitigation\",\n    \"priority\"\n  ],\n  \"requiredFields\": [\n    \"asset\",\n    \"vulnerability\",\n    \"category\",\n    \"threat\",\n    \"likelyIncident\",\n    \"ciaAim\",\n    \"justification\"\n  ]\n}\n```"},"id":"week2-northbank-vulnerability-register-source-remainder","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"markdown","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"formative":true,"prompt":"Complete this activity on the learner hub page, then write a short note to confirm you have finished.","questionId":"week2-northbank-vulnerability-register:learner-note","sourceQuestionId":"learner-note"},"id":"week2-northbank-vulnerability-register-learner-note","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"reflection","version":"0.1.0"}],"id":"week2-northbank-vulnerability-register","metadata":{"activityType":"Practical register","href":null,"runtimeGlobal":"Week2VulnerabilityRegister","status":"available","summary":"Northbank Vulnerability Register","title":"Northbank Vulnerability Register"},"relationships":{"assets":[],"assignment":"formative-practice","learningOutcomes":["LO1"],"questions":[]},"schema":"lp.content.activity","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","version":"1.0.0"},{"blocks":[{"content":{"level":2,"text":"Session 1 Retrieval Quiz"},"id":"week3-session1-retrieval-title","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"heading","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"correctOptionId":"B","feedback":{"correct":"A threat exploits a vulnerability to cause an incident.","incorrect":"Keep threat (source of harm) separate from vulnerability (weakness)."},"formative":true,"options":[{"id":"A","label":"A threat is a weakness; a vulnerability exploits it"},{"id":"B","label":"A threat exploits a vulnerability to cause a cyber security incident"},{"id":"C","label":"A vulnerability is always a person; a threat is always malware"},{"id":"D","label":"Threats and vulnerabilities are the same thing"}],"prompt":"Which statement best describes the relationship between a threat and a vulnerability?","questionId":"week3-session1-retrieval:S1Q1","sourceQuestionId":"S1Q1","sourceType":"single"},"id":"week3-session1-retrieval-q-1-S1Q1","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"single-choice","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"correctOptionId":"C","feedback":{"correct":"Missing patches are a software vulnerability.","incorrect":"The weakness is in the software state, not the attacker."},"formative":true,"options":[{"id":"A","label":"A threat actor"},{"id":"B","label":"A hardware vulnerability"},{"id":"C","label":"A software vulnerability"},{"id":"D","label":"A cyber-terrorist"}],"prompt":"An unpatched remote-access service on a Northbank clinic PC is best described as:","questionId":"week3-session1-retrieval:S1Q2","sourceQuestionId":"S1Q2","sourceType":"single"},"id":"week3-session1-retrieval-q-2-S1Q2","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"single-choice","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"correctOptionId":"A","feedback":{"correct":"Lack of encryption on a device is commonly treated as a hardware/device protection weakness in OCR-style classification when the physical device can expose data.","incorrect":"Focus on the weakness of the device protection, not who might use it."},"formative":true,"options":[{"id":"A","label":"A hardware vulnerability"},{"id":"B","label":"A phishing campaign"},{"id":"C","label":"An insider threat by definition"},{"id":"D","label":"A vulnerability broker"}],"prompt":"A clinic laptop with no disk encryption is primarily an example of:","questionId":"week3-session1-retrieval:S1Q3","sourceQuestionId":"S1Q3","sourceType":"single"},"id":"week3-session1-retrieval-q-3-S1Q3","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"single-choice","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"correctOptionId":"B","feedback":{"correct":"Weak or default settings are configuration vulnerabilities.","incorrect":"Configuration weaknesses are about how a system is set up."},"formative":true,"options":[{"id":"A","label":"A human vulnerability only"},{"id":"B","label":"A configuration vulnerability"},{"id":"C","label":"A cyber-criminal"},{"id":"D","label":"A malware category"}],"prompt":"Leaving a default administrator password unchanged is best classified as:","questionId":"week3-session1-retrieval:S1Q4","sourceQuestionId":"S1Q4","sourceType":"single"},"id":"week3-session1-retrieval-q-4-S1Q4","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"single-choice","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"correctOptionId":"B","feedback":{"correct":"Unsafe user behaviour is a human vulnerability.","incorrect":"Human vulnerabilities concern people and practice."},"formative":true,"options":[{"id":"A","label":"A hardware vulnerability"},{"id":"B","label":"A human vulnerability"},{"id":"C","label":"A vulnerability broker"},{"id":"D","label":"A denial-of-service attack"}],"prompt":"A staff member who reuses a simple password for clinical systems demonstrates:","questionId":"week3-session1-retrieval:S1Q5","sourceQuestionId":"S1Q5","sourceType":"single"},"id":"week3-session1-retrieval-q-5-S1Q5","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"single-choice","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"correctOptionId":"B","feedback":{"correct":"Ransomware is malware and can be the threat that exploits weaknesses.","incorrect":"Malware is malicious software; the vulnerability is what allows it in or to spread."},"formative":true,"options":[{"id":"A","label":"A social engineering method only"},{"id":"B","label":"A malware category used as a threat"},{"id":"C","label":"A configuration vulnerability"},{"id":"D","label":"Authorised penetration testing"}],"prompt":"Ransomware that encrypts files and demands payment is best described as:","questionId":"week3-session1-retrieval:S1Q6","sourceQuestionId":"S1Q6","sourceType":"single"},"id":"week3-session1-retrieval-q-6-S1Q6","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"single-choice","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"correctOptionId":"A","feedback":{"correct":"The phishing/exploit path is the threat action against a weakness (unpatched VPN).","incorrect":"Name the weakness and what could exploit it."},"formative":true,"options":[{"id":"A","label":"Phishing email exploiting unpatched VPN software to steal credentials"},{"id":"B","label":"Firewall rule exploiting a receptionist"},{"id":"C","label":"Encryption exploiting a ransom note"},{"id":"D","label":"A patch exploiting malware"}],"prompt":"Which pairing correctly matches a threat to a vulnerability?","questionId":"week3-session1-retrieval:S1Q7","sourceQuestionId":"S1Q7","sourceType":"single"},"id":"week3-session1-retrieval-q-7-S1Q7","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"single-choice","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"correctOptionId":"C","feedback":{"correct":"Attackers can be external or insiders; evidence decides.","incorrect":"Do not assume every attacker is external."},"formative":true,"options":[{"id":"A","label":"Only teenagers"},{"id":"B","label":"Only people outside the organisation"},{"id":"C","label":"External attackers or people with legitimate access, depending on the scenario"},{"id":"D","label":"Only vulnerability brokers"}],"prompt":"Who may choose to exploit a vulnerability at Northbank?","questionId":"week3-session1-retrieval:S1Q8","sourceQuestionId":"S1Q8","sourceType":"single"},"id":"week3-session1-retrieval-q-8-S1Q8","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"single-choice","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"correctOptionId":"B","feedback":{"correct":"Hacktivism and cyber-terrorism differ; use evidence about fear, coercion and essential services.","incorrect":"Protest publicity alone is not enough for cyber-terrorist."},"formative":true,"options":[{"id":"A","label":"True"},{"id":"B","label":"False"}],"prompt":"True or false: Every politically motivated cyber attack must be labelled cyber-terrorism in OCR answers.","questionId":"week3-session1-retrieval:S1Q9","sourceQuestionId":"S1Q9","sourceType":"single"},"id":"week3-session1-retrieval-q-9-S1Q9","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"single-choice","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"correctOptionId":"B","feedback":{"correct":"Credential harvesting via deceptive login pages indicates a phisher.","incorrect":"If the lure collects credentials, phisher is usually stronger than scammer."},"formative":true,"options":[{"id":"A","label":"Scammer"},{"id":"B","label":"Phisher"},{"id":"C","label":"Script kiddie"},{"id":"D","label":"Vulnerability broker"}],"prompt":"Which OCR attacker type best fits someone who uses a cloned Microsoft 365 page to steal staff passwords?","questionId":"week3-session1-retrieval:S1Q10","sourceQuestionId":"S1Q10","sourceType":"single"},"id":"week3-session1-retrieval-q-10-S1Q10","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"single-choice","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"format":"application/json","text":"```json\n{\n  \"weekNumber\": 3,\n  \"sessionNumber\": 1,\n  \"estimatedMinutes\": 15\n}\n```"},"id":"week3-session1-retrieval-source-remainder","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"markdown","version":"0.1.0"}],"id":"week3-session1-retrieval","metadata":{"activityType":"Retrieval quiz","href":null,"runtimeGlobal":"Week3Session1Retrieval","status":"available","summary":"Session 1 Retrieval Quiz","title":"Session 1 Retrieval Quiz"},"relationships":{"assets":[],"assignment":"formative-practice","learningOutcomes":["LO1"],"questions":[]},"schema":"lp.content.activity","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","version":"1.0.0"},{"blocks":[{"content":{"level":2,"text":"Attacker Types Learning"},"id":"week3-attacker-types-learning-title","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"heading","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"correctOptionId":"A","feedback":{"correct":"The evidence best matches a hacktivist.","incorrect":"Re-read motivation and method evidence; avoid stereotypes."},"formative":true,"options":[{"id":"A","label":"Hacktivist"},{"id":"B","label":"Cyber-criminal"},{"id":"C","label":"Insider"},{"id":"D","label":"Script kiddie"}],"prompt":"Which OCR attacker type is most likely?","questionId":"week3-attacker-types-learning:KC1","scenario":"A group defaces a public site and leaves a protest message about funding, without threatening emergency services.","sourceQuestionId":"KC1","sourceType":"single"},"id":"week3-attacker-types-learning-q-1-KC1","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"single-choice","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"correctOptionId":"A","feedback":{"correct":"The evidence best matches a cyber-criminal.","incorrect":"Re-read motivation and method evidence; avoid stereotypes."},"formative":true,"options":[{"id":"A","label":"Cyber-criminal"},{"id":"B","label":"Insider"},{"id":"C","label":"Script kiddie"},{"id":"D","label":"Vulnerability broker"}],"prompt":"Which OCR attacker type is most likely?","questionId":"week3-attacker-types-learning:KC2","scenario":"Clinic systems are encrypted and a cryptocurrency ransom is demanded.","sourceQuestionId":"KC2","sourceType":"single"},"id":"week3-attacker-types-learning-q-2-KC2","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"single-choice","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"correctOptionId":"A","feedback":{"correct":"The evidence best matches a insider.","incorrect":"Re-read motivation and method evidence; avoid stereotypes."},"formative":true,"options":[{"id":"A","label":"Insider"},{"id":"B","label":"Script kiddie"},{"id":"C","label":"Vulnerability broker"},{"id":"D","label":"Scammer"}],"prompt":"Which OCR attacker type is most likely?","questionId":"week3-attacker-types-learning:KC3","scenario":"A records officer uses their authorised account to export patient demographics without approval.","sourceQuestionId":"KC3","sourceType":"single"},"id":"week3-attacker-types-learning-q-3-KC3","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"single-choice","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"correctOptionId":"A","feedback":{"correct":"The evidence best matches a script kiddie.","incorrect":"Re-read motivation and method evidence; avoid stereotypes."},"formative":true,"options":[{"id":"A","label":"Script kiddie"},{"id":"B","label":"Vulnerability broker"},{"id":"C","label":"Scammer"},{"id":"D","label":"Phisher"}],"prompt":"Which OCR attacker type is most likely?","questionId":"week3-attacker-types-learning:KC4","scenario":"Someone downloads a public defacement tool and alters a leaflet page to impress friends.","sourceQuestionId":"KC4","sourceType":"single"},"id":"week3-attacker-types-learning-q-4-KC4","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"single-choice","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"correctOptionId":"A","feedback":{"correct":"The evidence best matches a vulnerability broker.","incorrect":"Re-read motivation and method evidence; avoid stereotypes."},"formative":true,"options":[{"id":"A","label":"Vulnerability broker"},{"id":"B","label":"Scammer"},{"id":"C","label":"Phisher"},{"id":"D","label":"Cyber-terrorist"}],"prompt":"Which OCR attacker type is most likely?","questionId":"week3-attacker-types-learning:KC5","scenario":"A researcher offers details of a booking flaw via a disclosure programme for a bounty.","sourceQuestionId":"KC5","sourceType":"single"},"id":"week3-attacker-types-learning-q-5-KC5","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"single-choice","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"correctOptionId":"A","feedback":{"correct":"The evidence best matches a scammer.","incorrect":"Re-read motivation and method evidence; avoid stereotypes."},"formative":true,"options":[{"id":"A","label":"Scammer"},{"id":"B","label":"Phisher"},{"id":"C","label":"Cyber-terrorist"},{"id":"D","label":"Hacktivist"}],"prompt":"Which OCR attacker type is most likely?","questionId":"week3-attacker-types-learning:KC6","scenario":"Finance is sent a false supplier invoice designed to trigger payment.","sourceQuestionId":"KC6","sourceType":"single"},"id":"week3-attacker-types-learning-q-6-KC6","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"single-choice","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"correctOptionId":"A","feedback":{"correct":"The evidence best matches a phisher.","incorrect":"Re-read motivation and method evidence; avoid stereotypes."},"formative":true,"options":[{"id":"A","label":"Phisher"},{"id":"B","label":"Cyber-terrorist"},{"id":"C","label":"Hacktivist"},{"id":"D","label":"Cyber-criminal"}],"prompt":"Which OCR attacker type is most likely?","questionId":"week3-attacker-types-learning:KC7","scenario":"Staff are emailed a link to a fake Microsoft 365 sign-in page collecting passwords.","sourceQuestionId":"KC7","sourceType":"single"},"id":"week3-attacker-types-learning-q-7-KC7","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"single-choice","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"correctOptionId":"A","feedback":{"correct":"The evidence best matches a cyber-terrorist.","incorrect":"Re-read motivation and method evidence; avoid stereotypes."},"formative":true,"options":[{"id":"A","label":"Cyber-terrorist"},{"id":"B","label":"Hacktivist"},{"id":"C","label":"Cyber-criminal"},{"id":"D","label":"Insider"}],"prompt":"Which OCR attacker type is most likely?","questionId":"week3-attacker-types-learning:KC8","scenario":"A group threatens to disable emergency booking systems to frighten the public into political change.","sourceQuestionId":"KC8","sourceType":"single"},"id":"week3-attacker-types-learning-q-8-KC8","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"single-choice","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"format":"application/json","text":"```json\n{\n  \"weekNumber\": 3,\n  \"sessionNumber\": 1,\n  \"estimatedMinutes\": 30\n}\n```"},"id":"week3-attacker-types-learning-source-remainder","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"markdown","version":"0.1.0"}],"id":"week3-attacker-types-learning","metadata":{"activityType":"Guided learning","href":null,"runtimeGlobal":"Week3AttackerTypesLearning","status":"available","summary":"Attacker Types Learning","title":"Attacker Types Learning"},"relationships":{"assets":[],"assignment":"formative-practice","learningOutcomes":["LO1"],"questions":[]},"schema":"lp.content.activity","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","version":"1.0.0"},{"blocks":[{"content":{"level":2,"text":"Attacker Case Study Matching"},"id":"week3-attacker-case-matching-title","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"heading","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"format":"application/json","text":"```json\n{\n  \"weekNumber\": 3,\n  \"sessionNumber\": 1,\n  \"estimatedMinutes\": 25,\n  \"attackerOptions\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"hacktivist\",\n      \"name\": \"Hacktivist\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"cyber-criminal\",\n      \"name\": \"Cyber-criminal\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"insider\",\n      \"name\": \"Insider\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"script-kiddie\",\n      \"name\": \"Script kiddie\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"vulnerability-broker\",\n      \"name\": \"Vulnerability broker\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"scammer\",\n      \"name\": \"Scammer\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"phisher\",\n      \"name\": \"Phisher\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"cyber-terrorist\",\n      \"name\": \"Cyber-terrorist\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"cases\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"C1\",\n      \"title\": \"Records export\",\n      \"scenario\": \"A disgruntled records employee exports confidential patient data using their authorised access after a dispute about rotas.\",\n      \"bestAnswer\": \"insider\",\n      \"plausibleAlternative\": \"cyber-criminal\",\n      \"evidencePoints\": [\n        \"Authorised staff account\",\n        \"Export of confidential patient data\",\n        \"Workplace grievance context\"\n      ],\n      \"whyBest\": \"Legitimate access used to take data strongly indicates an insider.\",\n      \"whyAlternativeWeaker\": \"A cyber-criminal label needs clearer external profit tradecraft; here the access path is internal and authorised.\",\n      \"stereotypeWarning\": \"Do not use personal characteristics; use access and behaviour evidence.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"C2\",\n      \"title\": \"Public tool defacement\",\n      \"scenario\": \"An inexperienced attacker downloads a public tool and defaces a clinic information page to impress friends, with no ransom demand.\",\n      \"bestAnswer\": \"script-kiddie\",\n      \"plausibleAlternative\": \"hacktivist\",\n      \"evidencePoints\": [\n        \"Ready-made public tool\",\n        \"Low sophistication defacement\",\n        \"Status-seeking among friends\"\n      ],\n      \"whyBest\": \"Reliance on a public tool for a prank/status defacement fits a script kiddie.\",\n      \"whyAlternativeWeaker\": \"Hacktivism needs clearer cause-driven protest messaging; impressing friends is not political activism.\",\n      \"stereotypeWarning\": \"Do not assume age; use tool and purpose evidence.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"C3\",\n      \"title\": \"Ransomware demand\",\n      \"scenario\": \"An organised group encrypts a health organisation\u2019s systems and demands cryptocurrency for restoration.\",\n      \"bestAnswer\": \"cyber-criminal\",\n      \"plausibleAlternative\": null,\n      \"evidencePoints\": [\n        \"Encryption of systems\",\n        \"Cryptocurrency ransom\",\n        \"Organised profit motive\"\n      ],\n      \"whyBest\": \"Ransom for money is core cyber-criminal evidence.\",\n      \"whyAlternativeWeaker\": \"\",\n      \"stereotypeWarning\": \"Organisation size alone is not proof; the ransom evidence is.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"C4\",\n      \"title\": \"Cause statement\",\n      \"scenario\": \"A politically motivated group disrupts an organisation\u2019s public website and publishes a statement supporting a social cause, without threatening emergency care.\",\n      \"bestAnswer\": \"hacktivist\",\n      \"plausibleAlternative\": \"cyber-terrorist\",\n      \"evidencePoints\": [\n        \"Political/social cause statement\",\n        \"Publicity-focused disruption\",\n        \"No threat to essential clinical services\"\n      ],\n      \"whyBest\": \"Cause-driven publicity/protest fits hacktivist.\",\n      \"whyAlternativeWeaker\": \"Cyber-terrorism needs fear/coercion against essential services or public safety; that evidence is missing.\",\n      \"stereotypeWarning\": \"Political language alone does not equal terrorism.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"C5\",\n      \"title\": \"Flaw offered\",\n      \"scenario\": \"A researcher discovers a software flaw in a supplier portal and offers the vulnerability through a disclosure programme / vulnerability market for payment.\",\n      \"bestAnswer\": \"vulnerability-broker\",\n      \"plausibleAlternative\": \"cyber-criminal\",\n      \"evidencePoints\": [\n        \"Discovery of a flaw\",\n        \"Offer via disclosure or vulnerability market\",\n        \"Focus on the vulnerability as the item of value\"\n      ],\n      \"whyBest\": \"Trading/disclosing the vulnerability itself indicates a vulnerability broker.\",\n      \"whyAlternativeWeaker\": \"Cyber-criminal usually implies direct exploitation for crime such as ransom; here the focus is the flaw transaction. Lawful bounty and unlawful markets both still map primarily to broker unless wider crime is shown.\",\n      \"stereotypeWarning\": \"Do not label every broker a criminal automatically.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"C6\",\n      \"title\": \"False invoice\",\n      \"scenario\": \"Someone sends a false invoice to an organisation\u2019s finance team to obtain a payment to attacker-controlled bank details.\",\n      \"bestAnswer\": \"scammer\",\n      \"plausibleAlternative\": \"phisher\",\n      \"evidencePoints\": [\n        \"False invoice\",\n        \"Payment fraud goal\",\n        \"Finance process targeted\"\n      ],\n      \"whyBest\": \"Direct payment deception is scammer evidence.\",\n      \"whyAlternativeWeaker\": \"No credential-harvesting page is described; the immediate goal is money via fraud.\",\n      \"stereotypeWarning\": \"Channel (email) alone does not decide phisher vs scammer.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"C7\",\n      \"title\": \"Cloned sign-in\",\n      \"scenario\": \"A cloned Microsoft 365 sign-in page is emailed to employees to collect their credentials.\",\n      \"bestAnswer\": \"phisher\",\n      \"plausibleAlternative\": \"scammer\",\n      \"evidencePoints\": [\n        \"Cloned login page\",\n        \"Credential collection\",\n        \"Employee-targeted lure\"\n      ],\n      \"whyBest\": \"Harvesting credentials via a fake login is phishing.\",\n      \"whyAlternativeWeaker\": \"A scammer may seek payment, but credential harvesting is the clearer goal here.\",\n      \"stereotypeWarning\": \"Brand logos in the lure are evidence of deception, not of the brand attacking you.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"C8\",\n      \"title\": \"Essential services threat\",\n      \"scenario\": \"A group threatens essential booking and emergency-related services to create fear and force political change.\",\n      \"bestAnswer\": \"cyber-terrorist\",\n      \"plausibleAlternative\": \"hacktivist\",\n      \"evidencePoints\": [\n        \"Threats to essential services\",\n        \"Intent to create fear\",\n        \"Political coercion\"\n      ],\n      \"whyBest\": \"Fear and coercion against essential services support cyber-terrorist.\",\n      \"whyAlternativeWeaker\": \"Hacktivism centres on protest/publicity; the coercion/fear aim is stronger here.\",\n      \"stereotypeWarning\": \"Do not decide from nationality stereotypes; use the threat evidence.\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```"},"id":"week3-attacker-case-matching-source-remainder","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"markdown","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"formative":true,"prompt":"Complete this activity on the learner hub page, then write a short note to confirm you have finished.","questionId":"week3-attacker-case-matching:learner-note","sourceQuestionId":"learner-note"},"id":"week3-attacker-case-matching-learner-note","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"reflection","version":"0.1.0"}],"id":"week3-attacker-case-matching","metadata":{"activityType":"Scenario matching","href":null,"runtimeGlobal":"Week3AttackerCaseMatching","status":"available","summary":"Attacker Case Study Matching","title":"Attacker Case Study Matching"},"relationships":{"assets":[],"assignment":"formative-practice","learningOutcomes":["LO1"],"questions":[]},"schema":"lp.content.activity","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","version":"1.0.0"},{"blocks":[{"content":{"level":2,"text":"Justified Identification Practice"},"id":"week3-justified-identification-title","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"heading","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"format":"application/json","text":"```json\n{\n  \"weekNumber\": 3,\n  \"sessionNumber\": 1,\n  \"marksPerScenario\": 3,\n  \"estimatedMinutes\": 30,\n  \"answerStructure\": \"The attacker is most likely a [type] because [specific scenario evidence]. Although the attacker could be a [alternative type], this is less likely because [reason].\",\n  \"scenarios\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"J1\",\n      \"marks\": 3,\n      \"scenario\": \"After being refused annual leave, a Northbank records officer uses their normal login to copy a large patient contact list to a personal USB stick.\",\n      \"bestAttacker\": \"insider\",\n      \"alternative\": \"cyber-criminal\",\n      \"evidenceHints\": [\n        \"authorised login\",\n        \"USB copy of patient contacts\",\n        \"workplace dispute\"\n      ],\n      \"sentenceStarters\": [\n        \"The attacker is most likely an insider because\",\n        \"Although the attacker could be a cyber-criminal,\"\n      ],\n      \"modelAnswer\": \"The attacker is most likely an insider because they used authorised records access to copy patient contacts after a workplace dispute. Although the attacker could be a cyber-criminal, this is less likely because the scenario emphasises misuse of legitimate access rather than an external intrusion for ransom or resale.\",\n      \"successCriteria\": [\n        \"Names insider\",\n        \"Uses scenario evidence\",\n        \"Rejects a plausible alternative with a reason\"\n      ],\n      \"keywordChecks\": {\n        \"attackerTerms\": [\n          \"insider\"\n        ],\n        \"evidenceTerms\": [\n          \"authorised\",\n          \"usb\",\n          \"patient\",\n          \"records\",\n          \"leave\"\n        ],\n        \"alternativeTerms\": [\n          \"cyber-criminal\",\n          \"cyber criminal\"\n        ]\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"J2\",\n      \"marks\": 3,\n      \"scenario\": \"Staff receive an urgent email linking to a near-identical Microsoft 365 login page that captures usernames and passwords.\",\n      \"bestAttacker\": \"phisher\",\n      \"alternative\": \"scammer\",\n      \"evidenceHints\": [\n        \"cloned login page\",\n        \"credential capture\",\n        \"urgent email\"\n      ],\n      \"sentenceStarters\": [\n        \"The attacker is most likely a phisher because\",\n        \"Although the attacker could be a scammer,\"\n      ],\n      \"modelAnswer\": \"The attacker is most likely a phisher because the lure uses a cloned Microsoft 365 page to steal credentials. Although the attacker could be a scammer, this is less likely because the immediate goal shown is credential harvesting rather than tricking finance into paying an invoice.\",\n      \"successCriteria\": [\n        \"Names phisher\",\n        \"Uses credential-harvesting evidence\",\n        \"Explains why scammer is weaker\"\n      ],\n      \"keywordChecks\": {\n        \"attackerTerms\": [\n          \"phisher\",\n          \"phishing\"\n        ],\n        \"evidenceTerms\": [\n          \"microsoft\",\n          \"login\",\n          \"password\",\n          \"credential\"\n        ],\n        \"alternativeTerms\": [\n          \"scammer\",\n          \"scam\"\n        ]\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"J3\",\n      \"marks\": 3,\n      \"scenario\": \"A group takes a public clinic webpage offline and posts that the action supports a campaign on healthcare funding. Emergency clinical systems remain untouched and no ransom is demanded.\",\n      \"bestAttacker\": \"hacktivist\",\n      \"alternative\": \"cyber-terrorist\",\n      \"evidenceHints\": [\n        \"cause statement\",\n        \"publicity/protest\",\n        \"no essential-service threat\"\n      ],\n      \"sentenceStarters\": [\n        \"The attacker is most likely a hacktivist because\",\n        \"Although the attacker could be a cyber-terrorist,\"\n      ],\n      \"modelAnswer\": \"The attacker is most likely a hacktivist because the disruption is linked to a social/political campaign message without threatening essential clinical services. Although the attacker could be a cyber-terrorist, this is less likely because there is no evidence of creating fear to coerce political change through essential-service threats.\",\n      \"successCriteria\": [\n        \"Names hacktivist\",\n        \"Uses cause/publicity evidence\",\n        \"Rejects cyber-terrorist with a reason\"\n      ],\n      \"keywordChecks\": {\n        \"attackerTerms\": [\n          \"hacktivist\"\n        ],\n        \"evidenceTerms\": [\n          \"campaign\",\n          \"funding\",\n          \"public\",\n          \"ransom\"\n        ],\n        \"alternativeTerms\": [\n          \"cyber-terrorist\",\n          \"cyber terrorist\",\n          \"terrorist\"\n        ]\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"J4\",\n      \"marks\": 3,\n      \"scenario\": \"A researcher finds an input-validation flaw in Northbank\u2019s supplier portal and asks to be paid through a disclosure programme before details are published.\",\n      \"bestAttacker\": \"vulnerability-broker\",\n      \"alternative\": \"cyber-criminal\",\n      \"evidenceHints\": [\n        \"reports a flaw\",\n        \"disclosure/bounty payment\",\n        \"not ransoming systems\"\n      ],\n      \"sentenceStarters\": [\n        \"The attacker is most likely a vulnerability broker because\",\n        \"Although the attacker could be a cyber-criminal,\"\n      ],\n      \"modelAnswer\": \"The attacker is most likely a vulnerability broker because they treat the software flaw as something to disclose for payment through a disclosure programme. Although the attacker could be a cyber-criminal, this is less likely because the scenario does not show encrypting systems or stealing data for direct criminal profit.\",\n      \"successCriteria\": [\n        \"Names vulnerability broker\",\n        \"Uses disclosure evidence\",\n        \"Rejects cyber-criminal carefully\"\n      ],\n      \"keywordChecks\": {\n        \"attackerTerms\": [\n          \"vulnerability broker\",\n          \"broker\"\n        ],\n        \"evidenceTerms\": [\n          \"flaw\",\n          \"disclosure\",\n          \"bounty\",\n          \"portal\"\n        ],\n        \"alternativeTerms\": [\n          \"cyber-criminal\",\n          \"cyber criminal\"\n        ]\n      }\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```"},"id":"week3-justified-identification-source-remainder","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"markdown","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"formative":true,"prompt":"Complete this activity on the learner hub page, then write a short note to confirm you have finished.","questionId":"week3-justified-identification:learner-note","sourceQuestionId":"learner-note"},"id":"week3-justified-identification-learner-note","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"reflection","version":"0.1.0"}],"id":"week3-justified-identification","metadata":{"activityType":"Exam skills","href":null,"runtimeGlobal":"Week3JustifiedIdentification","status":"available","summary":"Justified Identification Practice","title":"Justified Identification Practice"},"relationships":{"assets":[],"assignment":"formative-practice","learningOutcomes":["LO1"],"questions":[]},"schema":"lp.content.activity","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","version":"1.0.0"},{"blocks":[{"content":{"level":2,"text":"Session 2 Retrieval Quiz"},"id":"week3-session2-retrieval-title","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"heading","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"correctOptionId":"B","feedback":{"correct":"Script kiddies rely on tools written by others.","incorrect":"Do not use age stereotypes."},"formative":true,"options":[{"id":"A","label":"An organised attacker seeking ransom profit"},{"id":"B","label":"An inexperienced attacker using ready-made tools"},{"id":"C","label":"A staff member with legitimate access"},{"id":"D","label":"A researcher selling only lawful bounties"}],"prompt":"Which definition best matches a script kiddie?","questionId":"week3-session2-retrieval:S2Q1","sourceQuestionId":"S2Q1","sourceType":"single"},"id":"week3-session2-retrieval-q-1-S2Q1","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"single-choice","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"correctOptionId":"B","feedback":{"correct":"Immediate fraudulent payment points to a scammer.","incorrect":"Credential theft would lean towards phisher."},"formative":true,"options":[{"id":"A","label":"Phisher"},{"id":"B","label":"Scammer"},{"id":"C","label":"Cyber-terrorist"},{"id":"D","label":"Vulnerability broker"}],"prompt":"A finance team is tricked into paying a false invoice. Most likely attacker type?","questionId":"week3-session2-retrieval:S2Q2","sourceQuestionId":"S2Q2","sourceType":"single"},"id":"week3-session2-retrieval-q-2-S2Q2","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"single-choice","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"correctOptionId":"B","feedback":{"correct":"Authorised activity may resemble misuse without careful monitoring.","incorrect":"Least privilege and auditing help."},"formative":true,"options":[{"id":"A","label":"Insiders never leave logs"},{"id":"B","label":"Legitimate access can look like normal work"},{"id":"C","label":"Insiders cannot access data"},{"id":"D","label":"Insiders are always external contractors"}],"prompt":"Why can insider misuse be difficult to detect?","questionId":"week3-session2-retrieval:S2Q3","sourceQuestionId":"S2Q3","sourceType":"single"},"id":"week3-session2-retrieval-q-3-S2Q3","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"single-choice","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"correctOptionId":"B","feedback":{"correct":"Bug bounty/disclosure evidence supports vulnerability broker, not automatic criminality.","incorrect":"Brokers are not always criminals."},"formative":true,"options":[{"id":"A","label":"Cyber-criminal by default"},{"id":"B","label":"Vulnerability broker (lawful disclosure context)"},{"id":"C","label":"Hacktivist"},{"id":"D","label":"Script kiddie"}],"prompt":"A researcher discloses a flaw through a vendor bug bounty. Best label?","questionId":"week3-session2-retrieval:S2Q4","sourceQuestionId":"S2Q4","sourceType":"single"},"id":"week3-session2-retrieval-q-4-S2Q4","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"single-choice","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"correctOptionId":"A","feedback":{"correct":"Use motivation and impact evidence.","incorrect":"Avoid stereotypes."},"formative":true,"options":[{"id":"A","label":"Hacktivist seeks protest/publicity; cyber-terrorist seeks fear/coercion, often via essential services"},{"id":"B","label":"They are identical OCR terms"},{"id":"C","label":"Hacktivists always target hospitals; cyber-terrorists never do"},{"id":"D","label":"Cyber-terrorists only send invoices"}],"prompt":"Which distinction is most accurate?","questionId":"week3-session2-retrieval:S2Q5","sourceQuestionId":"S2Q5","sourceType":"single"},"id":"week3-session2-retrieval-q-5-S2Q5","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"single-choice","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"correctOptionId":"B","feedback":{"correct":"Account use and export behaviour are scenario evidence.","incorrect":"Reject age/location stereotypes."},"formative":true,"options":[{"id":"A","label":"The attacker must be young"},{"id":"B","label":"The attacker used a staff account during working hours to export records"},{"id":"C","label":"The attacker lives abroad"},{"id":"D","label":"The attacker likes gaming"}],"prompt":"Which is scenario evidence rather than a stereotype?","questionId":"week3-session2-retrieval:S2Q6","sourceQuestionId":"S2Q6","sourceType":"single"},"id":"week3-session2-retrieval-q-6-S2Q6","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"single-choice","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"correctOptionId":"B","feedback":{"correct":"Authorisation and agreed rules define lawful testing.","incorrect":"Tools alone do not decide."},"formative":true,"options":[{"id":"A","label":"The tools used"},{"id":"B","label":"Permission, scope and rules of engagement"},{"id":"C","label":"Whether Python is used"},{"id":"D","label":"Whether the tester is employed full-time"}],"prompt":"Authorised penetration testing differs from malicious attacking mainly because of:","questionId":"week3-session2-retrieval:S2Q7","sourceQuestionId":"S2Q7","sourceType":"single"},"id":"week3-session2-retrieval-q-7-S2Q7","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"single-choice","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"correctOptionId":"B","feedback":{"correct":"Profit-seeking ransomware is classic cyber-criminal evidence.","incorrect":"Script kiddie lacks organised profit focus."},"formative":true,"options":[{"id":"A","label":"Script kiddie"},{"id":"B","label":"Cyber-criminal"},{"id":"C","label":"Scammer only"},{"id":"D","label":"Insider by definition"}],"prompt":"Organised ransomware for cryptocurrency most strongly indicates:","questionId":"week3-session2-retrieval:S2Q8","sourceQuestionId":"S2Q8","sourceType":"single"},"id":"week3-session2-retrieval-q-8-S2Q8","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"single-choice","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"correctOptionId":"B","feedback":{"correct":"Credential harvesting indicates phisher.","incorrect":"False invoices without credential theft lean scammer."},"formative":true,"options":[{"id":"A","label":"Scammer"},{"id":"B","label":"Phisher"},{"id":"C","label":"Vulnerability broker"},{"id":"D","label":"Cyber-terrorist"}],"prompt":"A cloned login page harvesting passwords is stronger evidence for:","questionId":"week3-session2-retrieval:S2Q9","sourceQuestionId":"S2Q9","sourceType":"single"},"id":"week3-session2-retrieval-q-9-S2Q9","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"single-choice","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"correctOptionId":"B","feedback":{"correct":"Legitimate access is not itself misconduct.","incorrect":"Focus on risk and controls."},"formative":true,"options":[{"id":"A","label":"They are an insider threat incident"},{"id":"B","label":"They have legitimate access that must be controlled with least privilege"},{"id":"C","label":"They are a cyber-terrorist"},{"id":"D","label":"They are a script kiddie"}],"prompt":"An outsourced IT contractor uses approved admin rights to maintain servers. This alone means:","questionId":"week3-session2-retrieval:S2Q10","sourceQuestionId":"S2Q10","sourceType":"single"},"id":"week3-session2-retrieval-q-10-S2Q10","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"single-choice","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"correctOptionId":"B","feedback":{"correct":"OCR types remain the examination vocabulary.","incorrect":"Industry hats are supplementary."},"formative":true,"options":[{"id":"A","label":"Replace the eight OCR attacker types"},{"id":"B","label":"Only be used if the question asks about industry vocabulary; otherwise use OCR types"},{"id":"C","label":"Always be preferred"},{"id":"D","label":"Be used instead of \u201cinsider\u201d"}],"prompt":"White hat / grey hat / black hat terms in OCR answers should:","questionId":"week3-session2-retrieval:S2Q11","sourceQuestionId":"S2Q11","sourceType":"single"},"id":"week3-session2-retrieval-q-11-S2Q11","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"single-choice","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"correctOptionId":"B","feedback":{"correct":"Purpose and method evidence separate the labels.","incorrect":"Unlawful markets can still be criminal \u2014 use the given evidence."},"formative":true,"options":[{"id":"A","label":"Brokers are never paid"},{"id":"B","label":"The scenario focuses on disclosing/trading a flaw rather than ransoming systems for profit"},{"id":"C","label":"Brokers are always staff"},{"id":"D","label":"Cyber-criminals never use vulnerabilities"}],"prompt":"Best reason a vulnerability broker case is less likely cyber-criminal:","questionId":"week3-session2-retrieval:S2Q12","sourceQuestionId":"S2Q12","sourceType":"single"},"id":"week3-session2-retrieval-q-12-S2Q12","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"single-choice","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"format":"application/json","text":"```json\n{\n  \"weekNumber\": 3,\n  \"sessionNumber\": 2,\n  \"estimatedMinutes\": 20\n}\n```"},"id":"week3-session2-retrieval-source-remainder","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"markdown","version":"0.1.0"}],"id":"week3-session2-retrieval","metadata":{"activityType":"Retrieval quiz","href":null,"runtimeGlobal":"Week3Session2Retrieval","status":"available","summary":"Session 2 Retrieval Quiz","title":"Session 2 Retrieval Quiz"},"relationships":{"assets":[],"assignment":"formative-practice","learningOutcomes":["LO1"],"questions":[]},"schema":"lp.content.activity","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","version":"1.0.0"},{"blocks":[{"content":{"level":2,"text":"OCR-Style Question Practice"},"id":"week3-ocr-question-practice-title","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"heading","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"commandWord":"Identify","correctOptionId":"B","feedback":{"correct":"","incorrect":""},"formative":true,"marks":1,"options":[{"id":"A","label":"Scammer"},{"id":"B","label":"Phisher"},{"id":"C","label":"Script kiddie"},{"id":"D","label":"Hacktivist"}],"prompt":"Identify the OCR attacker type that uses deceptive messages or sites to steal credentials.","questionId":"week3-ocr-question-practice:O1","sourceQuestionId":"O1","sourceType":"single"},"id":"week3-ocr-question-practice-q-1-O1","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"single-choice","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"commandWord":"Identify","correctOptionId":"A","feedback":{"correct":"","incorrect":""},"formative":true,"marks":1,"options":[{"id":"A","label":"Insider"},{"id":"B","label":"Cyber-terrorist"},{"id":"C","label":"Vulnerability broker"},{"id":"D","label":"Phisher"}],"prompt":"Identify the attacker type that already has legitimate access to systems or data.","questionId":"week3-ocr-question-practice:O2","sourceQuestionId":"O2","sourceType":"single"},"id":"week3-ocr-question-practice-q-2-O2","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"single-choice","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"commandWord":"Describe","correctOptionId":"","feedback":{"correct":"","incorrect":""},"formative":true,"marks":4,"options":[],"prompt":"Describe what is meant by an insider threat in a healthcare organisation such as Northbank.","questionId":"week3-ocr-question-practice:O3","sourceQuestionId":"O3","sourceType":"single"},"id":"week3-ocr-question-practice-q-3-O3","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"single-choice","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"commandWord":"Explain","correctOptionId":"","feedback":{"correct":"","incorrect":""},"formative":true,"marks":4,"options":[],"prompt":"Explain why insider activity can be difficult to detect.","questionId":"week3-ocr-question-practice:O4","sourceQuestionId":"O4","sourceType":"single"},"id":"week3-ocr-question-practice-q-4-O4","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"single-choice","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"commandWord":"Justify","correctOptionId":"","feedback":{"correct":"","incorrect":""},"formative":true,"marks":4,"options":[],"prompt":"A fake invoice is emailed to Northbank finance requesting urgent payment to new bank details. Justify the most likely OCR attacker type and reject one alternative.","questionId":"week3-ocr-question-practice:O5","sourceQuestionId":"O5","sourceType":"single"},"id":"week3-ocr-question-practice-q-5-O5","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"single-choice","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"commandWord":"Explain","correctOptionId":"","feedback":{"correct":"","incorrect":""},"formative":true,"marks":6,"options":[],"prompt":"Northbank\u2019s public site is defaced with a message about a social cause; clinical systems are unaffected. A second scenario threatens to disable emergency booking unless a political demand is met. Explain how you would classify each attacker type using evidence.","questionId":"week3-ocr-question-practice:O6","sourceQuestionId":"O6","sourceType":"single"},"id":"week3-ocr-question-practice-q-6-O6","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"single-choice","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"format":"application/json","text":"```json\n{\n  \"weekNumber\": 3,\n  \"sessionNumber\": 2,\n  \"suggestedMinutes\": 20\n}\n```"},"id":"week3-ocr-question-practice-source-remainder","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"markdown","version":"0.1.0"}],"id":"week3-ocr-question-practice","metadata":{"activityType":"Exam skills","href":null,"runtimeGlobal":"Week3OcrPractice","status":"available","summary":"OCR-Style Question Practice","title":"OCR-Style Question Practice"},"relationships":{"assets":[],"assignment":"formative-practice","learningOutcomes":["LO1"],"questions":[]},"schema":"lp.content.activity","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","version":"1.0.0"},{"blocks":[{"content":{"level":2,"text":"Peer Marking and Answer Improvement"},"id":"week3-peer-marking-title","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"heading","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"format":"application/json","text":"```json\n{\n  \"weekNumber\": 3,\n  \"sessionNumber\": 2,\n  \"allowsPartner\": true,\n  \"question\": {\n    \"prompt\": \"A cloned Microsoft 365 page is sent to Northbank staff to collect passwords. Identify the most likely attacker type and justify your answer using scenario evidence. Reject one alternative.\",\n    \"marks\": 4\n  },\n  \"guidance\": [\n    \"Name the attacker type.\",\n    \"Quote or paraphrase scenario evidence.\",\n    \"Explain why the evidence supports the identification.\",\n    \"Where appropriate, explain why another plausible attacker type is less likely.\"\n  ],\n  \"commonError\": \"Describing what the attacker did without explaining what the behaviour reveals about the attacker type.\",\n  \"criteria\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"c1\",\n      \"label\": \"Names a precise OCR attacker type\",\n      \"marks\": 1\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"c2\",\n      \"label\": \"Uses scenario evidence (not stereotypes)\",\n      \"marks\": 1\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"c3\",\n      \"label\": \"Explains what the evidence shows about the type\",\n      \"marks\": 1\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"c4\",\n      \"label\": \"Rejects a plausible alternative with a reason\",\n      \"marks\": 1\n    }\n  ],\n  \"samples\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"weak\",\n      \"label\": \"Weak response\",\n      \"text\": \"It is probably a young hacker because young people are good with computers and like breaking things.\",\n      \"issues\": [\n        \"Stereotype\",\n        \"No OCR type precision\",\n        \"No evidence link\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"mid\",\n      \"label\": \"Mid-level response\",\n      \"text\": \"This is a phisher because there is a cloned Microsoft 365 page.\",\n      \"issues\": [\n        \"Names type and evidence but does not explain or reject alternative\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"strong\",\n      \"label\": \"Strong response\",\n      \"text\": \"The attacker is most likely a phisher because a cloned Microsoft 365 page is used to collect staff passwords. Although the attacker could be a scammer, this is less likely because the immediate aim shown is credential theft rather than tricking finance into paying an invoice.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"exemplar\": \"The attacker is most likely a phisher because the cloned Microsoft 365 sign-in page is designed to harvest credentials. Although a scammer also uses deception, that label is weaker here without payment-fraud evidence.\",\n  \"selfScoreMax\": 6\n}\n```"},"id":"week3-peer-marking-source-remainder","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"markdown","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"formative":true,"prompt":"Complete this activity on the learner hub page, then write a short note to confirm you have finished.","questionId":"week3-peer-marking:learner-note","sourceQuestionId":"learner-note"},"id":"week3-peer-marking-learner-note","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"reflection","version":"0.1.0"}],"id":"week3-peer-marking","metadata":{"activityType":"Reflection","href":null,"runtimeGlobal":"Week3PeerMarking","status":"available","summary":"Peer Marking and Answer Improvement","title":"Peer Marking and Answer Improvement"},"relationships":{"assets":[],"assignment":"formative-practice","learningOutcomes":["LO1"],"questions":[]},"schema":"lp.content.activity","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","version":"1.0.0"},{"blocks":[{"content":{"level":2,"text":"Session 1 Retrieval and Homework Harvest"},"id":"week4-session1-retrieval-title","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"heading","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"correctOptionId":"a","feedback":{"correct":"A hacktivist uses cyber methods to promote a cause. Do not confuse this with cyber-terrorism.","incorrect":"A hacktivist uses cyber methods to promote a cause. Do not confuse this with cyber-terrorism."},"formative":true,"options":[{"id":"a","label":"Hacktivist"},{"id":"b","label":"Script kiddie"},{"id":"c","label":"Vulnerability broker"},{"id":"d","label":"Cyber-criminal"}],"prompt":"Which OCR attacker type typically promotes a political, social or ethical cause?","questionId":"week4-session1-retrieval:s1q1","sourceQuestionId":"s1q1","sourceType":"single"},"id":"week4-session1-retrieval-q-1-s1q1","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"single-choice","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"correctOptionId":"b","feedback":{"correct":"Cyber-criminals are characterised by profit-seeking activity.","incorrect":"Cyber-criminals are characterised by profit-seeking activity."},"formative":true,"options":[{"id":"a","label":"Hacktivist"},{"id":"b","label":"Cyber-criminal"},{"id":"c","label":"Script kiddie"},{"id":"d","label":"Cyber-terrorist"}],"prompt":"Which attacker type is defined mainly by financial gain or criminal profit?","questionId":"week4-session1-retrieval:s1q2","sourceQuestionId":"s1q2","sourceType":"single"},"id":"week4-session1-retrieval-q-2-s1q2","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"single-choice","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"correctOptionId":"b","feedback":{"correct":"Legitimate access is the key feature of an insider threat.","incorrect":"Legitimate access is the key feature of an insider threat."},"formative":true,"options":[{"id":"a","label":"Anyone who uses phishing"},{"id":"b","label":"A person with legitimate access who causes harm through malicious or negligent behaviour"},{"id":"c","label":"Only an external criminal group"},{"id":"d","label":"A person who always seeks publicity"}],"prompt":"An insider is best described as:","questionId":"week4-session1-retrieval:s1q3","sourceQuestionId":"s1q3","sourceType":"single"},"id":"week4-session1-retrieval-q-3-s1q3","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"single-choice","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"correctOptionId":"b","feedback":{"correct":"Script kiddies typically rely on existing tools rather than advanced custom capability.","incorrect":"Script kiddies typically rely on existing tools rather than advanced custom capability."},"formative":true,"options":[{"id":"a","label":"Advanced custom exploit development only"},{"id":"b","label":"Limited skill and use of ready-made tools"},{"id":"c","label":"State-sponsored espionage"},{"id":"d","label":"Authorised penetration testing"}],"prompt":"A script kiddie is most accurately associated with:","questionId":"week4-session1-retrieval:s1q4","sourceQuestionId":"s1q4","sourceType":"single"},"id":"week4-session1-retrieval-q-4-s1q4","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"single-choice","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"correctOptionId":"b","feedback":{"correct":"Phishing uses deceptive messages. Remember: phishing is a method, not a motivation.","incorrect":"Phishing uses deceptive messages. Remember: phishing is a method, not a motivation."},"formative":true,"options":[{"id":"a","label":"Physical damage to equipment"},{"id":"b","label":"Deceptive messages designed to obtain credentials or sensitive action"},{"id":"c","label":"Quiet espionage without human contact"},{"id":"d","label":"Supply-chain hardware theft"}],"prompt":"Phishers are primarily associated with which method family?","questionId":"week4-session1-retrieval:s1q5","sourceQuestionId":"s1q5","sourceType":"single"},"id":"week4-session1-retrieval-q-5-s1q5","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"single-choice","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"correctOptionId":"b","feedback":{"correct":"Week 4 focuses on motivation (why), then target and method.","incorrect":"Week 4 focuses on motivation (why), then target and method."},"formative":true,"options":[{"id":"a","label":"Only listing more attacker types"},{"id":"b","label":"What the attacker wanted (motivation)"},{"id":"c","label":"Writing legislation essays"},{"id":"d","label":"Scanning unauthorised networks"}],"prompt":"Week 4 asks you to move from who the attacker is to:","questionId":"week4-session1-retrieval:s1q6","sourceQuestionId":"s1q6","sourceType":"single"},"id":"week4-session1-retrieval-q-6-s1q6","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"single-choice","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"correctOptionId":"c","feedback":{"correct":"Phishing describes how an attack is carried out. The others are motivations.","incorrect":"Phishing describes how an attack is carried out. The others are motivations."},"formative":true,"options":[{"id":"a","label":"Publicity"},{"id":"b","label":"Fraud"},{"id":"c","label":"Phishing"},{"id":"d","label":"Thrill"}],"prompt":"Which answer is a method rather than a motivation?","questionId":"week4-session1-retrieval:s1q7","sourceQuestionId":"s1q7","sourceType":"single"},"id":"week4-session1-retrieval-q-7-s1q7","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"single-choice","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"correctOptionId":"b","feedback":{"correct":"Vulnerability brokers deal in vulnerability information, often linked to payment or disclosure routes.","incorrect":"Vulnerability brokers deal in vulnerability information, often linked to payment or disclosure routes."},"formative":true,"options":[{"id":"a","label":"Defaces websites for protest messages"},{"id":"b","label":"Finds and trades or reports vulnerabilities, often for payment"},{"id":"c","label":"Always works only for public good with no payment"},{"id":"d","label":"Is identical to a cyber-terrorist"}],"prompt":"A vulnerability broker typically:","questionId":"week4-session1-retrieval:s1q8","sourceQuestionId":"s1q8","sourceType":"single"},"id":"week4-session1-retrieval-q-8-s1q8","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"single-choice","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"correctOptionId":"a","feedback":{"correct":"Motivation = why. Target = what. Method = how.","incorrect":"Motivation = why. Target = what. Method = how."},"formative":true,"options":[{"id":"a","label":"Why the attacker acted"},{"id":"b","label":"What was attacked"},{"id":"c","label":"How the attack was carried out"},{"id":"d","label":"Which tool was used"}],"prompt":"Motivation means:","questionId":"week4-session1-retrieval:s1q9","sourceQuestionId":"s1q9","sourceType":"single"},"id":"week4-session1-retrieval-q-9-s1q9","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"single-choice","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"correctOptionId":"b","feedback":{"correct":"OCR Week 4 target categories are people, organisations, equipment and information.","incorrect":"OCR Week 4 target categories are people, organisations, equipment and information."},"formative":true,"options":[{"id":"a","label":"Only large hospital trusts"},{"id":"b","label":"People, organisations, equipment and information"},{"id":"c","label":"Only passwords"},{"id":"d","label":"Only malware families"}],"prompt":"Targets for cyber security threats include:","questionId":"week4-session1-retrieval:s1q10","sourceQuestionId":"s1q10","sourceType":"single"},"id":"week4-session1-retrieval-q-10-s1q10","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"single-choice","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"format":"application/json","text":"```json\n{\n  \"weekNumber\": 4,\n  \"sessionNumber\": 1,\n  \"estimatedMinutes\": 20,\n  \"attackerTypes\": [\n    \"Hacktivist\",\n    \"Cyber-criminal\",\n    \"Insider\",\n    \"Script kiddie\",\n    \"Scammers / fraudsters\",\n    \"Phishers\",\n    \"Cyber-terrorist\",\n    \"Vulnerability broker\"\n  ],\n  \"researchProfileKey\": \"unit3-week3-attacker-research-profile\",\n  \"harvestPrompts\": {\n    \"intro\": \"Select or review one Week 3 attacker research profile. If your saved profile is not available in this browser, use your written Week 3 profile notes. Do not invent a learner profile.\",\n    \"fields\": [\n      {\n        \"id\": \"attackerType\",\n        \"label\": \"Attacker type\",\n        \"required\": true\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"tryingToAchieve\",\n        \"label\": \"What was the attacker trying to achieve?\",\n        \"required\": true\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"evidence\",\n        \"label\": \"Evidence that supports that interpretation\",\n        \"required\": true\n      }\n    ],\n    \"placeholderNotice\": \"No Week 3 attacker research profile was found in this browser. Use your Week 3 directed-study profile notes to complete the harvest fields.\"\n  }\n}\n```"},"id":"week4-session1-retrieval-source-remainder","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"markdown","version":"0.1.0"}],"id":"week4-session1-retrieval","metadata":{"activityType":"Retrieval quiz","href":null,"runtimeGlobal":"Week4Session1Retrieval","status":"available","summary":"Session 1 Retrieval and Homework Harvest","title":"Session 1 Retrieval and Homework Harvest"},"relationships":{"assets":[],"assignment":"formative-practice","learningOutcomes":["LO1"],"questions":[]},"schema":"lp.content.activity","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","version":"1.0.0"},{"blocks":[{"content":{"level":2,"text":"Motivations for Attack"},"id":"week4-motivations-learning-title","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"heading","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"correctOptionId":"b","feedback":{"correct":"Wanting publicity describes why the attacker acted. Phishing, interception and damage describe how or what was attacked.","incorrect":"Wanting publicity describes why the attacker acted. Phishing, interception and damage describe how or what was attacked."},"formative":true,"options":[{"id":"a","label":"The attacker used phishing emails"},{"id":"b","label":"The attacker wanted publicity for a protest message"},{"id":"c","label":"The attacker intercepted network traffic"},{"id":"d","label":"The attacker damaged clinic equipment"}],"prompt":"Which statement is a motivation rather than a method?","questionId":"week4-motivations-learning:mot-kc1","sourceQuestionId":"mot-kc1","sourceType":"single"},"id":"week4-motivations-learning-q-1-mot-kc1","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"single-choice","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"correctOptionId":"b","feedback":{"correct":"Fraud involves deception. Income generation may involve no deception, for example a ransom demand that does not rely on tricking someone with a fake identity.","incorrect":"Fraud involves deception. Income generation may involve no deception, for example a ransom demand that does not rely on tricking someone with a fake identity."},"formative":true,"options":[{"id":"a","label":"Fraud never involves money"},{"id":"b","label":"Fraud requires deception; income generation may involve no deception"},{"id":"c","label":"Income generation is always illegal and fraud is not"},{"id":"d","label":"They are identical OCR motivations"}],"prompt":"Why is fraud not identical to income generation?","questionId":"week4-motivations-learning:mot-kc2","sourceQuestionId":"mot-kc2","sourceType":"single"},"id":"week4-motivations-learning-q-2-mot-kc2","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"single-choice","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"correctOptionId":"b","feedback":{"correct":"Wanting the incident noticed supports publicity. Thrill is personal excitement; espionage seeks secrecy; phishing is a method, not a motivation.","incorrect":"Wanting the incident noticed supports publicity. Thrill is personal excitement; espionage seeks secrecy; phishing is a method, not a motivation."},"formative":true,"options":[{"id":"a","label":"Thrill"},{"id":"b","label":"Publicity"},{"id":"c","label":"Espionage"},{"id":"d","label":"Phishing"}],"prompt":"An attacker defaces a public website overnight so a protest message is widely seen. The best primary motivation is:","questionId":"week4-motivations-learning:mot-kc3","sourceQuestionId":"mot-kc3","sourceType":"single"},"id":"week4-motivations-learning-q-3-mot-kc3","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"single-choice","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"correctOptionId":"c","feedback":{"correct":"Quiet collection of confidential information without publicity fits espionage. Social engineering is a method.","incorrect":"Quiet collection of confidential information without publicity fits espionage. Social engineering is a method."},"formative":true,"options":[{"id":"a","label":"Publicity"},{"id":"b","label":"Thrill"},{"id":"c","label":"Espionage"},{"id":"d","label":"Social engineering"}],"prompt":"An attacker quietly copies confidential partnership documents without seeking attention. The best primary motivation is:","questionId":"week4-motivations-learning:mot-kc4","sourceQuestionId":"mot-kc4","sourceType":"single"},"id":"week4-motivations-learning-q-4-mot-kc4","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"single-choice","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"correctOptionId":"b","feedback":{"correct":"A ransom demand shows income generation. Exfiltration is a method. Publicity is weaker if the main aim is payment rather than attention.","incorrect":"A ransom demand shows income generation. Exfiltration is a method. Publicity is weaker if the main aim is payment rather than attention."},"formative":true,"options":[{"id":"a","label":"Public good"},{"id":"b","label":"Income generation"},{"id":"c","label":"Publicity"},{"id":"d","label":"Exfiltration"}],"prompt":"Clinic systems are encrypted and a cryptocurrency payment is demanded to restore access. The best primary motivation is:","questionId":"week4-motivations-learning:mot-kc5","sourceQuestionId":"mot-kc5","sourceType":"single"},"id":"week4-motivations-learning-q-5-mot-kc5","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"single-choice","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"correctOptionId":"b","feedback":{"correct":"Phishing describes how the attacker acts. It is a method, not a motivation.","incorrect":"Phishing describes how the attacker acts. It is a method, not a motivation."},"formative":true,"options":[{"id":"a","label":"This describes why the attacker acted"},{"id":"b","label":"This describes how the attack was carried out"},{"id":"c","label":"This describes what was attacked"},{"id":"d","label":"This is always an accepted motivation term"}],"prompt":"Which feedback best describes answering \u201cphishing\u201d to a motivation question?","questionId":"week4-motivations-learning:mot-kc6","sourceQuestionId":"mot-kc6","sourceType":"single"},"id":"week4-motivations-learning-q-6-mot-kc6","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"single-choice","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"correctOptionId":"a","feedback":{"correct":"Retaliation after a dispute fits score settling. Theft is a method against equipment.","incorrect":"Retaliation after a dispute fits score settling. Theft is a method against equipment."},"formative":true,"options":[{"id":"a","label":"Score settling"},{"id":"b","label":"Espionage"},{"id":"c","label":"Fraud"},{"id":"d","label":"Theft"}],"prompt":"A former contractor damages equipment after a heated dispute with managers. The best primary motivation is:","questionId":"week4-motivations-learning:mot-kc7","sourceQuestionId":"mot-kc7","sourceType":"single"},"id":"week4-motivations-learning-q-7-mot-kc7","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"single-choice","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"correctOptionId":"a","feedback":{"correct":"Where evidence supports more than one motivation, more than one answer may be defensible. Learners must still explain the connection to target and method.","incorrect":"Where evidence supports more than one motivation, more than one answer may be defensible. Learners must still explain the connection to target and method."},"formative":true,"options":[{"id":"a","label":"More than one motivation may be defensible when the evidence supports it"},{"id":"b","label":"Only one motivation can ever be discussed in an OCR answer"},{"id":"c","label":"Motivation and method are interchangeable terms"},{"id":"d","label":"Targets are always organisations"}],"prompt":"Which statement is true?","questionId":"week4-motivations-learning:mot-kc8","sourceQuestionId":"mot-kc8","sourceType":"single"},"id":"week4-motivations-learning-q-8-mot-kc8","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"single-choice","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"format":"application/json","text":"```json\n{\n  \"weekNumber\": 4,\n  \"sessionNumber\": 1,\n  \"distinction\": {\n    \"motivation\": \"Why the attacker acted\",\n    \"target\": \"What was attacked\",\n    \"method\": \"How the attack was carried out\"\n  },\n  \"misconceptions\": [\n    \"Answering a motivation question with a method (for example saying the attacker was motivated by phishing)\",\n    \"Treating fraud and income generation as identical\",\n    \"Collapsing thrill and publicity into a single idea of showing off\",\n    \"Assuming the target is always an organisation\"\n  ],\n  \"motivations\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"espionage\",\n      \"term\": \"Espionage\",\n      \"definition\": \"Gathering confidential information secretly for a state, competitor or other interested party.\",\n      \"explanation\": \"The attacker wants information advantage, not necessarily publicity or immediate payment.\",\n      \"evidence\": \"Quiet collection of sensitive data; focus on secrecy; interest in strategic or commercial intelligence.\",\n      \"testQuestion\": \"Did the attacker want information that others did not intend to share, without drawing attention?\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"righting-wrongs\",\n      \"term\": \"Righting perceived wrongs\",\n      \"definition\": \"Acting because the attacker believes an injustice needs to be corrected.\",\n      \"explanation\": \"The driver is a grievance or sense of unfairness, whether or not others agree with that view.\",\n      \"evidence\": \"Statements about injustice; targeting linked to a dispute; emphasis on making something \u201cright\u201d.\",\n      \"testQuestion\": \"Was the attacker mainly trying to correct something they believed was unfair?\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"public-good\",\n      \"term\": \"Public good\",\n      \"definition\": \"Claiming to act for the benefit of society, patients, citizens or the wider public.\",\n      \"explanation\": \"A claimed public-good motive does not make the act lawful. Learners still separate motivation from legality.\",\n      \"evidence\": \"Claims about protecting the public; disclosures framed as warnings; statements about patient or citizen benefit.\",\n      \"testQuestion\": \"Did the attacker claim the main reason for acting was to benefit the public?\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"publicity\",\n      \"term\": \"Publicity\",\n      \"definition\": \"Seeking attention, visibility or awareness for a message, group or cause.\",\n      \"explanation\": \"Publicity is about being noticed. It is not the same as thrill-seeking for personal excitement.\",\n      \"evidence\": \"Defacement messages; media contact; timing chosen for maximum visibility.\",\n      \"testQuestion\": \"Did the attacker want the incident to be noticed?\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"thrill\",\n      \"term\": \"Thrill\",\n      \"definition\": \"Acting mainly for excitement, challenge or personal enjoyment.\",\n      \"explanation\": \"Thrill focuses on the experience of the attack, not necessarily on a public message.\",\n      \"evidence\": \"Boasting in private channels; focus on difficulty of the challenge; little coherent public cause.\",\n      \"testQuestion\": \"Was the main reason personal excitement or challenge rather than a public message or profit?\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"fraud\",\n      \"term\": \"Fraud\",\n      \"definition\": \"Gaining money or advantage through deception.\",\n      \"explanation\": \"Fraud requires deception. It is not identical to every form of income generation.\",\n      \"evidence\": \"Fake invoices; spoofed identity; tricking staff into transferring funds or credentials.\",\n      \"testQuestion\": \"Did the attacker use deception to obtain money or another advantage?\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"score-settling\",\n      \"term\": \"Score settling\",\n      \"definition\": \"Acting to punish, retaliate or get even with a person or organisation.\",\n      \"explanation\": \"The driver is revenge or retaliation linked to a prior conflict.\",\n      \"evidence\": \"Prior dispute; personal targeting; messages about payback.\",\n      \"testQuestion\": \"Was the attacker mainly trying to retaliate against someone or something?\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"income-generation\",\n      \"term\": \"Income generation\",\n      \"definition\": \"Seeking financial gain, which may or may not involve deception.\",\n      \"explanation\": \"Income generation does not always require deception. Ransomware payment demands can be income generation without the same deception pattern as invoice fraud.\",\n      \"evidence\": \"Ransom demands; sale of stolen data; repeated monetisation patterns.\",\n      \"testQuestion\": \"Was the primary aim to make money, whether or not deception was used?\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```"},"id":"week4-motivations-learning-source-remainder","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"markdown","version":"0.1.0"}],"id":"week4-motivations-learning","metadata":{"activityType":"Guided learning","href":null,"runtimeGlobal":"Week4Motivations","status":"available","summary":"Motivations for Attack","title":"Motivations for Attack"},"relationships":{"assets":[],"assignment":"formative-practice","learningOutcomes":["LO1"],"questions":[]},"schema":"lp.content.activity","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","version":"1.0.0"},{"blocks":[{"content":{"level":2,"text":"Targets and Methods"},"id":"week4-targets-methods-title","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"heading","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"format":"application/json","text":"```json\n{\n  \"weekNumber\": 4,\n  \"sessionNumber\": 1,\n  \"whyWhatHow\": {\n    \"why\": \"Motivation \u2014 why the attacker acted\",\n    \"what\": \"Target \u2014 what was attacked\",\n    \"how\": \"Method \u2014 how the attack was conducted\"\n  },\n  \"targetCategories\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"people\",\n      \"term\": \"People\",\n      \"methods\": [\n        \"Social engineering\",\n        \"Phishing\"\n      ],\n      \"explanation\": \"People are targeted when the attacker manipulates human trust or behaviour.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"organisations\",\n      \"term\": \"Organisations\",\n      \"methods\": [\n        \"System compromise\",\n        \"Supply-chain compromise\"\n      ],\n      \"explanation\": \"Organisations are targeted when systems, processes or trusted suppliers are compromised.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"equipment\",\n      \"term\": \"Equipment\",\n      \"methods\": [\n        \"Theft\",\n        \"Damage\"\n      ],\n      \"explanation\": \"Equipment is targeted when devices or hardware are stolen or physically harmed.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"information\",\n      \"term\": \"Information\",\n      \"methods\": [\n        \"Interception\",\n        \"Exfiltration\"\n      ],\n      \"explanation\": \"Information is targeted when data is intercepted in transit or taken from systems.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"classificationItems\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"tm1\",\n      \"statement\": \"The attacker wanted to raise awareness of a protest message.\",\n      \"correctCategory\": \"motivation\",\n      \"explanation\": \"This describes why the attacker acted (publicity).\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"tm2\",\n      \"statement\": \"Reception staff were targeted with fake payroll emails.\",\n      \"correctCategory\": \"target\",\n      \"explanation\": \"People are the target category. Phishing would be the method.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"tm3\",\n      \"statement\": \"The attacker used phishing to collect login details.\",\n      \"correctCategory\": \"method\",\n      \"explanation\": \"Phishing describes how the attack was carried out.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"tm4\",\n      \"statement\": \"A clinic laptop was stolen from an unlocked room.\",\n      \"correctCategory\": \"method\",\n      \"explanation\": \"Theft is a method used against equipment. The equipment is the target.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"tm5\",\n      \"statement\": \"Patient appointment records were copied out of the system.\",\n      \"correctCategory\": \"method\",\n      \"explanation\": \"Exfiltration describes how information was taken. Information is the target.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"tm6\",\n      \"statement\": \"The attacker aimed to generate income through a ransom demand.\",\n      \"correctCategory\": \"motivation\",\n      \"explanation\": \"Income generation is why the attacker acted. Ransomware language alone is not the motivation label.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"tm7\",\n      \"statement\": \"A trusted supplier portal was compromised to reach Northbank systems.\",\n      \"correctCategory\": \"method\",\n      \"explanation\": \"Supply-chain compromise is a method used against an organisation target.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"tm8\",\n      \"statement\": \"The main thing attacked was the organisation\u2019s booking systems.\",\n      \"correctCategory\": \"target\",\n      \"explanation\": \"Organisations (and their systems) are what was targeted.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"categories\": [\n    \"motivation\",\n    \"target\",\n    \"method\"\n  ]\n}\n```"},"id":"week4-targets-methods-source-remainder","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"markdown","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"formative":true,"prompt":"Complete this activity on the learner hub page, then write a short note to confirm you have finished.","questionId":"week4-targets-methods:learner-note","sourceQuestionId":"learner-note"},"id":"week4-targets-methods-learner-note","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"reflection","version":"0.1.0"}],"id":"week4-targets-methods","metadata":{"activityType":"Classification","href":null,"runtimeGlobal":"Week4TargetsMethods","status":"available","summary":"Targets and Methods","title":"Targets and Methods"},"relationships":{"assets":[],"assignment":"formative-practice","learningOutcomes":["LO1"],"questions":[]},"schema":"lp.content.activity","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","version":"1.0.0"},{"blocks":[{"content":{"level":2,"text":"Northbank Passive-Exposure Reflection"},"id":"week4-northbank-exposure-title","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"heading","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"format":"application/json","text":"```json\n{\n  \"weekNumber\": 4,\n  \"sessionNumber\": 1,\n  \"organisationName\": \"Northbank Community Health Partnership\",\n  \"fictionalNotice\": \"Northbank is a fictional teaching organisation used across Unit 3. Do not treat it as a real health provider and do not perform passive reconnaissance against any real organisation.\",\n  \"establishedFacts\": [\n    \"Northbank is a healthcare organisation with clinics.\",\n    \"It has a patient appointment portal.\",\n    \"It has a public website.\",\n    \"Reception staff handle email and visitor-facing tasks.\",\n    \"Finance processes invoices and payments.\",\n    \"There is a server room and clinic computing equipment (including laptops).\",\n    \"Remote access arrangements (such as RDP for home working) have been discussed in earlier weeks.\",\n    \"There is a supplier / booking portal context in earlier week scenarios.\",\n    \"Patient records and contact lists are sensitive information holdings discussed in earlier weeks.\"\n  ],\n  \"notAvailableGuidance\": \"If a detail is not available in the Northbank briefing or earlier week materials, write \u201cnot available in the briefing\u201d rather than inventing systems, employees, suppliers, vulnerabilities or services.\",\n  \"conclusion\": \"Target selection may be driven by exposure and opportunity rather than by a personal grudge against the victim.\",\n  \"prompts\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"exposure-1\",\n      \"label\": \"Exposure item 1\",\n      \"fields\": [\n        {\n          \"id\": \"item\",\n          \"label\": \"What could a passive reconnaissance sweep expose about Northbank?\",\n          \"required\": true\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"motivation\",\n          \"label\": \"Which motivation could this exposed item serve?\",\n          \"required\": true\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"whyAttractive\",\n          \"label\": \"Why might that exposure make Northbank an attractive or opportunistic target?\",\n          \"required\": true\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"exposure-2\",\n      \"label\": \"Exposure item 2\",\n      \"fields\": [\n        {\n          \"id\": \"item\",\n          \"label\": \"What could a passive reconnaissance sweep expose about Northbank?\",\n          \"required\": true\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"motivation\",\n          \"label\": \"Which motivation could this exposed item serve?\",\n          \"required\": true\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"whyAttractive\",\n          \"label\": \"Why might that exposure make Northbank an attractive or opportunistic target?\",\n          \"required\": true\n        }\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"exposure-3\",\n      \"label\": \"Exposure item 3\",\n      \"fields\": [\n        {\n          \"id\": \"item\",\n          \"label\": \"What could a passive reconnaissance sweep expose about Northbank?\",\n          \"required\": true\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"motivation\",\n          \"label\": \"Which motivation could this exposed item serve?\",\n          \"required\": true\n        },\n        {\n          \"id\": \"whyAttractive\",\n          \"label\": \"Why might that exposure make Northbank an attractive or opportunistic target?\",\n          \"required\": true\n        }\n      ]\n    }\n  ],\n  \"session1Review\": {\n    \"title\": \"Session 1 review\",\n    \"fields\": [\n      {\n        \"id\": \"mtmDifference\",\n        \"label\": \"Difference between motivation, target and method\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"opportunisticExample\",\n        \"label\": \"One example of opportunistic target selection\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"misconceptionCorrected\",\n        \"label\": \"One misconception you corrected\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"directedStudyTasks\",\n        \"label\": \"Your directed independent study tasks\"\n      }\n    ]\n  },\n  \"motivationBank\": [\n    \"Espionage\",\n    \"Righting perceived wrongs\",\n    \"Public good\",\n    \"Publicity\",\n    \"Thrill\",\n    \"Fraud\",\n    \"Score settling\",\n    \"Income generation\"\n  ]\n}\n```"},"id":"week4-northbank-exposure-source-remainder","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"markdown","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"formative":true,"prompt":"Complete this activity on the learner hub page, then write a short note to confirm you have finished.","questionId":"week4-northbank-exposure:learner-note","sourceQuestionId":"learner-note"},"id":"week4-northbank-exposure-learner-note","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"reflection","version":"0.1.0"}],"id":"week4-northbank-exposure","metadata":{"activityType":"Reflection","href":null,"runtimeGlobal":"Week4NorthbankExposure","status":"available","summary":"Northbank Passive-Exposure Reflection","title":"Northbank Passive-Exposure Reflection"},"relationships":{"assets":[],"assignment":"formative-practice","learningOutcomes":["LO1"],"questions":[]},"schema":"lp.content.activity","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","version":"1.0.0"},{"blocks":[{"content":{"level":2,"text":"Session 2 Retrieval Quiz"},"id":"week4-session2-retrieval-title","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"heading","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"correctOptionId":"a","feedback":{"correct":"Wanting publicity describes why the attacker acted. Motivation = why.","incorrect":"Wanting publicity describes why the attacker acted. Motivation = why."},"formative":true,"options":[{"id":"a","label":"Motivation"},{"id":"b","label":"Target"},{"id":"c","label":"Method"}],"prompt":"Classify this statement: \u201cThe attacker wanted publicity for a protest message.\u201d","questionId":"week4-session2-retrieval:s2q1","sourceQuestionId":"s2q1","sourceType":"single"},"id":"week4-session2-retrieval-q-1-s2q1","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"single-choice","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"correctOptionId":"c","feedback":{"correct":"Phishing describes how the attacker acts. It is a method, not a motivation. People are the target category.","incorrect":"Phishing describes how the attacker acts. It is a method, not a motivation. People are the target category."},"formative":true,"options":[{"id":"a","label":"Motivation"},{"id":"b","label":"Target"},{"id":"c","label":"Method"}],"prompt":"Classify this statement: \u201cReception staff were sent phishing emails.\u201d","questionId":"week4-session2-retrieval:s2q2","sourceQuestionId":"s2q2","sourceType":"single"},"id":"week4-session2-retrieval-q-2-s2q2","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"single-choice","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"correctOptionId":"c","feedback":{"correct":"Exfiltration describes how information was taken. Information is the target; exfiltration is the method.","incorrect":"Exfiltration describes how information was taken. Information is the target; exfiltration is the method."},"formative":true,"options":[{"id":"a","label":"Motivation"},{"id":"b","label":"Target"},{"id":"c","label":"Method"}],"prompt":"Classify this statement: \u201cPatient appointment records were copied out of the system.\u201d","questionId":"week4-session2-retrieval:s2q3","sourceQuestionId":"s2q3","sourceType":"single"},"id":"week4-session2-retrieval-q-3-s2q3","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"single-choice","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"correctOptionId":"b","feedback":{"correct":"Organisations (and their systems) are what was attacked. Target = what.","incorrect":"Organisations (and their systems) are what was attacked. Target = what."},"formative":true,"options":[{"id":"a","label":"Motivation"},{"id":"b","label":"Target"},{"id":"c","label":"Method"}],"prompt":"Classify this statement: \u201cThe main thing attacked was the organisation\u2019s booking systems.\u201d","questionId":"week4-session2-retrieval:s2q4","sourceQuestionId":"s2q4","sourceType":"single"},"id":"week4-session2-retrieval-q-4-s2q4","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"single-choice","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"correctOptionId":"c","feedback":{"correct":"Theft is a method used against equipment. Equipment is the target category.","incorrect":"Theft is a method used against equipment. Equipment is the target category."},"formative":true,"options":[{"id":"a","label":"Motivation"},{"id":"b","label":"Target"},{"id":"c","label":"Method"}],"prompt":"Classify this statement: \u201cA clinic laptop was stolen from an unlocked room.\u201d","questionId":"week4-session2-retrieval:s2q5","sourceQuestionId":"s2q5","sourceType":"single"},"id":"week4-session2-retrieval-q-5-s2q5","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"single-choice","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"correctOptionId":"a","feedback":{"correct":"Income generation is why the attacker acted. Do not treat ransomware alone as the motivation label.","incorrect":"Income generation is why the attacker acted. Do not treat ransomware alone as the motivation label."},"formative":true,"options":[{"id":"a","label":"Motivation"},{"id":"b","label":"Target"},{"id":"c","label":"Method"}],"prompt":"Classify this statement: \u201cThe attacker aimed to generate income through a ransom demand.\u201d","questionId":"week4-session2-retrieval:s2q6","sourceQuestionId":"s2q6","sourceType":"single"},"id":"week4-session2-retrieval-q-6-s2q6","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"single-choice","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"correctOptionId":"c","feedback":{"correct":"Supply-chain compromise is a method. The organisation is the target category.","incorrect":"Supply-chain compromise is a method. The organisation is the target category."},"formative":true,"options":[{"id":"a","label":"Motivation"},{"id":"b","label":"Target"},{"id":"c","label":"Method"}],"prompt":"Classify this statement: \u201cA trusted supplier portal was compromised to reach Northbank systems.\u201d","questionId":"week4-session2-retrieval:s2q7","sourceQuestionId":"s2q7","sourceType":"single"},"id":"week4-session2-retrieval-q-7-s2q7","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"single-choice","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"correctOptionId":"b","feedback":{"correct":"Phishing is a method because it describes how the attacker acts. It is not the reason the attacker chose to act.","incorrect":"Phishing is a method because it describes how the attacker acts. It is not the reason the attacker chose to act."},"formative":true,"options":[{"id":"a","label":"Because phishing is never used against people"},{"id":"b","label":"Because phishing describes how the attacker acts, not why"},{"id":"c","label":"Because phishing is always the same as fraud"},{"id":"d","label":"Because OCR does not recognise phishing"}],"prompt":"Why is \u201cphishing\u201d not a valid answer to a motivation question?","questionId":"week4-session2-retrieval:s2q8","sourceQuestionId":"s2q8","sourceType":"single"},"id":"week4-session2-retrieval-q-8-s2q8","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"single-choice","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"correctOptionId":"b","feedback":{"correct":"Fraud requires deception. Income generation does not always require deception.","incorrect":"Fraud requires deception. Income generation does not always require deception."},"formative":true,"options":[{"id":"a","label":"Fraud never involves money"},{"id":"b","label":"Fraud requires deception; income generation may involve no deception"},{"id":"c","label":"They are identical OCR motivations"},{"id":"d","label":"Income generation is only about publicity"}],"prompt":"Fraud differs from income generation because:","questionId":"week4-session2-retrieval:s2q9","sourceQuestionId":"s2q9","sourceType":"single"},"id":"week4-session2-retrieval-q-9-s2q9","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"single-choice","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"correctOptionId":"b","feedback":{"correct":"Publicity is about being noticed. Thrill is about personal excitement or challenge.","incorrect":"Publicity is about being noticed. Thrill is about personal excitement or challenge."},"formative":true,"options":[{"id":"a","label":"Both always involve ransomware"},{"id":"b","label":"Publicity seeks notice for a message; thrill focuses on personal excitement or challenge"},{"id":"c","label":"OCR only allows one motivation ever"},{"id":"d","label":"Thrill is a method and publicity is a target"}],"prompt":"Publicity and thrill should not be collapsed into one idea because:","questionId":"week4-session2-retrieval:s2q10","sourceQuestionId":"s2q10","sourceType":"single"},"id":"week4-session2-retrieval-q-10-s2q10","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"single-choice","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"correctOptionId":"a","feedback":{"correct":"Targets are people, organisations, equipment and information \u2014 not attacker types or methods.","incorrect":"Targets are people, organisations, equipment and information \u2014 not attacker types or methods."},"formative":true,"options":[{"id":"a","label":"People, organisations, equipment and information"},{"id":"b","label":"Malware, phishing, ransomware and firewalls"},{"id":"c","label":"Hacktivists, insiders, criminals and script kiddies"},{"id":"d","label":"Only large hospital trusts"}],"prompt":"Which list correctly names the four OCR target categories for Week 4?","questionId":"week4-session2-retrieval:s2q11","sourceQuestionId":"s2q11","sourceType":"single"},"id":"week4-session2-retrieval-q-11-s2q11","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"single-choice","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"correctOptionId":"b","feedback":{"correct":"Analysis states a connection or consequence. Connectives help only when the link is logically meaningful.","incorrect":"Analysis states a connection or consequence. Connectives help only when the link is logically meaningful."},"formative":true,"options":[{"id":"a","label":"List separate facts without linking them"},{"id":"b","label":"State a meaningful connection or consequence between facts"},{"id":"c","label":"Insert connective words with no logical link"},{"id":"d","label":"Change examples halfway through to show breadth"}],"prompt":"Analyse as a command word requires learners to:","questionId":"week4-session2-retrieval:s2q12","sourceQuestionId":"s2q12","sourceType":"single"},"id":"week4-session2-retrieval-q-12-s2q12","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"single-choice","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"format":"application/json","text":"```json\n{\n  \"weekNumber\": 4,\n  \"sessionNumber\": 2,\n  \"estimatedMinutes\": 15,\n  \"distinction\": {\n    \"motivation\": \"Why the attacker acted\",\n    \"target\": \"What was attacked\",\n    \"method\": \"How the attack was carried out\"\n  }\n}\n```"},"id":"week4-session2-retrieval-source-remainder","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"markdown","version":"0.1.0"}],"id":"week4-session2-retrieval","metadata":{"activityType":"Retrieval quiz","href":null,"runtimeGlobal":"Week4Session2Retrieval","status":"available","summary":"Session 2 Retrieval Quiz","title":"Session 2 Retrieval Quiz"},"relationships":{"assets":[],"assignment":"formative-practice","learningOutcomes":["LO1"],"questions":[]},"schema":"lp.content.activity","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","version":"1.0.0"},{"blocks":[{"content":{"level":2,"text":"Motivation, Target and Method Mapping"},"id":"week4-mtm-mapping-title","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"heading","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"format":"application/json","text":"```json\n{\n  \"weekNumber\": 4,\n  \"sessionNumber\": 2,\n  \"columnLabels\": {\n    \"motivation\": \"Motivation (why)\",\n    \"target\": \"Target (what)\",\n    \"method\": \"Method (how)\",\n    \"evidence\": \"Evidence from the scenario\",\n    \"connection\": \"How the motivation made the target and method a logical choice\",\n    \"alternative\": \"Optional alternative motivation\",\n    \"alternativeWhy\": \"Why the alternative is weaker or equally defensible\"\n  },\n  \"motivationBank\": [\n    \"Espionage\",\n    \"Righting perceived wrongs\",\n    \"Public good\",\n    \"Publicity\",\n    \"Thrill\",\n    \"Fraud\",\n    \"Score settling\",\n    \"Income generation\"\n  ],\n  \"targetBank\": [\n    \"People\",\n    \"Organisations\",\n    \"Equipment\",\n    \"Information\"\n  ],\n  \"methodBank\": [\n    \"Social engineering\",\n    \"Phishing\",\n    \"System compromise\",\n    \"Supply-chain compromise\",\n    \"Theft\",\n    \"Damage\",\n    \"Interception\",\n    \"Exfiltration\"\n  ],\n  \"presentationOptions\": [\n    \"Verbal two-minute explanation\",\n    \"Slide-based explanation\",\n    \"Annotated diagram\"\n  ],\n  \"presentationChecklist\": [\n    \"State the motivation (why)\",\n    \"State the target (what)\",\n    \"State the method (how)\",\n    \"Explain why the motivation made that target logical\",\n    \"Explain why the selected method suited the target\"\n  ],\n  \"workedRows\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"worked-1\",\n      \"theme\": \"Espionage (worked example)\",\n      \"scenario\": \"Quiet collection of confidential partnership documents from a Northbank shared drive overnight. No public message is left and no ransom is demanded.\",\n      \"motivation\": \"Espionage\",\n      \"target\": \"Information\",\n      \"method\": \"Exfiltration\",\n      \"evidence\": \"Quiet collection; confidential documents; no publicity or ransom demand.\",\n      \"connection\": \"Because the attacker wanted secret information advantage, information was a logical target, and exfiltration suited removing copies without seeking attention.\",\n      \"alternative\": \"Thrill\",\n      \"alternativeWhy\": \"Thrill is weaker here because the evidence emphasises secrecy and useful documents rather than personal challenge or excitement.\",\n      \"teachingNote\": \"Notice the connection sentence links why \u2192 what \u2192 how. Listing the three facts alone would only describe, not analyse.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"worked-2\",\n      \"theme\": \"High-profile defacement (worked example)\",\n      \"scenario\": \"Northbank\u2019s public website is changed overnight to display a large protest message about NHS funding. Clinical systems are not encrypted.\",\n      \"motivation\": \"Publicity\",\n      \"target\": \"Organisations\",\n      \"method\": \"System compromise\",\n      \"evidence\": \"Public protest message; high-visibility website; clinical systems left alone.\",\n      \"connection\": \"Because the attacker wanted the incident noticed, a public organisational website was a logical target, and system compromise of that site suited delivering a visible message.\",\n      \"alternative\": \"Thrill\",\n      \"alternativeWhy\": \"Thrill could be discussed, but the protest message and funding theme make publicity the stronger primary motivation.\",\n      \"teachingNote\": \"Publicity seeks notice. Do not collapse this into thrill just because the attacker \u201cshowed off\u201d.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"scenarios\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"map-espionage\",\n      \"theme\": \"Espionage\",\n      \"title\": \"Quiet document collection\",\n      \"scenario\": \"An attacker copies confidential supplier-contract files from Northbank systems and leaves no public statement. The copies appear intended for another interested party.\",\n      \"acceptedMotivations\": [\n        \"Espionage\"\n      ],\n      \"acceptedTargets\": [\n        \"Information\",\n        \"Organisations\"\n      ],\n      \"acceptedMethods\": [\n        \"Exfiltration\",\n        \"System compromise\"\n      ],\n      \"primaryMotivation\": \"Espionage\",\n      \"primaryTarget\": \"Information\",\n      \"primaryMethod\": \"Exfiltration\",\n      \"ambiguous\": false,\n      \"hint\": \"Look for secrecy and information advantage rather than publicity or payment.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"map-hacktivism\",\n      \"theme\": \"Hacktivism\",\n      \"title\": \"Cause-driven website message\",\n      \"scenario\": \"Northbank\u2019s public site shows a message criticising local health funding. The attackers claim they acted so patients and citizens would notice the issue. Clinical systems are unaffected.\",\n      \"acceptedMotivations\": [\n        \"Publicity\",\n        \"Public good\",\n        \"Righting perceived wrongs\"\n      ],\n      \"acceptedTargets\": [\n        \"Organisations\"\n      ],\n      \"acceptedMethods\": [\n        \"System compromise\"\n      ],\n      \"primaryMotivation\": \"Publicity\",\n      \"primaryTarget\": \"Organisations\",\n      \"primaryMethod\": \"System compromise\",\n      \"ambiguous\": true,\n      \"ambiguousNote\": \"Publicity is strongly supported by wanting the incident noticed. Public good or righting perceived wrongs may also be defensible if you use the claim about patients and citizens \u2014 explain which evidence you rely on.\",\n      \"hint\": \"At least two motivations can be defensible; explain the connection rather than only naming labels.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"map-ransomware\",\n      \"theme\": \"Ransomware\",\n      \"title\": \"Encrypted clinics and payment demand\",\n      \"scenario\": \"Clinic booking systems are encrypted and a cryptocurrency payment is demanded to restore access. No political message is published.\",\n      \"acceptedMotivations\": [\n        \"Income generation\"\n      ],\n      \"acceptedTargets\": [\n        \"Organisations\",\n        \"Information\"\n      ],\n      \"acceptedMethods\": [\n        \"System compromise\"\n      ],\n      \"primaryMotivation\": \"Income generation\",\n      \"primaryTarget\": \"Organisations\",\n      \"primaryMethod\": \"System compromise\",\n      \"ambiguous\": false,\n      \"hint\": \"Payment demand without deception language points to income generation rather than fraud.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"map-defacement\",\n      \"theme\": \"High-profile defacement\",\n      \"title\": \"Visible protest banner\",\n      \"scenario\": \"A high-visibility banner is placed on Northbank\u2019s homepage overnight so that anyone visiting the site sees a protest slogan. Staff later find the change came through a compromised web account.\",\n      \"acceptedMotivations\": [\n        \"Publicity\"\n      ],\n      \"acceptedTargets\": [\n        \"Organisations\"\n      ],\n      \"acceptedMethods\": [\n        \"System compromise\"\n      ],\n      \"primaryMotivation\": \"Publicity\",\n      \"primaryTarget\": \"Organisations\",\n      \"primaryMethod\": \"System compromise\",\n      \"ambiguous\": false,\n      \"hint\": \"Wanting visitors to see a slogan supports publicity as why.\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```"},"id":"week4-mtm-mapping-source-remainder","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"markdown","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"formative":true,"prompt":"Complete this activity on the learner hub page, then write a short note to confirm you have finished.","questionId":"week4-mtm-mapping:learner-note","sourceQuestionId":"learner-note"},"id":"week4-mtm-mapping-learner-note","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"reflection","version":"0.1.0"}],"id":"week4-mtm-mapping","metadata":{"activityType":"Scenario mapping","href":null,"runtimeGlobal":"Week4MtmMapping","status":"available","summary":"Motivation, Target and Method Mapping","title":"Motivation, Target and Method Mapping"},"relationships":{"assets":[],"assignment":"formative-practice","learningOutcomes":["LO1"],"questions":[]},"schema":"lp.content.activity","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","version":"1.0.0"},{"blocks":[{"content":{"level":2,"text":"From Describe to Analyse"},"id":"week4-analyse-practice-title","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"heading","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"format":"application/json","text":"```json\n{\n  \"weekNumber\": 4,\n  \"sessionNumber\": 2,\n  \"commandWords\": {\n    \"describe\": \"Present the main features of something. Separate facts can be enough when the command word is describe.\",\n    \"analyse\": \"Examine in detail and state a connection or consequence. Analysis is more than listing motivation, target and method as separate facts.\"\n  },\n  \"connectives\": [\n    \"because\",\n    \"which means that\",\n    \"as a result\",\n    \"therefore\"\n  ],\n  \"connectiveWarning\": \"Inserting these words does not automatically create analysis. The connection must be logically meaningful.\",\n  \"planningQuestion\": \"Why might a small health partnership be a more attractive target than a large hospital trust?\",\n  \"planningGuidance\": \"Use only existing Northbank information. If a detail is not in the briefing, stay appropriately general rather than inventing operational facts about either organisation. Sustain one case throughout.\",\n  \"planningTemplates\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"frame\",\n      \"label\": \"Writing frame\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"table\",\n      \"label\": \"Planning table\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"mindmap\",\n      \"label\": \"Mind map notes\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"writingFrame\": [\n    \"Plausible motivation (why): \u2026\",\n    \"Relevant target (what): \u2026\",\n    \"Appropriate method (how): \u2026\",\n    \"Connection: \u2026 because \u2026 which means that \u2026 As a result \u2026 Therefore \u2026\"\n  ],\n  \"weakResponse\": {\n    \"label\": \"Weak (descriptive) response\",\n    \"text\": \"A small health partnership might be targeted. The motivation could be income generation. The target could be organisations. The method could be system compromise. Large trusts are bigger.\",\n    \"problem\": \"This lists separate facts about motivation, target and method with no sentence connecting them, and it switches comparison focus without sustaining one analytical thread.\"\n  },\n  \"improvedResponse\": {\n    \"label\": \"Improved (analytical) response\",\n    \"text\": \"Income generation could motivate an attacker to choose a small health partnership such as Northbank because limited specialist cyber capacity may make recovery slower after system compromise of booking systems, which means that a ransom demand is more likely to succeed. As a result, the organisation becomes an opportunistic target. Therefore the motivation makes the organisational target and encryption-style method a logical combination, rather than a personal grudge against that specific partnership.\",\n    \"annotations\": [\n      \"Names a motivation (income generation).\",\n      \"Keeps one case (small health partnership / Northbank) throughout.\",\n      \"Connects organisation characteristics to attacker choice.\",\n      \"Links motivation \u2192 target \u2192 method with meaningful connectives.\",\n      \"Completes the final connection rather than leaving it implied.\"\n    ]\n  },\n  \"checklist\": [\n    \"Identify a plausible motivation\",\n    \"Identify the relevant target\",\n    \"Identify an appropriate method\",\n    \"Connect organisation characteristics to the attacker\u2019s choice\",\n    \"Sustain the same case throughout\",\n    \"Complete the final connection explicitly\"\n  ]\n}\n```"},"id":"week4-analyse-practice-source-remainder","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"markdown","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"formative":true,"prompt":"Complete this activity on the learner hub page, then write a short note to confirm you have finished.","questionId":"week4-analyse-practice:learner-note","sourceQuestionId":"learner-note"},"id":"week4-analyse-practice-learner-note","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"reflection","version":"0.1.0"}],"id":"week4-analyse-practice","metadata":{"activityType":"Exam skills","href":null,"runtimeGlobal":"Week4AnalysePractice","status":"available","summary":"From Describe to Analyse","title":"From Describe to Analyse"},"relationships":{"assets":[],"assignment":"formative-practice","learningOutcomes":["LO1"],"questions":[]},"schema":"lp.content.activity","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","version":"1.0.0"},{"blocks":[{"content":{"level":2,"text":"OCR-Style Question Practice"},"id":"week4-ocr-question-practice-title","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"heading","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"commandWord":"Identify","correctOptionId":"b","feedback":{"correct":"","incorrect":""},"formative":true,"marks":1,"options":[{"id":"a","label":"Phishing"},{"id":"b","label":"Publicity"},{"id":"c","label":"Exfiltration"},{"id":"d","label":"Damage"}],"prompt":"Identify which of the following is an OCR attacker motivation.","questionId":"week4-ocr-question-practice:ocr-1","sourceQuestionId":"ocr-1","sourceType":"single"},"id":"week4-ocr-question-practice-q-1-ocr-1","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"single-choice","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"commandWord":"Identify","correctOptionId":"a","feedback":{"correct":"","incorrect":""},"formative":true,"marks":1,"options":[{"id":"a","label":"People"},{"id":"b","label":"Equipment"},{"id":"c","label":"Fraud"},{"id":"d","label":"Thrill"}],"prompt":"Identify the target category when reception staff are sent deceptive emails.","questionId":"week4-ocr-question-practice:ocr-2","sourceQuestionId":"ocr-2","sourceType":"single"},"id":"week4-ocr-question-practice-q-2-ocr-2","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"single-choice","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"commandWord":"Explain","correctOptionId":"","feedback":{"correct":"","incorrect":""},"formative":true,"marks":2,"options":[],"prompt":"Explain the difference between fraud and income generation as attacker motivations.","questionId":"week4-ocr-question-practice:ocr-3","sourceQuestionId":"ocr-3","sourceType":"single"},"id":"week4-ocr-question-practice-q-3-ocr-3","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"single-choice","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"commandWord":"Describe","correctOptionId":"","feedback":{"correct":"","incorrect":""},"formative":true,"marks":4,"options":[],"prompt":"Describe the four categories of target for cyber security threats and give one associated method for each.","questionId":"week4-ocr-question-practice:ocr-4","sourceQuestionId":"ocr-4","sourceType":"single"},"id":"week4-ocr-question-practice-q-4-ocr-4","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"single-choice","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"commandWord":"Explain","correctOptionId":"","feedback":{"correct":"","incorrect":""},"formative":true,"marks":4,"options":[],"prompt":"Explain the difference between motivation, target and method, using one short Northbank-related example.","questionId":"week4-ocr-question-practice:ocr-5","sourceQuestionId":"ocr-5","sourceType":"single"},"id":"week4-ocr-question-practice-q-5-ocr-5","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"single-choice","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"commandWord":"Analyse","correctOptionId":"","feedback":{"correct":"","incorrect":""},"formative":true,"marks":8,"options":[],"prompt":"Northbank\u2019s public website is defaced with a protest message about health funding. Clinical systems are not encrypted and no ransom is demanded. Analyse why this organisation was targeted, connecting attacker motivation, selected target and method used. Use evidence from the scenario.","questionId":"week4-ocr-question-practice:ocr-6","sourceQuestionId":"ocr-6","sourceType":"single"},"id":"week4-ocr-question-practice-q-6-ocr-6","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"single-choice","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"format":"application/json","text":"```json\n{\n  \"weekNumber\": 4,\n  \"sessionNumber\": 2,\n  \"suggestedMinutes\": 20,\n  \"timingGuidance\": \"Use approximately one minute per mark where this helps you manage time.\",\n  \"beforeReminders\": [\n    \"Read whether the question asks for motivation, target or method.\",\n    \"Use one case consistently.\",\n    \"Include explicit connections.\",\n    \"Complete the final connection rather than leaving it implied.\",\n    \"Allocate time according to the marks available.\"\n  ]\n}\n```"},"id":"week4-ocr-question-practice-source-remainder","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"markdown","version":"0.1.0"}],"id":"week4-ocr-question-practice","metadata":{"activityType":"Exam skills","href":null,"runtimeGlobal":"Week4OcrPractice","status":"available","summary":"OCR-Style Question Practice","title":"OCR-Style Question Practice"},"relationships":{"assets":[],"assignment":"formative-practice","learningOutcomes":["LO1"],"questions":[]},"schema":"lp.content.activity","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","version":"1.0.0"},{"blocks":[{"content":{"level":2,"text":"Marking and Answer Improvement"},"id":"week4-answer-improvement-title","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"heading","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"format":"application/json","text":"```json\n{\n  \"weekNumber\": 4,\n  \"sessionNumber\": 2,\n  \"commonError\": \"A list of separate facts about motivation and target with no sentence connecting them.\",\n  \"question\": {\n    \"marks\": 8,\n    \"commandWord\": \"Analyse\",\n    \"prompt\": \"Northbank clinic booking systems are encrypted and a cryptocurrency payment is demanded. No political message is published. Analyse why this organisation was targeted, connecting motivation, target and method with evidence from the scenario.\"\n  },\n  \"markSchemePoints\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"motivation\",\n      \"label\": \"A valid motivation was named\",\n      \"marks\": 1\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"target\",\n      \"label\": \"The target was identified\",\n      \"marks\": 1\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"method\",\n      \"label\": \"The method was identified\",\n      \"marks\": 1\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"evidence\",\n      \"label\": \"Evidence from the scenario was used\",\n      \"marks\": 1\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"connection\",\n      \"label\": \"A connection was made between motivation, target and method\",\n      \"marks\": 2\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"final\",\n      \"label\": \"The final connection was explicit rather than implied\",\n      \"marks\": 1\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"sustained\",\n      \"label\": \"The response sustained one case (did not switch examples)\",\n      \"marks\": 1\n    }\n  ],\n  \"sampleResponse\": {\n    \"id\": \"sample-weak\",\n    \"label\": \"Sample extended response to mark\",\n    \"text\": \"The motivation could be income generation. The target could be organisations. The method could be system compromise. Booking systems were encrypted. A payment was demanded. Large hospitals are also attacked sometimes. Phishing might be involved.\"\n  },\n  \"dominantIssues\": [\n    \"Motivation, target and method are listed separately with no connecting sentence.\",\n    \"The final connection remains implied.\",\n    \"The response switches towards large hospitals and phishing, leaving the main case incomplete.\"\n  ],\n  \"modelImprovedSentence\": \"Income generation is the most likely motivation because a cryptocurrency payment is demanded without a political message, which means that Northbank\u2019s organisational booking systems were a logical target for system compromise so that recovery pressure would support payment.\",\n  \"modelResponse\": \"Income generation is the most likely motivation because a cryptocurrency payment is demanded and no political message is published. As a result, Northbank\u2019s organisational booking systems were a logical target. Therefore system compromise that encrypts those systems suits the motivation by creating pressure to pay, completing the connection between why, what and how without switching to a different example.\",\n  \"rewritePrompt\": \"Rewrite one descriptive sentence from the sample as an analytical sentence using a meaningful connective (because / which means that / as a result / therefore).\",\n  \"improvementActionPrompt\": \"Record one specific improvement action for your next analyse response.\"\n}\n```"},"id":"week4-answer-improvement-source-remainder","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"markdown","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"formative":true,"prompt":"Complete this activity on the learner hub page, then write a short note to confirm you have finished.","questionId":"week4-answer-improvement:learner-note","sourceQuestionId":"learner-note"},"id":"week4-answer-improvement-learner-note","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"reflection","version":"0.1.0"}],"id":"week4-answer-improvement","metadata":{"activityType":"Self marking","href":null,"runtimeGlobal":"Week4AnswerImprovement","status":"available","summary":"Marking and Answer Improvement","title":"Marking and Answer Improvement"},"relationships":{"assets":[],"assignment":"formative-practice","learningOutcomes":["LO1"],"questions":[]},"schema":"lp.content.activity","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","version":"1.0.0"},{"blocks":[{"content":{"level":2,"text":"Ethical Review Discussion"},"id":"week4-ethical-review-title","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"heading","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"format":"application/json","text":"```json\n{\n  \"weekNumber\": 4,\n  \"sessionNumber\": 2,\n  \"prompt\": \"Can an attack claimed to serve the public good be justified?\",\n  \"requirements\": [\n    \"Take a clear position (yes, no, or a carefully qualified view).\",\n    \"Support the position with a reason rather than an assertion.\",\n    \"Recognise that a claimed motivation does not change the legal position of the act.\"\n  ],\n  \"boundaries\": [\n    \"This is an ethical-review discussion for Week 4.\",\n    \"Do not expand into detailed legislation content from later weeks.\",\n    \"Do not introduce detailed statutes or legal requirements here.\"\n  ],\n  \"sentenceStarters\": [\n    \"I argue that \u2026 because \u2026\",\n    \"Even if the claimed motivation is public good, \u2026\",\n    \"A claimed motivation does not change the legal position because \u2026\"\n  ]\n}\n```"},"id":"week4-ethical-review-source-remainder","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"markdown","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"formative":true,"prompt":"Complete this activity on the learner hub page, then write a short note to confirm you have finished.","questionId":"week4-ethical-review:learner-note","sourceQuestionId":"learner-note"},"id":"week4-ethical-review-learner-note","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"reflection","version":"0.1.0"}],"id":"week4-ethical-review","metadata":{"activityType":"Discussion","href":null,"runtimeGlobal":"Week4EthicalReview","status":"available","summary":"Ethical Review Discussion","title":"Ethical Review Discussion"},"relationships":{"assets":[],"assignment":"formative-practice","learningOutcomes":["LO1"],"questions":[]},"schema":"lp.content.activity","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","version":"1.0.0"},{"blocks":[{"content":{"level":2,"text":"Session 1 Retrieval and Homework Harvest"},"id":"week5-session1-retrieval-title","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"heading","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"correctOptionId":"b","feedback":{"correct":"Week 5 moves from cause and motivation to consequence: loss, disruption and safety impacts.","incorrect":"Week 5 moves from cause and motivation to consequence: loss, disruption and safety impacts."},"formative":true,"options":[{"id":"a","label":"Risk scoring formulae"},{"id":"b","label":"The consequences and impacts of cyber security incidents"},{"id":"c","label":"Incident-response stage ordering"},{"id":"d","label":"Choosing security controls for LO4"}],"prompt":"Week 4 focused mainly on why attackers act and what they target. Week 5 focuses on:","questionId":"week5-session1-retrieval:s1q1","sourceQuestionId":"s1q1","sourceType":"single"},"id":"week5-session1-retrieval-q-1-s1q1","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"single-choice","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"correctOptionId":"b","feedback":{"correct":"Income generation is a motivation (why). The other options describe consequences for services or stakeholders.","incorrect":"Income generation is a motivation (why). The other options describe consequences for services or stakeholders."},"formative":true,"options":[{"id":"a","label":"Patients cannot book appointments for two days"},{"id":"b","label":"Income generation through ransom demands"},{"id":"c","label":"Northbank\u2019s reputation is damaged for months"},{"id":"d","label":"A traffic-control system becomes unreliable"}],"prompt":"Which statement best describes a motivation rather than an impact?","questionId":"week5-session1-retrieval:s1q2","sourceQuestionId":"s1q2","sourceType":"single"},"id":"week5-session1-retrieval-q-2-s1q2","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"single-choice","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"correctOptionId":"b","feedback":{"correct":"Learners must cover loss, disruption and safety \u2014 not treat every impact as financial loss alone.","incorrect":"Learners must cover loss, disruption and safety \u2014 not treat every impact as financial loss alone."},"formative":true,"options":[{"id":"a","label":"Confidentiality, integrity and availability only"},{"id":"b","label":"Loss, disruption and safety"},{"id":"c","label":"Prevention, detection and recovery"},{"id":"d","label":"People, organisations and equipment"}],"prompt":"OCR teaching content 2.5 groups impacts under which three broad categories?","questionId":"week5-session1-retrieval:s1q3","sourceQuestionId":"s1q3","sourceType":"single"},"id":"week5-session1-retrieval-q-3-s1q3","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"single-choice","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"correctOptionId":"b","feedback":{"correct":"One incident can create several impacts, and different stakeholders experience the same incident differently.","incorrect":"One incident can create several impacts, and different stakeholders experience the same incident differently."},"formative":true,"options":[{"id":"a","label":"Create only one financial impact"},{"id":"b","label":"Create several different impacts for different stakeholders"},{"id":"c","label":"Affect only the IT support contractor"},{"id":"d","label":"Have consequences that end as soon as systems restart"}],"prompt":"A single ransomware incident at Northbank is most likely to:","questionId":"week5-session1-retrieval:s1q4","sourceQuestionId":"s1q4","sourceType":"single"},"id":"week5-session1-retrieval-q-4-s1q4","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"single-choice","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"correctOptionId":"c","feedback":{"correct":"Reputational damage and loss of customer confidence may continue after immediate financial costs are addressed and can be hard to quantify.","incorrect":"Reputational damage and loss of customer confidence may continue after immediate financial costs are addressed and can be hard to quantify."},"formative":true,"options":[{"id":"a","label":"Paying an emergency IT call-out fee"},{"id":"b","label":"Buying replacement hard drives"},{"id":"c","label":"Loss of customer confidence over several months"},{"id":"d","label":"Hiring temporary reception cover for one afternoon"}],"prompt":"Which consequence is typically harder to quantify than an immediate recovery invoice?","questionId":"week5-session1-retrieval:s1q5","sourceQuestionId":"s1q5","sourceType":"single"},"id":"week5-session1-retrieval-q-5-s1q5","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"single-choice","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"correctOptionId":"c","feedback":{"correct":"Examination answers should use evidence from the scenario provided, not invent or import unrelated incident facts.","incorrect":"Examination answers should use evidence from the scenario provided, not invent or import unrelated incident facts."},"formative":true,"options":[{"id":"a","label":"So answers can ignore the organisation named in the question"},{"id":"b","label":"So learners can import facts from famous unrelated breaches"},{"id":"c","label":"So each claimed impact can be justified from the given case"},{"id":"d","label":"So only financial loss needs to be mentioned"}],"prompt":"Why must impact claims be supported by scenario evidence?","questionId":"week5-session1-retrieval:s1q6","sourceQuestionId":"s1q6","sourceType":"single"},"id":"week5-session1-retrieval-q-6-s1q6","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"single-choice","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"correctOptionId":"b","feedback":{"correct":"The same event can be disruption for the healthcare organisation and also create a safety impact for the patient, depending on the stakeholder considered.","incorrect":"The same event can be disruption for the healthcare organisation and also create a safety impact for the patient, depending on the stakeholder considered."},"formative":true,"options":[{"id":"a","label":"Only a financial loss for the patient"},{"id":"b","label":"Disruption for the organisation and potentially a safety impact for the patient"},{"id":"c","label":"Only a safety impact for the regulator"},{"id":"d","label":"Neither disruption nor safety"}],"prompt":"Cancelling a healthcare appointment after systems fail may be:","questionId":"week5-session1-retrieval:s1q7","sourceQuestionId":"s1q7","sourceType":"single"},"id":"week5-session1-retrieval-q-7-s1q7","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"single-choice","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"correctOptionId":"b","feedback":{"correct":"Week 5 establishes that cyber security incidents can affect individuals, organisations and states.","incorrect":"Week 5 establishes that cyber security incidents can affect individuals, organisations and states."},"formative":true,"options":[{"id":"a","label":"Only large banks"},{"id":"b","label":"Individuals, organisations and states"},{"id":"c","label":"Only healthcare partnerships"},{"id":"d","label":"Only reputational loss"}],"prompt":"Cyber security is treated as a global problem because incidents can affect:","questionId":"week5-session1-retrieval:s1q8","sourceQuestionId":"s1q8","sourceType":"single"},"id":"week5-session1-retrieval-q-8-s1q8","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"single-choice","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"format":"application/json","text":"```json\n{\n  \"weekNumber\": 5,\n  \"sessionNumber\": 1,\n  \"estimatedMinutes\": 15,\n  \"homeworkReminder\": \"Submit your Week 4 case study analysis if you have not already done so. Use the method your tutor has set \u2014 this hub does not provide a new file-upload system.\",\n  \"harvestPrompts\": {\n    \"intro\": \"Think of one cyber security incident you have studied (for example from Week 4). Move from cause and motivation to consequence.\",\n    \"fields\": [\n      {\n        \"id\": \"whoHarmed\",\n        \"label\": \"Who was harmed?\",\n        \"required\": true\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"whatLost\",\n        \"label\": \"What did each party lose?\",\n        \"required\": true\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"timescale\",\n        \"label\": \"Was the harm immediate or longer term? Explain briefly.\",\n        \"required\": true\n      }\n    ]\n  }\n}\n```"},"id":"week5-session1-retrieval-source-remainder","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"markdown","version":"0.1.0"}],"id":"week5-session1-retrieval","metadata":{"activityType":"Retrieval quiz","href":null,"runtimeGlobal":"Week5Session1Retrieval","status":"available","summary":"Session 1 Retrieval and Homework Harvest","title":"Session 1 Retrieval and Homework Harvest"},"relationships":{"assets":[],"assignment":"formative-practice","learningOutcomes":["LO1"],"questions":[]},"schema":"lp.content.activity","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","version":"1.0.0"},{"blocks":[{"content":{"level":2,"text":"Impacts Learning: Loss, Disruption and Safety"},"id":"week5-impacts-learning-title","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"heading","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"correctOptionId":"b","feedback":{"correct":"Unavailable clinic booking is disruption of a depended-on service. Overtime is financial loss; income generation is motivation.","incorrect":"Unavailable clinic booking is disruption of a depended-on service. Overtime is financial loss; income generation is motivation."},"formative":true,"options":[{"id":"a","label":"Northbank paid \u00a32,000 in overtime"},{"id":"b","label":"Clinic booking services were unavailable for two working days"},{"id":"c","label":"An attacker wanted income generation"},{"id":"d","label":"A student copied a mark scheme"}],"prompt":"Which option is a disruption impact rather than a pure financial-loss statement?","questionId":"week5-impacts-learning:k1","sourceQuestionId":"k1","sourceType":"single"},"id":"week5-impacts-learning-q-1-k1","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"single-choice","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"correctOptionId":"b","feedback":{"correct":"Delayed time-critical care places a person at physical risk \u2014 a safety impact supported by the scenario.","incorrect":"Delayed time-critical care places a person at physical risk \u2014 a safety impact supported by the scenario."},"formative":true,"options":[{"id":"a","label":"Northbank\u2019s logo looks outdated on the website"},{"id":"b","label":"A patient misses a time-critical review because records and booking systems are down"},{"id":"c","label":"A supplier invoice is emailed a day late"},{"id":"d","label":"Staff discuss the incident in a team meeting"}],"prompt":"Which statement best shows a safety impact?","questionId":"week5-impacts-learning:k2","sourceQuestionId":"k2","sourceType":"single"},"id":"week5-impacts-learning-q-2-k2","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"single-choice","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"correctOptionId":"b","feedback":{"correct":"A cancelled appointment may be disruption for the organisation and safety for the patient. Categories can combine when justified.","incorrect":"A cancelled appointment may be disruption for the organisation and safety for the patient. Categories can combine when justified."},"formative":true,"options":[{"id":"a","label":"Always mutually exclusive labels"},{"id":"b","label":"Categories that can overlap when a scenario supports more than one"},{"id":"c","label":"Only used for state-level incidents"},{"id":"d","label":"Replacements for naming stakeholders"}],"prompt":"Loss, disruption and safety are:","questionId":"week5-impacts-learning:k3","sourceQuestionId":"k3","sourceType":"single"},"id":"week5-impacts-learning-q-3-k3","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"single-choice","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"correctOptionId":"b","feedback":{"correct":"Reputation and confidence harms may continue for months after immediate financial costs are addressed.","incorrect":"Reputation and confidence harms may continue for months after immediate financial costs are addressed."},"formative":true,"options":[{"id":"a","label":"Emergency call-out fee and same-day taxi receipt"},{"id":"b","label":"Reputational loss and loss of customer confidence"},{"id":"c","label":"A one-hour reboot delay only"},{"id":"d","label":"A single printed leaflet cost"}],"prompt":"Which pair is most likely to continue after immediate recovery spending?","questionId":"week5-impacts-learning:k4","sourceQuestionId":"k4","sourceType":"single"},"id":"week5-impacts-learning-q-4-k4","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"single-choice","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"correctOptionId":"b","feedback":{"correct":"Identity theft is an individual loss impact, even when an organisation was the breached party.","incorrect":"Identity theft is an individual loss impact, even when an organisation was the breached party."},"formative":true,"options":[{"id":"a","label":"Only the broadcasting regulator"},{"id":"b","label":"Individuals whose personal details are misused"},{"id":"c","label":"Only oil installations"},{"id":"d","label":"Nobody if backups exist"}],"prompt":"Identity theft after a healthcare breach primarily harms:","questionId":"week5-impacts-learning:k5","sourceQuestionId":"k5","sourceType":"single"},"id":"week5-impacts-learning-q-5-k5","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"single-choice","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"correctOptionId":"b","feedback":{"correct":"Week 5 teaching asks which service stopped or became unreliable, who depended on it, and how they were affected.","incorrect":"Week 5 teaching asks which service stopped or became unreliable, who depended on it, and how they were affected."},"formative":true,"options":[{"id":"a","label":"A famous unrelated breach from the news"},{"id":"b","label":"Which service stopped, who depended on it, and how they were affected"},{"id":"c","label":"The LO4 incident-response stage name"},{"id":"d","label":"A risk score from Week 7"}],"prompt":"When classifying an impact you should first identify:","questionId":"week5-impacts-learning:k6","sourceQuestionId":"k6","sourceType":"single"},"id":"week5-impacts-learning-q-6-k6","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"single-choice","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"correctOptionId":"b","feedback":{"correct":"Transport and traffic-control contexts show disruption and can raise safety issues when people are placed at physical risk.","incorrect":"Transport and traffic-control contexts show disruption and can raise safety issues when people are placed at physical risk."},"formative":true,"options":[{"id":"a","label":"Only financial loss for advertisers"},{"id":"b","label":"Disruption of a depended-on service and possible safety consequences"},{"id":"c","label":"Motivation taxonomy from Week 4"},{"id":"d","label":"Legislation from Week 6"}],"prompt":"Traffic-control interference is included in Week 5 mainly to illustrate:","questionId":"week5-impacts-learning:k7","sourceQuestionId":"k7","sourceType":"single"},"id":"week5-impacts-learning-q-7-k7","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"single-choice","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"correctOptionId":"b","feedback":{"correct":"Analysis needs a named stakeholder, a specific consequence, evidence from the scenario and clear timescale thinking.","incorrect":"Analysis needs a named stakeholder, a specific consequence, evidence from the scenario and clear timescale thinking."},"formative":true,"options":[{"id":"a","label":"Only a list of malware names"},{"id":"b","label":"Named stakeholder, consequence, scenario evidence and timescale where relevant"},{"id":"c","label":"Invented controls not present in the briefing"},{"id":"d","label":"Official OCR examination paper numbers"}],"prompt":"A strong impact answer for Northbank should usually include:","questionId":"week5-impacts-learning:k8","sourceQuestionId":"k8","sourceType":"single"},"id":"week5-impacts-learning-q-8-k8","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"single-choice","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"correctOptionId":"b","feedback":{"correct":"Name who is affected and what happened. Vague organisational suffering without stakeholder or evidence earns limited credit.","incorrect":"Name who is affected and what happened. Vague organisational suffering without stakeholder or evidence earns limited credit."},"formative":true,"options":[{"id":"a","label":"Because organisations never suffer impacts"},{"id":"b","label":"Because it fails to name the stakeholder and the specific consequence"},{"id":"c","label":"Because only states can be named"},{"id":"d","label":"Because financial loss is forbidden"}],"prompt":"Why is \u201cthe organisation suffered\u201d a weak examination phrase on its own?","questionId":"week5-impacts-learning:k9","sourceQuestionId":"k9","sourceType":"single"},"id":"week5-impacts-learning-q-9-k9","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"single-choice","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"format":"application/json","text":"```json\n{\n  \"weekNumber\": 5,\n  \"sessionNumber\": 1,\n  \"estimatedMinutes\": 35,\n  \"overviewNote\": \"Do not treat every cyber security impact as financial loss. A single incident can create loss, disruption and safety consequences together. Categories are not always mutually exclusive.\",\n  \"definitions\": {\n    \"loss\": \"Something of value is taken, damaged, corrupted, reduced or no longer trusted \u2014 including data, money, identity, reputation or confidence.\",\n    \"disruption\": \"A service, process or operation stops, slows or becomes unreliable for people who depend on it.\",\n    \"safety\": \"People are placed at physical risk, or physical harm becomes more likely, because of the cyber incident or its consequences.\"\n  },\n  \"lossForms\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"confidentiality\",\n      \"term\": \"Loss of confidentiality\",\n      \"explanation\": \"Information that should be restricted becomes known to unauthorised people.\",\n      \"example\": \"Northbank patient contact details from a shared mailbox are emailed to the wrong external address.\",\n      \"distinction\": \"Different from integrity loss: the data may still be accurate, but the wrong people can see it.\",\n      \"check\": {\n        \"prompt\": \"A staff member posts a screenshot of a patient booking list in a public group chat. Which loss is clearest?\",\n        \"options\": [\n          \"Loss of confidentiality\",\n          \"Loss of availability\",\n          \"Safety only\",\n          \"No impact\"\n        ],\n        \"correctIndex\": 0,\n        \"explanation\": \"Restricted patient information has been exposed. That is loss of confidentiality even if systems still work.\"\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"integrity\",\n      \"term\": \"Loss of integrity\",\n      \"explanation\": \"Information is altered so it is no longer accurate or trustworthy.\",\n      \"example\": \"Ransomware encrypts Northbank appointment records so staff cannot trust which visits remain scheduled.\",\n      \"distinction\": \"Different from confidentiality: the issue is trustworthiness of the data, not only who can see it.\",\n      \"check\": {\n        \"prompt\": \"An attacker changes dosage fields in a shared prescribing note template used by Northbank. This is primarily:\",\n        \"options\": [\n          \"Loss of integrity\",\n          \"Loss of business only\",\n          \"Disruption of broadcasting\",\n          \"Identity theft only\"\n        ],\n        \"correctIndex\": 0,\n        \"explanation\": \"Altering clinical information so it is no longer trustworthy is loss of integrity. It may also raise safety concerns later, but integrity is the direct data impact.\"\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"availability\",\n      \"term\": \"Loss of availability\",\n      \"explanation\": \"Systems, data or services cannot be used when needed.\",\n      \"example\": \"Northbank\u2019s booking system is offline after encryption, so staff cannot open today\u2019s clinic list.\",\n      \"distinction\": \"Closely linked to disruption of services, but availability focuses on whether the asset can be used.\",\n      \"check\": {\n        \"prompt\": \"Staff cannot open the encrypted shared drive containing clinic rotas. The clearest CIA-related loss is:\",\n        \"options\": [\n          \"Loss of availability\",\n          \"Identity theft\",\n          \"Loss of customer confidence only\",\n          \"Reputational loss only\"\n        ],\n        \"correctIndex\": 0,\n        \"explanation\": \"The information exists but cannot be used when needed \u2014 loss of availability.\"\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"data\",\n      \"term\": \"Loss of data\",\n      \"explanation\": \"Data is destroyed, permanently inaccessible, or no longer recoverable in a usable form.\",\n      \"example\": \"Northbank cannot restore last week\u2019s referral letters after backups fail during a ransomware event.\",\n      \"distinction\": \"Wider than confidentiality: the organisation may no longer have the data at all.\",\n      \"check\": {\n        \"prompt\": \"Which statement best illustrates loss of data rather than temporary unavailability?\",\n        \"options\": [\n          \"The system is down for ten minutes during a reboot\",\n          \"Backups fail and referral letters cannot be restored\",\n          \"A patient is late for an appointment\",\n          \"A supplier invoice is paid on time\"\n        ],\n        \"correctIndex\": 1,\n        \"explanation\": \"If information cannot be restored, the organisation has lost data, not merely waited for a short outage.\"\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"financial\",\n      \"term\": \"Financial loss\",\n      \"explanation\": \"Money is spent, stolen or otherwise lost because of the incident.\",\n      \"example\": \"Northbank pays emergency IT contractor fees and overtime to recover encrypted booking systems.\",\n      \"distinction\": \"Important, but not the only impact. Do not stop at money when a question asks for impacts.\",\n      \"check\": {\n        \"prompt\": \"Paying overtime and recovery fees after ransomware is best described as:\",\n        \"options\": [\n          \"Financial loss\",\n          \"Safety impact only\",\n          \"Motivation for attack\",\n          \"No organisational impact\"\n        ],\n        \"correctIndex\": 0,\n        \"explanation\": \"Direct extra spending is financial loss. Strong answers also consider disruption and safety where relevant.\"\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"business\",\n      \"term\": \"Loss of business\",\n      \"explanation\": \"Customers, patients or partners take their activity elsewhere, reducing future work or service use.\",\n      \"example\": \"Local residents choose another clinic for routine bookings after repeated Northbank outages.\",\n      \"distinction\": \"Related to, but not identical with, loss of customer confidence \u2014 business loss is the reduced activity itself.\",\n      \"check\": {\n        \"prompt\": \"Patients start booking elsewhere after repeated Northbank outages. This illustrates:\",\n        \"options\": [\n          \"Loss of business\",\n          \"Loss of confidentiality only\",\n          \"A transport-network impact\",\n          \"An oil-installation safety case\"\n        ],\n        \"correctIndex\": 0,\n        \"explanation\": \"Activity moving away from the organisation is loss of business.\"\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"identity\",\n      \"term\": \"Identity loss or identity theft\",\n      \"explanation\": \"Personal identifying information is misused so someone can pretend to be another person or take over their accounts.\",\n      \"example\": \"Stolen Northbank patient identity details are used to open fraudulent accounts in a patient\u2019s name.\",\n      \"distinction\": \"A form of loss for the individual; it may also create longer-term financial and confidence harms.\",\n      \"check\": {\n        \"prompt\": \"Stolen patient details are used to open fraudulent accounts. Which impact fits best?\",\n        \"options\": [\n          \"Identity theft / identity loss\",\n          \"Broadcasting disruption\",\n          \"Utilities disruption only\",\n          \"No individual impact\"\n        ],\n        \"correctIndex\": 0,\n        \"explanation\": \"Misuse of personal identity information is identity theft / identity loss for the individual.\"\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"reputation\",\n      \"term\": \"Reputational loss\",\n      \"explanation\": \"Trust in the organisation\u2019s competence or trustworthiness is damaged in public or professional opinion.\",\n      \"example\": \"Local news reports that Northbank cancelled clinics after ransomware, and GPs hesitate to refer patients.\",\n      \"distinction\": \"May continue after immediate financial recovery costs are paid.\",\n      \"check\": {\n        \"prompt\": \"Why might reputational loss still matter after recovery fees are paid?\",\n        \"options\": [\n          \"Because reputation always equals insurance payouts\",\n          \"Because damaged trust can continue for months and affect future use of the service\",\n          \"Because reputation is never an OCR impact\",\n          \"Because only states experience reputational loss\"\n        ],\n        \"correctIndex\": 1,\n        \"explanation\": \"Reputational loss can continue after immediate financial costs are addressed and remains important even when hard to quantify.\"\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"confidence\",\n      \"term\": \"Loss of customer confidence\",\n      \"explanation\": \"Patients, customers or partners become less willing to trust the organisation with their care, data or business.\",\n      \"example\": \"Patients ask reception whether Northbank can keep medical information safe after a publicised breach.\",\n      \"distinction\": \"Closely linked to reputational loss; confidence focuses on the stakeholder\u2019s willingness to trust and continue using the service.\",\n      \"check\": {\n        \"prompt\": \"Patients repeatedly ask whether Northbank can keep records safe after an incident. This best shows:\",\n        \"options\": [\n          \"Loss of customer confidence\",\n          \"Loss of availability of a traffic system\",\n          \"A state-level utilities outage\",\n          \"No longer-term consequence\"\n        ],\n        \"correctIndex\": 0,\n        \"explanation\": \"Reduced willingness to trust the organisation is loss of customer confidence and may continue after immediate recovery.\"\n      }\n    }\n  ],\n  \"disruptionContexts\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"healthcare\",\n      \"context\": \"Healthcare services / hospitals\",\n      \"explanation\": \"Clinical or administrative services stop or become unreliable for patients and staff who depend on them.\",\n      \"example\": \"Northbank cannot run booked clinics while systems are offline, so appointments are cancelled.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"transport\",\n      \"context\": \"Transport networks\",\n      \"explanation\": \"Travel services become delayed, cancelled or unsafe to rely on.\",\n      \"example\": \"A ransomware incident on a regional booking platform leaves passengers unable to confirm journeys.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"broadcasting\",\n      \"context\": \"Broadcasting\",\n      \"explanation\": \"Media or public-information services cannot transmit as planned.\",\n      \"example\": \"A broadcaster cannot air scheduled public-service announcements during an outage.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"utilities\",\n      \"context\": \"Utilities\",\n      \"explanation\": \"Essential utility services become unreliable for households or organisations.\",\n      \"example\": \"A cyber incident interrupts monitoring for a local utility, affecting service continuity.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"oil\",\n      \"context\": \"Oil installations\",\n      \"explanation\": \"Industrial operations are interrupted, with possible wider supply and safety consequences.\",\n      \"example\": \"Control systems at an oil installation are taken offline, stopping normal operations.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"traffic\",\n      \"context\": \"Traffic-control interference\",\n      \"explanation\": \"Traffic management becomes unreliable, affecting road users who depend on signals or control systems.\",\n      \"example\": \"Interference with traffic-control systems causes unpredictable signal behaviour on major routes.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"safetyTeaching\": \"A cyber security incident can cause physical harm or place people at physical risk. Safety is not optional content when the scenario supports it.\",\n  \"safetyExamples\": [\n    \"A cancelled urgent healthcare appointment leaves a patient without timely clinical review.\",\n    \"Traffic-control interference increases the chance of collisions.\",\n    \"Disrupted hospital systems delay access to care records needed for treatment decisions.\"\n  ]\n}\n```"},"id":"week5-impacts-learning-source-remainder","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"markdown","version":"0.1.0"}],"id":"week5-impacts-learning","metadata":{"activityType":"Guided learning","href":null,"runtimeGlobal":"Week5ImpactsLearning","status":"available","summary":"Impacts Learning: Loss, Disruption and Safety","title":"Impacts Learning: Loss, Disruption and Safety"},"relationships":{"assets":[],"assignment":"formative-practice","learningOutcomes":["LO1"],"questions":[]},"schema":"lp.content.activity","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","version":"1.0.0"},{"blocks":[{"content":{"level":2,"text":"Loss, Disruption and Safety Classification"},"id":"week5-impact-classification-title","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"heading","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"format":"application/json","text":"```json\n{\n  \"weekNumber\": 5,\n  \"sessionNumber\": 1,\n  \"estimatedMinutes\": 25,\n  \"categories\": [\n    \"Loss\",\n    \"Disruption\",\n    \"Safety\",\n    \"More than one category\"\n  ],\n  \"instructions\": [\n    \"Classify each short impact statement.\",\n    \"Choose More than one category where a justified combination fits.\",\n    \"For ambiguous examples, write a short reason naming the stakeholder perspective you used.\",\n    \"Categories are not always mutually exclusive.\"\n  ],\n  \"checklist\": [\n    \"Have I considered loss?\",\n    \"Have I considered disruption?\",\n    \"Have I considered safety?\",\n    \"Have I named whose perspective I am using?\"\n  ],\n  \"items\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"c1\",\n      \"statement\": \"Northbank pays emergency contractor fees to rebuild encrypted servers.\",\n      \"accepted\": [\n        \"Loss\"\n      ],\n      \"ambiguous\": false,\n      \"feedback\": \"Direct extra spending is financial loss. It does not, by itself, describe a stopped service or physical risk.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"c2\",\n      \"statement\": \"Clinic booking services are unavailable for two working days, so reception cannot confirm visits.\",\n      \"accepted\": [\n        \"Disruption\",\n        \"More than one category\"\n      ],\n      \"ambiguous\": true,\n      \"reasonRequired\": true,\n      \"feedback\": \"This is clearly disruption of a depended-on service. Some learners may also argue loss of availability; if you chose more than one category, your reason should identify the service and who depended on it.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"c3\",\n      \"statement\": \"A patient\u2019s urgent review is cancelled because Northbank cannot access records; the delay increases clinical risk for that patient.\",\n      \"accepted\": [\n        \"Safety\",\n        \"More than one category\"\n      ],\n      \"ambiguous\": true,\n      \"reasonRequired\": true,\n      \"feedback\": \"Physical or clinical risk to the patient is a safety impact. It may also be disruption for the organisation. More than one category is defensible when both perspectives are explained.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"c4\",\n      \"statement\": \"Stolen patient identity details are later used to open fraudulent accounts.\",\n      \"accepted\": [\n        \"Loss\"\n      ],\n      \"ambiguous\": false,\n      \"feedback\": \"Identity theft is a loss impact for the individual. Focus on what the person lost or had misused.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"c5\",\n      \"statement\": \"Local news coverage leaves patients unsure whether Northbank can be trusted with medical information for months afterwards.\",\n      \"accepted\": [\n        \"Loss\"\n      ],\n      \"ambiguous\": false,\n      \"feedback\": \"This is reputational loss / loss of customer confidence. It may be hard to quantify but remains an important longer-term loss impact.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"c6\",\n      \"statement\": \"Interference with a traffic-control system causes unpredictable signal behaviour on major routes used by ambulances.\",\n      \"accepted\": [\n        \"Disruption\",\n        \"Safety\",\n        \"More than one category\"\n      ],\n      \"ambiguous\": true,\n      \"reasonRequired\": true,\n      \"feedback\": \"The service becomes unreliable (disruption) and people may be placed at physical risk (safety). More than one category is often the strongest justified choice.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"c7\",\n      \"statement\": \"A healthcare appointment is cancelled after systems fail.\",\n      \"accepted\": [\n        \"Disruption\",\n        \"Safety\",\n        \"More than one category\"\n      ],\n      \"ambiguous\": true,\n      \"reasonRequired\": true,\n      \"teachingFocus\": true,\n      \"feedback\": \"Weekly-plan example: cancellation may be disruption for the healthcare organisation and may also create a safety impact for the patient. The defensible answer depends on the stakeholder considered \u2014 explain your reasoning.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"c8\",\n      \"statement\": \"An oil installation\u2019s control systems are taken offline and normal operations stop.\",\n      \"accepted\": [\n        \"Disruption\",\n        \"More than one category\"\n      ],\n      \"ambiguous\": true,\n      \"reasonRequired\": true,\n      \"feedback\": \"Stopped operations are disruption. Safety may also be argued if the scenario evidence shows people placed at physical risk; do not invent hazards that are not stated.\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```"},"id":"week5-impact-classification-source-remainder","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"markdown","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"formative":true,"prompt":"Complete this activity on the learner hub page, then write a short note to confirm you have finished.","questionId":"week5-impact-classification:learner-note","sourceQuestionId":"learner-note"},"id":"week5-impact-classification-learner-note","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"reflection","version":"0.1.0"}],"id":"week5-impact-classification","metadata":{"activityType":"Classification","href":null,"runtimeGlobal":"Week5ImpactClassification","status":"available","summary":"Loss, Disruption and Safety Classification","title":"Loss, Disruption and Safety Classification"},"relationships":{"assets":[],"assignment":"formative-practice","learningOutcomes":["LO1"],"questions":[]},"schema":"lp.content.activity","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","version":"1.0.0"},{"blocks":[{"content":{"level":2,"text":"Northbank Ransomware Exercise Companion"},"id":"week5-ransomware-companion-title","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"heading","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"format":"application/json","text":"```json\n{\n  \"weekNumber\": 5,\n  \"sessionNumber\": 1,\n  \"estimatedMinutes\": 40,\n  \"ncsc\": {\n    \"producer\": \"National Cyber Security Centre (NCSC)\",\n    \"productName\": \"Exercise in a Box\",\n    \"purpose\": \"Exercise in a Box is designed for organisations to test their readiness through structured discussion exercises.\",\n    \"namedExercise\": \"Responding to a ransomware attack\",\n    \"overviewUrl\": \"https://www.ncsc.gov.uk/section/exercise-in-a-box/overview\",\n    \"exerciseUrl\": \"https://www.ncsc.gov.uk/section/exercise-in-a-box/responding-ransomware-attack\",\n    \"classroomRules\": [\n      \"The class will role-play Northbank Community Health Partnership.\",\n      \"Answer from your allocated organisational role, not from personal opinion alone.\",\n      \"Base decisions on the Northbank briefing and established posture.\",\n      \"Do not invent controls, staff, systems or capabilities that are not present in the briefing.\",\n      \"Staged exercise prompts remain on the official NCSC materials and are tutor-facilitated.\",\n      \"This hub is a companion workspace before, during and after the facilitated exercise \u2014 it does not replace the NCSC exercise content.\"\n    ]\n  },\n  \"roles\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"practice-manager\",\n      \"title\": \"Practice manager\",\n      \"responsibility\": \"Overall service continuity and prioritisation for Northbank Community Health Partnership, including decisions that affect clinics, patients and staff working arrangements.\",\n      \"decisionPrompt\": \"State one decision this role may be responsible for during a ransomware incident (do not invent systems or staff that are not in the Northbank briefing).\",\n      \"prompts\": [\n        \"Which patient-facing services must be prioritised if systems stay down?\",\n        \"Who needs clear instruction first: reception, clinicians or partners?\",\n        \"Which impact are you trying to reduce for patients and for the organisation?\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"it-support\",\n      \"title\": \"IT support contractor\",\n      \"responsibility\": \"Technical containment and recovery advice for Northbank systems within the capabilities described in the briefing \u2014 without inventing advanced tooling that is not present.\",\n      \"decisionPrompt\": \"State one decision this role may be responsible for during a ransomware incident, staying within briefing capabilities.\",\n      \"prompts\": [\n        \"What must be protected first: data integrity, remaining available systems, or recovery paths?\",\n        \"What information do other roles need from you before they decide?\",\n        \"Which loss or disruption impacts could worsen if systems are brought back too quickly?\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"records-officer\",\n      \"title\": \"Records officer\",\n      \"responsibility\": \"Care and confidentiality of patient and organisational records, including what can still be accessed, shared or trusted during the incident.\",\n      \"decisionPrompt\": \"State one decision this role may be responsible for during a ransomware incident relating to records or information trust.\",\n      \"prompts\": [\n        \"Which records are needed for safe care today?\",\n        \"How do you prevent further loss of confidentiality while services continue manually?\",\n        \"What evidence would show integrity problems in records?\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"communications-lead\",\n      \"title\": \"Communications lead\",\n      \"responsibility\": \"Internal and external messaging for Northbank so patients, staff and partners receive accurate information without inventing capabilities or making unsupported promises.\",\n      \"decisionPrompt\": \"State one decision this role may be responsible for during a ransomware incident about what is communicated and to whom.\",\n      \"prompts\": [\n        \"Which stakeholders need information first?\",\n        \"How do you reduce reputational loss without claiming facts you do not have?\",\n        \"What message would protect patient safety without creating panic?\"\n      ]\n    }\n  ],\n  \"decisionRecord\": {\n    \"intro\": \"Use this record during the tutor-facilitated exercise. There is no single correct answer bank here \u2014 record reasoned group decisions. Do not invent NCSC prompts.\",\n    \"fields\": [\n      {\n        \"id\": \"decision\",\n        \"label\": \"Decision made\",\n        \"rows\": 3\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"reason\",\n        \"label\": \"Reason for the decision\",\n        \"rows\": 3\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"stakeholder\",\n        \"label\": \"Stakeholder or service being protected\",\n        \"rows\": 2\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"impactReduced\",\n        \"label\": \"Impact the decision is intended to reduce\",\n        \"rows\": 2\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"impactCategory\",\n        \"label\": \"Impact category (loss, disruption, safety, or justified combination)\",\n        \"rows\": 2\n      }\n    ],\n    \"minDecisions\": 2,\n    \"completionNote\": \"Opening the NCSC page alone does not complete this activity. Completion requires role preparation and at least two reasoned decision records, plus confirmation that the facilitated exercise discussion was used.\"\n  },\n  \"impactOptions\": [\n    \"Loss\",\n    \"Disruption\",\n    \"Safety\",\n    \"Loss and disruption\",\n    \"Disruption and safety\",\n    \"Loss and safety\",\n    \"Loss, disruption and safety\"\n  ]\n}\n```"},"id":"week5-ransomware-companion-source-remainder","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"markdown","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"formative":true,"prompt":"Complete this activity on the learner hub page, then write a short note to confirm you have finished.","questionId":"week5-ransomware-companion:learner-note","sourceQuestionId":"learner-note"},"id":"week5-ransomware-companion-learner-note","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"reflection","version":"0.1.0"}],"id":"week5-ransomware-companion","metadata":{"activityType":"Facilitated companion","href":null,"runtimeGlobal":"Week5RansomwareCompanion","status":"available","summary":"Northbank Ransomware Exercise Companion","title":"Northbank Ransomware Exercise Companion"},"relationships":{"assets":[],"assignment":"formative-practice","learningOutcomes":["LO1"],"questions":[]},"schema":"lp.content.activity","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","version":"1.0.0"},{"blocks":[{"content":{"level":2,"text":"Exercise Debrief"},"id":"week5-exercise-debrief-title","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"heading","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"text":"Revisit the decisions recorded in the companion workspace. This debrief is about impacts and stakeholders, not formal incident-response stage teaching."},"id":"week5-exercise-debrief-intro","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"paragraph","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"format":"application/json","text":"```json\n{\n  \"weekNumber\": 5,\n  \"sessionNumber\": 1,\n  \"estimatedMinutes\": 20,\n  \"intro\": \"Revisit the decisions recorded in the companion workspace. This debrief is about impacts and stakeholders, not formal incident-response stage teaching.\",\n  \"globalIssueNote\": \"Cyber security is a global issue affecting individuals, organisations and states. Use your Northbank decisions to show how one incident can reach beyond a single IT team.\",\n  \"prompts\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"impactReduced\",\n      \"label\": \"Which impact was each key decision intended to reduce?\",\n      \"rows\": 4\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"stakeholderBenefit\",\n      \"label\": \"Which stakeholder benefited from each key decision?\",\n      \"rows\": 3\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"timescale\",\n      \"label\": \"Was the intended effect immediate or longer term? Explain for at least one decision.\",\n      \"rows\": 3\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"negativeEffect\",\n      \"label\": \"Could another stakeholder have been negatively affected by the same decision? Explain.\",\n      \"rows\": 3\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"globalLink\",\n      \"label\": \"In two or three sentences, explain how this incident shows cyber security affecting individuals, organisations and states.\",\n      \"rows\": 4\n    }\n  ],\n  \"sentenceStarters\": [\n    \"Immediately after the incident\u2026\",\n    \"This would affect the stakeholder because\u2026\",\n    \"Six months later\u2026\",\n    \"The scenario states that\u2026, which means\u2026\",\n    \"This is a safety impact because\u2026\"\n  ]\n}\n```"},"id":"week5-exercise-debrief-source-remainder","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"markdown","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"formative":true,"prompt":"Complete this activity on the learner hub page, then write a short note to confirm you have finished.","questionId":"week5-exercise-debrief:learner-note","sourceQuestionId":"learner-note"},"id":"week5-exercise-debrief-learner-note","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"reflection","version":"0.1.0"}],"id":"week5-exercise-debrief","metadata":{"activityType":"Reflection","href":null,"runtimeGlobal":"Week5ExerciseDebrief","status":"available","summary":"Exercise Debrief","title":"Exercise Debrief"},"relationships":{"assets":[],"assignment":"formative-practice","learningOutcomes":["LO1"],"questions":[]},"schema":"lp.content.activity","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","version":"1.0.0"},{"blocks":[{"content":{"level":2,"text":"Session 2 Retrieval Quiz"},"id":"week5-session2-retrieval-title","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"heading","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"correctOptionId":"a","feedback":{"correct":"Destroyed or unrecoverable information is a loss of data.","incorrect":"Destroyed or unrecoverable information is a loss of data."},"formative":true,"options":[{"id":"a","label":"Loss"},{"id":"b","label":"Disruption only"},{"id":"c","label":"Safety only"},{"id":"d","label":"Motivation"}],"prompt":"Which impact category best fits unrecovered destruction of referral letters?","questionId":"week5-session2-retrieval:s2q1","sourceQuestionId":"s2q1","sourceType":"single"},"id":"week5-session2-retrieval-q-1-s2q1","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"single-choice","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"correctOptionId":"a","feedback":{"correct":"A depended-on service has become unreliable \u2014 disruption.","incorrect":"A depended-on service has become unreliable \u2014 disruption."},"formative":true,"options":[{"id":"a","label":"Disruption"},{"id":"b","label":"Identity theft"},{"id":"c","label":"A motivation"},{"id":"d","label":"Legislation"}],"prompt":"Reception cannot confirm any clinic visits for two days. This is primarily:","questionId":"week5-session2-retrieval:s2q2","sourceQuestionId":"s2q2","sourceType":"single"},"id":"week5-session2-retrieval-q-2-s2q2","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"single-choice","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"correctOptionId":"a","feedback":{"correct":"Physical or clinical risk to a person is a safety impact.","incorrect":"Physical or clinical risk to a person is a safety impact."},"formative":true,"options":[{"id":"a","label":"Safety"},{"id":"b","label":"Financial loss only"},{"id":"c","label":"Broadcasting disruption"},{"id":"d","label":"Publicity motivation"}],"prompt":"A patient faces increased clinical risk because an urgent review is delayed. This is primarily:","questionId":"week5-session2-retrieval:s2q3","sourceQuestionId":"s2q3","sourceType":"single"},"id":"week5-session2-retrieval-q-3-s2q3","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"single-choice","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"correctOptionId":"b","feedback":{"correct":"Different stakeholders can experience the same incident differently \u2014 individuals, the organisation, employees, patients, suppliers, regulators and the state.","incorrect":"Different stakeholders can experience the same incident differently \u2014 individuals, the organisation, employees, patients, suppliers, regulators and the state."},"formative":true,"options":[{"id":"a","label":"Only the attacker group"},{"id":"b","label":"Patients, employees, suppliers, regulators and the organisation itself, among others"},{"id":"c","label":"Only the college tutor"},{"id":"d","label":"Only oil installations"}],"prompt":"Who is a stakeholder in a Northbank ransomware scenario?","questionId":"week5-session2-retrieval:s2q4","sourceQuestionId":"s2q4","sourceType":"single"},"id":"week5-session2-retrieval-q-4-s2q4","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"single-choice","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"correctOptionId":"b","feedback":{"correct":"Immediate consequences occur at or shortly after the incident.","incorrect":"Immediate consequences occur at or shortly after the incident."},"formative":true,"options":[{"id":"a","label":"Appears only in national legislation"},{"id":"b","label":"Occurs at or shortly after the incident"},{"id":"c","label":"Can never involve safety"},{"id":"d","label":"Is always financial"}],"prompt":"An immediate consequence is best described as one that:","questionId":"week5-session2-retrieval:s2q5","sourceQuestionId":"s2q5","sourceType":"single"},"id":"week5-session2-retrieval-q-5-s2q5","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"single-choice","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"correctOptionId":"b","feedback":{"correct":"Confidence and reputational harms often continue for months and are longer-term consequences.","incorrect":"Confidence and reputational harms often continue for months and are longer-term consequences."},"formative":true,"options":[{"id":"a","label":"An immediate availability outage only"},{"id":"b","label":"A longer-term consequence"},{"id":"c","label":"A Week 6 legal duty"},{"id":"d","label":"An NCSC staged prompt"}],"prompt":"Loss of customer confidence six months later is best described as:","questionId":"week5-session2-retrieval:s2q6","sourceQuestionId":"s2q6","sourceType":"single"},"id":"week5-session2-retrieval-q-6-s2q6","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"single-choice","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"correctOptionId":"b","feedback":{"correct":"Name who was affected and what happened; avoid vague organisational suffering.","incorrect":"Name who was affected and what happened; avoid vague organisational suffering."},"formative":true,"options":[{"id":"a","label":"It names every stakeholder clearly"},{"id":"b","label":"It does not name the stakeholder or the specific impact"},{"id":"c","label":"It covers loss, disruption and safety in detail"},{"id":"d","label":"It uses scenario evidence precisely"}],"prompt":"Awkward example: \u201cNorthbank suffered.\u201d Why is this weak?","questionId":"week5-session2-retrieval:s2q7","sourceQuestionId":"s2q7","sourceType":"single"},"id":"week5-session2-retrieval-q-7-s2q7","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"single-choice","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"correctOptionId":"b","feedback":{"correct":"Listing is not analysis. Connect stakeholder, consequence, evidence and timescale.","incorrect":"Listing is not analysis. Connect stakeholder, consequence, evidence and timescale."},"formative":true,"options":[{"id":"a","label":"Uses too many safety examples"},{"id":"b","label":"Lists impacts without analysis, evidence or stakeholder focus"},{"id":"c","label":"Mentions disruption too often"},{"id":"d","label":"Uses British English"}],"prompt":"Awkward example: listing \u201cmoney, reputation, trust\u201d with no explanation mainly fails because it:","questionId":"week5-session2-retrieval:s2q8","sourceQuestionId":"s2q8","sourceType":"single"},"id":"week5-session2-retrieval-q-8-s2q8","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"single-choice","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"correctOptionId":"b","feedback":{"correct":"Ambiguous cases can have more than one defensible classification when stakeholder perspective is explained.","incorrect":"Ambiguous cases can have more than one defensible classification when stakeholder perspective is explained."},"formative":true,"options":[{"id":"a","label":"Only one classification is ever allowed"},{"id":"b","label":"More than one classification may be defensible depending on the stakeholder"},{"id":"c","label":"Safety never applies in healthcare"},{"id":"d","label":"Financial loss is the only valid lens"}],"prompt":"A cancelled healthcare appointment may be disruption for the organisation and safety for the patient. This shows that:","questionId":"week5-session2-retrieval:s2q9","sourceQuestionId":"s2q9","sourceType":"single"},"id":"week5-session2-retrieval-q-9-s2q9","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"single-choice","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"correctOptionId":"b","feedback":{"correct":"Use scenario evidence about the service that stopped or became unreliable.","incorrect":"Use scenario evidence about the service that stopped or became unreliable."},"formative":true,"options":[{"id":"a","label":"\u201cHospitals somewhere had ransomware once.\u201d"},{"id":"b","label":"\u201cThe booking system could not confirm visits for two working days.\u201d"},{"id":"c","label":"\u201cAttackers like money.\u201d"},{"id":"d","label":"\u201cAll organisations always lose reputation.\u201d"}],"prompt":"Which evidence best supports a disruption claim for Northbank?","questionId":"week5-session2-retrieval:s2q10","sourceQuestionId":"s2q10","sourceType":"single"},"id":"week5-session2-retrieval-q-10-s2q10","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"single-choice","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"correctOptionId":"b","feedback":{"correct":"The same incident affects a patient differently from a regulator \u2014 both perspectives need analysis.","incorrect":"The same incident affects a patient differently from a regulator \u2014 both perspectives need analysis."},"formative":true,"options":[{"id":"a","label":"They experience the incident in the same way as a patient"},{"id":"b","label":"They may face reporting, oversight or assurance consequences that differ from patient impacts"},{"id":"c","label":"They replace the need to discuss safety"},{"id":"d","label":"They are the only stakeholder that matters"}],"prompt":"Regulators are included in the stakeholder grid because:","questionId":"week5-session2-retrieval:s2q11","sourceQuestionId":"s2q11","sourceType":"single"},"id":"week5-session2-retrieval-q-11-s2q11","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"single-choice","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"correctOptionId":"c","feedback":{"correct":"Week 5 learning outcomes require recognition that individuals, organisations and states can all be affected.","incorrect":"Week 5 learning outcomes require recognition that individuals, organisations and states can all be affected."},"formative":true,"options":[{"id":"a","label":"Individuals only"},{"id":"b","label":"Organisations only"},{"id":"c","label":"Individuals, organisations and states"},{"id":"d","label":"Only Northbank Community Health Partnership"}],"prompt":"Cyber security is a global problem affecting:","questionId":"week5-session2-retrieval:s2q12","sourceQuestionId":"s2q12","sourceType":"single"},"id":"week5-session2-retrieval-q-12-s2q12","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"single-choice","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"format":"application/json","text":"```json\n{\n  \"weekNumber\": 5,\n  \"sessionNumber\": 2,\n  \"estimatedMinutes\": 15\n}\n```"},"id":"week5-session2-retrieval-source-remainder","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"markdown","version":"0.1.0"}],"id":"week5-session2-retrieval","metadata":{"activityType":"Retrieval quiz","href":null,"runtimeGlobal":"Week5Session2Retrieval","status":"available","summary":"Session 2 Retrieval Quiz","title":"Session 2 Retrieval Quiz"},"relationships":{"assets":[],"assignment":"formative-practice","learningOutcomes":["LO1"],"questions":[]},"schema":"lp.content.activity","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","version":"1.0.0"},{"blocks":[{"content":{"level":2,"text":"Stakeholder Impact Grid"},"id":"week5-stakeholder-grid-title","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"heading","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"format":"application/json","text":"```json\n{\n  \"weekNumber\": 5,\n  \"sessionNumber\": 2,\n  \"estimatedMinutes\": 35,\n  \"scenario\": \"Ransomware encrypts Northbank Community Health Partnership booking and shared-drive systems. Clinic lists cannot be opened for two working days. Some appointments are cancelled. Patient contact details may have been exposed from a shared mailbox. Emergency recovery spending begins immediately. Local media report the outage. Patients ask whether records are safe. Partner clinics pause some referrals while assurance is sought. Staff work from paper lists where possible.\",\n  \"instructionsVisible\": \"Complete every stakeholder row. Cover loss, disruption and safety \u2014 do not finish by filling only financial loss. Keep these instructions visible while you work.\",\n  \"checklist\": [\n    \"Loss considered for this stakeholder\",\n    \"Disruption considered for this stakeholder\",\n    \"Safety considered for this stakeholder\",\n    \"Scenario evidence recorded\",\n    \"Immediate or longer-term consequence stated\"\n  ],\n  \"columns\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"loss\",\n      \"label\": \"Loss\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"disruption\",\n      \"label\": \"Disruption\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"safety\",\n      \"label\": \"Safety\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"evidence\",\n      \"label\": \"Supporting scenario evidence\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"timescale\",\n      \"label\": \"Immediate or longer-term consequence\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"stakeholders\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"individuals\",\n      \"label\": \"Individuals\",\n      \"workedExample\": true,\n      \"worked\": {\n        \"loss\": \"Exposed contact details create confidentiality loss and possible later identity misuse.\",\n        \"disruption\": \"Cancelled appointments disrupt access to planned care.\",\n        \"safety\": \"Delayed urgent review can increase clinical risk for a patient.\",\n        \"evidence\": \"Scenario: appointments cancelled; patient contact details may have been exposed; booking systems down for two days.\",\n        \"timescale\": \"Immediate: cancelled visits and uncertainty. Longer-term: reduced confidence and possible identity harms.\"\n      }\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"organisation\",\n      \"label\": \"Northbank as the organisation\",\n      \"workedExample\": false\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"employees\",\n      \"label\": \"Employees\",\n      \"workedExample\": false\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"patients\",\n      \"label\": \"Customers or patients\",\n      \"workedExample\": false\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"suppliers\",\n      \"label\": \"Suppliers\",\n      \"workedExample\": false\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"regulators\",\n      \"label\": \"Regulators\",\n      \"workedExample\": false\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"state\",\n      \"label\": \"The state\",\n      \"workedExample\": false\n    }\n  ],\n  \"partlyCompletedSeed\": {\n    \"organisation\": {\n      \"loss\": \"Emergency recovery spending and possible reputational loss.\",\n      \"disruption\": \"\",\n      \"safety\": \"\",\n      \"evidence\": \"Emergency recovery spending begins immediately; local media report the outage.\",\n      \"timescale\": \"Immediate financial recovery cost.\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"reflection\": {\n    \"overlooked\": \"Name two impacts you initially overlooked when you first thought about the incident.\",\n    \"hardest\": \"Which stakeholder did you find hardest to analyse, and why?\",\n    \"compare\": \"Why does the same incident affect a patient differently from a regulator?\"\n  },\n  \"sentenceStarters\": [\n    \"Immediately after the incident\u2026\",\n    \"This would affect the stakeholder because\u2026\",\n    \"Six months later\u2026\",\n    \"The scenario states that\u2026, which means\u2026\",\n    \"This is a safety impact because\u2026\"\n  ]\n}\n```"},"id":"week5-stakeholder-grid-source-remainder","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"markdown","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"formative":true,"prompt":"Complete this activity on the learner hub page, then write a short note to confirm you have finished.","questionId":"week5-stakeholder-grid:learner-note","sourceQuestionId":"learner-note"},"id":"week5-stakeholder-grid-learner-note","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"reflection","version":"0.1.0"}],"id":"week5-stakeholder-grid","metadata":{"activityType":"Scenario analysis","href":null,"runtimeGlobal":"Week5StakeholderGrid","status":"available","summary":"Stakeholder Impact Grid","title":"Stakeholder Impact Grid"},"relationships":{"assets":[],"assignment":"formative-practice","learningOutcomes":["LO1"],"questions":[]},"schema":"lp.content.activity","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","version":"1.0.0"},{"blocks":[{"content":{"level":2,"text":"Analysing Rather Than Listing Impacts"},"id":"week5-impact-analysis-title","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"heading","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"format":"application/json","text":"```json\n{\n  \"weekNumber\": 5,\n  \"sessionNumber\": 2,\n  \"estimatedMinutes\": 25,\n  \"teachingPoint\": \"Strong answers name a stakeholder, state a specific consequence, use scenario evidence, show timescale, and explain why the consequence follows.\",\n  \"scenario\": \"Ransomware encrypts Northbank booking systems for two working days. Urgent reviews are delayed. Patient contact details may have been exposed. Local media report the outage and patients ask whether records are safe.\",\n  \"weakResponse\": {\n    \"label\": \"Weak response\",\n    \"text\": \"Northbank suffered. Impacts include money, reputation, trust, systems and patients. It was bad. Other hospitals had ransomware too so the same things happened.\",\n    \"problems\": [\n      \"Lists several impacts without explanation\",\n      \"Says the organisation suffered without naming a stakeholder clearly\",\n      \"Mentions money without developing other categories\",\n      \"Fails to use scenario evidence\",\n      \"Ignores timescale\",\n      \"Imports unrelated incidents\"\n    ]\n  },\n  \"strongResponse\": {\n    \"label\": \"Stronger analytical response\",\n    \"text\": \"Patients at Northbank face an immediate safety-related consequence because urgent reviews are delayed while booking systems remain encrypted for two working days, which means time-critical care may be postponed. The scenario also states that patient contact details may have been exposed, so individuals can suffer longer-term loss of confidentiality and confidence. Six months later, reputational damage may continue even after recovery fees are paid, because local media reporting leaves patients asking whether records are safe.\",\n    \"creditAnnotations\": [\n      {\n        \"id\": \"a1\",\n        \"label\": \"Names a stakeholder (patients / individuals)\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"a2\",\n        \"label\": \"States a specific consequence (delayed urgent reviews)\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"a3\",\n        \"label\": \"Uses scenario evidence (two working days; exposed contact details; media reporting)\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"a4\",\n        \"label\": \"Shows immediate and longer-term timescales\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"a5\",\n        \"label\": \"Connects evidence to why the consequence follows\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"id\": \"a6\",\n        \"label\": \"Covers more than financial loss (safety, confidentiality, reputation/confidence)\"\n      }\n    ]\n  },\n  \"writingTasks\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"immediate\",\n      \"label\": \"Write one sentence explaining an immediate impact of the Northbank ransomware incident.\",\n      \"starter\": \"Immediately after the incident\u2026\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"sixMonths\",\n      \"label\": \"Write one sentence explaining an impact that may still be felt six months later.\",\n      \"starter\": \"Six months later\u2026\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"improvementPrompt\": \"Improve your weaker sentence by adding a missing stakeholder, evidence or timescale connection.\"\n}\n```"},"id":"week5-impact-analysis-source-remainder","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"markdown","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"formative":true,"prompt":"Complete this activity on the learner hub page, then write a short note to confirm you have finished.","questionId":"week5-impact-analysis:learner-note","sourceQuestionId":"learner-note"},"id":"week5-impact-analysis-learner-note","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"reflection","version":"0.1.0"}],"id":"week5-impact-analysis","metadata":{"activityType":"Exam skills","href":null,"runtimeGlobal":"Week5ImpactAnalysis","status":"available","summary":"Analysing Rather Than Listing Impacts","title":"Analysing Rather Than Listing Impacts"},"relationships":{"assets":[],"assignment":"formative-practice","learningOutcomes":["LO1"],"questions":[]},"schema":"lp.content.activity","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","version":"1.0.0"},{"blocks":[{"content":{"level":2,"text":"OCR-Style Impact Questions"},"id":"week5-ocr-question-practice-title","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"heading","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"commandWord":"Identify","correctOptionId":"a","feedback":{"correct":"","incorrect":""},"formative":true,"marks":1,"options":[{"id":"a","label":"Loss"},{"id":"b","label":"Disruption only"},{"id":"c","label":"Safety only"},{"id":"d","label":"Motivation"}],"prompt":"Identify which impact category best matches unrecovered destruction of referral letters.","questionId":"week5-ocr-question-practice:ocr-1","sourceQuestionId":"ocr-1","sourceType":"single"},"id":"week5-ocr-question-practice-q-1-ocr-1","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"single-choice","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"commandWord":"Identify","correctOptionId":"a","feedback":{"correct":"","incorrect":""},"formative":true,"marks":1,"options":[{"id":"a","label":"Disruption"},{"id":"b","label":"Identity theft"},{"id":"c","label":"Publicity motivation"},{"id":"d","label":"Legislation"}],"prompt":"Identify which impact category best matches clinic booking services being unavailable for two working days.","questionId":"week5-ocr-question-practice:ocr-2","sourceQuestionId":"ocr-2","sourceType":"single"},"id":"week5-ocr-question-practice-q-2-ocr-2","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"single-choice","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"commandWord":"Identify","correctOptionId":"a","feedback":{"correct":"","incorrect":""},"formative":true,"marks":1,"options":[{"id":"a","label":"Safety"},{"id":"b","label":"Financial loss only"},{"id":"c","label":"Broadcasting disruption"},{"id":"d","label":"No impact"}],"prompt":"Identify which impact category best matches increased clinical risk from a delayed urgent review.","questionId":"week5-ocr-question-practice:ocr-3","sourceQuestionId":"ocr-3","sourceType":"single"},"id":"week5-ocr-question-practice-q-3-ocr-3","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"single-choice","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"commandWord":"Describe","correctOptionId":"","feedback":{"correct":"","incorrect":""},"formative":true,"marks":2,"options":[],"prompt":"Describe one loss impact of the Northbank ransomware incident for an individual patient.","questionId":"week5-ocr-question-practice:ocr-4","sourceQuestionId":"ocr-4","sourceType":"single"},"id":"week5-ocr-question-practice-q-4-ocr-4","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"single-choice","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"commandWord":"Describe","correctOptionId":"","feedback":{"correct":"","incorrect":""},"formative":true,"marks":2,"options":[],"prompt":"Describe one disruption impact for Northbank Community Health Partnership.","questionId":"week5-ocr-question-practice:ocr-5","sourceQuestionId":"ocr-5","sourceType":"single"},"id":"week5-ocr-question-practice-q-5-ocr-5","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"single-choice","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"commandWord":"Explain","correctOptionId":"","feedback":{"correct":"","incorrect":""},"formative":true,"marks":3,"options":[],"prompt":"Explain how the same Northbank ransomware incident can affect a patient differently from a regulator.","questionId":"week5-ocr-question-practice:ocr-6","sourceQuestionId":"ocr-6","sourceType":"single"},"id":"week5-ocr-question-practice-q-6-ocr-6","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"single-choice","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"commandWord":"Explain","correctOptionId":"","feedback":{"correct":"","incorrect":""},"formative":true,"marks":4,"options":[],"prompt":"Explain one immediate consequence and one longer-term consequence of the Northbank incident.","questionId":"week5-ocr-question-practice:ocr-7","sourceQuestionId":"ocr-7","sourceType":"single"},"id":"week5-ocr-question-practice-q-7-ocr-7","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"single-choice","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"commandWord":"Analyse","correctOptionId":"","feedback":{"correct":"","incorrect":""},"formative":true,"marks":6,"options":[],"prompt":"Analyse the impacts of the Northbank ransomware incident on the organisation and its patients.","questionId":"week5-ocr-question-practice:ocr-8","sourceQuestionId":"ocr-8","sourceType":"single"},"id":"week5-ocr-question-practice-q-8-ocr-8","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"single-choice","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"format":"application/json","text":"```json\n{\n  \"weekNumber\": 5,\n  \"sessionNumber\": 2,\n  \"suggestedMinutes\": 20,\n  \"timingGuidance\": \"Use approximately one minute per mark where this helps you manage time. These are OCR-style practice questions, not official OCR examination questions.\",\n  \"beforeReminders\": [\n    \"Cover loss, disruption and safety when impacts are requested.\",\n    \"Name the stakeholder affected.\",\n    \"Distinguish immediate and longer-term consequences.\",\n    \"Use scenario evidence \u2014 do not import unrelated incidents.\",\n    \"Mark schemes stay hidden until you open review.\"\n  ],\n  \"northbankScenario\": \"Northbank Community Health Partnership suffers a ransomware incident. Booking systems and a shared drive are encrypted for two working days. Some appointments are cancelled, including an urgent review. Patient contact details may have been exposed from a shared mailbox. Recovery spending begins immediately. Local media report the outage and patients ask whether records remain safe. A partner clinic pauses some referrals while it seeks assurance.\"\n}\n```"},"id":"week5-ocr-question-practice-source-remainder","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"markdown","version":"0.1.0"}],"id":"week5-ocr-question-practice","metadata":{"activityType":"Exam skills","href":null,"runtimeGlobal":"Week5OcrPractice","status":"available","summary":"OCR-Style Impact Questions","title":"OCR-Style Impact Questions"},"relationships":{"assets":[],"assignment":"formative-practice","learningOutcomes":["LO1"],"questions":[]},"schema":"lp.content.activity","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","version":"1.0.0"},{"blocks":[{"content":{"level":2,"text":"Marking and Answer Improvement"},"id":"week5-answer-improvement-title","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"heading","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"format":"application/json","text":"```json\n{\n  \"weekNumber\": 5,\n  \"sessionNumber\": 2,\n  \"estimatedMinutes\": 25,\n  \"commonError\": \"Covering loss thoroughly \u2014 especially financial loss \u2014 while ignoring disruption and safety.\",\n  \"question\": {\n    \"commandWord\": \"Analyse\",\n    \"marks\": 6,\n    \"prompt\": \"Analyse the impacts of a ransomware incident on Northbank Community Health Partnership and its patients.\"\n  },\n  \"sampleResponse\": {\n    \"text\": \"Northbank would lose money because it must pay for recovery and overtime. It might also lose reputation if people hear about the attack. Patients might worry. Money is the main impact.\"\n  },\n  \"dominantIssues\": [\n    \"Financial loss is developed, but disruption of booking services is ignored\",\n    \"Safety for patients with delayed urgent care is ignored\",\n    \"Stakeholder naming is thin\",\n    \"Scenario evidence is limited\",\n    \"Timescale is not developed beyond immediate spending\"\n  ],\n  \"markSchemePoints\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"m1\",\n      \"label\": \"Names organisation and/or patient stakeholders\",\n      \"marks\": \"1\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"m2\",\n      \"label\": \"Develops a loss impact with evidence\",\n      \"marks\": \"1\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"m3\",\n      \"label\": \"Develops a disruption impact with evidence\",\n      \"marks\": \"1\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"m4\",\n      \"label\": \"Develops a safety impact with evidence\",\n      \"marks\": \"1\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"m5\",\n      \"label\": \"Makes analytical connections rather than a list\",\n      \"marks\": \"1\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"m6\",\n      \"label\": \"Includes immediate and longer-term consequences\",\n      \"marks\": \"1\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"improvementRequirements\": [\n    \"Add a missing safety impact\",\n    \"Name the stakeholder affected\",\n    \"Add evidence or reasoning from the scenario\",\n    \"Add a timescale where relevant\"\n  ],\n  \"modelAfterSubmit\": \"Improved responses should add a patient safety impact (for example delayed urgent review), name the stakeholder, cite scenario evidence, and show whether the consequence is immediate or longer term. Do not rely on financial loss alone.\"\n}\n```"},"id":"week5-answer-improvement-source-remainder","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"markdown","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"formative":true,"prompt":"Complete this activity on the learner hub page, then write a short note to confirm you have finished.","questionId":"week5-answer-improvement:learner-note","sourceQuestionId":"learner-note"},"id":"week5-answer-improvement-learner-note","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"reflection","version":"0.1.0"}],"id":"week5-answer-improvement","metadata":{"activityType":"Self marking","href":null,"runtimeGlobal":"Week5AnswerImprovement","status":"available","summary":"Marking and Answer Improvement","title":"Marking and Answer Improvement"},"relationships":{"assets":[],"assignment":"formative-practice","learningOutcomes":["LO1"],"questions":[]},"schema":"lp.content.activity","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","version":"1.0.0"},{"blocks":[{"content":{"level":2,"text":"LO2 Diagnostic Retrieval"},"id":"week6-lo2-diagnostic-title","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"heading","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"correctOptionId":"b","feedback":{"correct":"A threat is a potential cause of harm. A vulnerability is a weakness that may be exploited.","incorrect":"A threat is a potential cause of harm. A vulnerability is a weakness that may be exploited."},"formative":true,"options":[{"id":"a","label":"A weakness that makes harm more likely"},{"id":"b","label":"A potential cause of harm or damage to systems or data"},{"id":"c","label":"A law that organisations must follow"},{"id":"d","label":"The cost of running a security control"}],"prompt":"Which option best describes a cyber security threat?","questionId":"week6-lo2-diagnostic:d1","sourceQuestionId":"d1","sourceType":"single"},"id":"week6-lo2-diagnostic-q-1-d1","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"single-choice","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"correctOptionId":"b","feedback":{"correct":"An unpatched server is a weakness that could be exploited. Threats and vulnerabilities are linked but not the same.","incorrect":"An unpatched server is a weakness that could be exploited. Threats and vulnerabilities are linked but not the same."},"formative":true,"options":[{"id":"a","label":"A motivation"},{"id":"b","label":"A vulnerability"},{"id":"c","label":"An operational consideration only"},{"id":"d","label":"A government initiative"}],"prompt":"An unpatched server is best classified as:","questionId":"week6-lo2-diagnostic:d2","sourceQuestionId":"d2","sourceType":"single"},"id":"week6-lo2-diagnostic-q-2-d2","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"single-choice","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"correctOptionId":"b","feedback":{"correct":"Insiders already have access or knowledge of internal systems. Other attacker types may also target organisations from outside.","incorrect":"Insiders already have access or knowledge of internal systems. Other attacker types may also target organisations from outside."},"formative":true,"options":[{"id":"a","label":"Script kiddie"},{"id":"b","label":"Insider"},{"id":"c","label":"Hacktivist only"},{"id":"d","label":"Nation state only"}],"prompt":"Which attacker type is most associated with acting from inside an organisation?","questionId":"week6-lo2-diagnostic:d3","sourceQuestionId":"d3","sourceType":"single"},"id":"week6-lo2-diagnostic-q-3-d3","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"single-choice","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"correctOptionId":"b","feedback":{"correct":"Income generation is a motivation (why someone acts). Impacts and legal duties are separate ideas.","incorrect":"Income generation is a motivation (why someone acts). Impacts and legal duties are separate ideas."},"formative":true,"options":[{"id":"a","label":"Operational downtime"},{"id":"b","label":"Financial motivation"},{"id":"c","label":"Responsible disclosure"},{"id":"d","label":"A legal duty under data protection legislation"}],"prompt":"Seeking ransom payment after encrypting files is mainly an example of:","questionId":"week6-lo2-diagnostic:d4","sourceQuestionId":"d4","sourceType":"single"},"id":"week6-lo2-diagnostic-q-4-d4","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"single-choice","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"correctOptionId":"b","feedback":{"correct":"Healthcare data is sensitive and valuable to attackers for fraud, resale or coercion.","incorrect":"Healthcare data is sensitive and valuable to attackers for fraud, resale or coercion."},"formative":true,"options":[{"id":"a","label":"Always public information"},{"id":"b","label":"Valuable and sensitive data held by the organisation"},{"id":"c","label":"Only an operational cost"},{"id":"d","label":"Defined by the Cyber Essentials Scheme"}],"prompt":"Patient records at Northbank Community Health Partnership are mainly a target because they are:","questionId":"week6-lo2-diagnostic:d5","sourceQuestionId":"d5","sourceType":"single"},"id":"week6-lo2-diagnostic-q-5-d5","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"single-choice","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"correctOptionId":"a","feedback":{"correct":"Phishing is a social-engineering method attackers use to gain access or information.","incorrect":"Phishing is a social-engineering method attackers use to gain access or information."},"formative":true,"options":[{"id":"a","label":"A method or attack technique"},{"id":"b","label":"An ethical hacking rule of engagement"},{"id":"c","label":"The United Kingdom Cyber Security Strategy"},{"id":"d","label":"Lost productivity"}],"prompt":"Phishing emails used to trick staff into revealing credentials are an example of:","questionId":"week6-lo2-diagnostic:d6","sourceQuestionId":"d6","sourceType":"single"},"id":"week6-lo2-diagnostic-q-6-d6","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"single-choice","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"correctOptionId":"b","feedback":{"correct":"Cancelled appointments describe disruption to a service. The same event may also create loss or safety impacts for other stakeholders.","incorrect":"Cancelled appointments describe disruption to a service. The same event may also create loss or safety impacts for other stakeholders."},"formative":true,"options":[{"id":"a","label":"Loss only"},{"id":"b","label":"Disruption"},{"id":"c","label":"Operational consideration only"},{"id":"d","label":"Government initiative"}],"prompt":"When clinic appointments are cancelled because systems fail, which impact category fits best?","questionId":"week6-lo2-diagnostic:d7","sourceQuestionId":"d7","sourceType":"single"},"id":"week6-lo2-diagnostic-q-7-d7","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"single-choice","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"correctOptionId":"b","feedback":{"correct":"Responsible disclosure balances helping fix a flaw with avoiding unnecessary harm from publicising it too early.","incorrect":"Responsible disclosure balances helping fix a flaw with avoiding unnecessary harm from publicising it too early."},"formative":true,"options":[{"id":"a","label":"Insider trading"},{"id":"b","label":"Responsible disclosure"},{"id":"c","label":"Computer misuse"},{"id":"d","label":"Mandatory breach notification without context"}],"prompt":"Reporting a vulnerability privately to a vendor before public release is called:","questionId":"week6-lo2-diagnostic:d8","sourceQuestionId":"d8","sourceType":"single"},"id":"week6-lo2-diagnostic-q-8-d8","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"single-choice","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"correctOptionId":"b","feedback":{"correct":"The Computer Misuse Act 1990 covers unauthorised access and related offences. Guidance documents are not statutes.","incorrect":"The Computer Misuse Act 1990 covers unauthorised access and related offences. Guidance documents are not statutes."},"formative":true,"options":[{"id":"a","label":"Cyber Streetwise only"},{"id":"b","label":"Computer Misuse Act 1990"},{"id":"c","label":"10 Steps to Cyber Security"},{"id":"d","label":"Operational downtime planning"}],"prompt":"Unauthorised access to a computer system without permission in the United Kingdom is mainly addressed by:","questionId":"week6-lo2-diagnostic:d9","sourceQuestionId":"d9","sourceType":"single"},"id":"week6-lo2-diagnostic-q-9-d9","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"single-choice","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"correctOptionId":"b","feedback":{"correct":"Organisations processing personal data must follow current United Kingdom data protection legislation, not guidance schemes alone.","incorrect":"Organisations processing personal data must follow current United Kingdom data protection legislation, not guidance schemes alone."},"formative":true,"options":[{"id":"a","label":"Cyber Essentials Scheme only"},{"id":"b","label":"Current United Kingdom data protection legislation"},{"id":"c","label":"Ethical hacking rules of engagement only"},{"id":"d","label":"Lost productivity policies"}],"prompt":"Handling personal data at Northbank must comply with:","questionId":"week6-lo2-diagnostic:d10","sourceQuestionId":"d10","sourceType":"single"},"id":"week6-lo2-diagnostic-q-10-d10","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"single-choice","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"correctOptionId":"b","feedback":{"correct":"Operational factors include usability and whether controls encourage staff to find unsafe shortcuts.","incorrect":"Operational factors include usability and whether controls encourage staff to find unsafe shortcuts."},"formative":true,"options":[{"id":"a","label":"Legal certainty only"},{"id":"b","label":"Workarounds and lost productivity"},{"id":"c","label":"Responsible disclosure"},{"id":"d","label":"Nation-state motivation"}],"prompt":"Requiring very long complex passwords that staff cannot remember may increase:","questionId":"week6-lo2-diagnostic:d11","sourceQuestionId":"d11","sourceType":"single"},"id":"week6-lo2-diagnostic-q-11-d11","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"single-choice","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"correctOptionId":"b","feedback":{"correct":"Operational considerations include cost, staff time, downtime, usability and productivity effects.","incorrect":"Operational considerations include cost, staff time, downtime, usability and productivity effects."},"formative":true,"options":[{"id":"a","label":"Whether the action is unethical"},{"id":"b","label":"Staff time needed to operate the control"},{"id":"c","label":"Whether hacktivists exist"},{"id":"d","label":"The name of a statute alone"}],"prompt":"Which factor is an operational consideration when choosing a security control?","questionId":"week6-lo2-diagnostic:d12","sourceQuestionId":"d12","sourceType":"single"},"id":"week6-lo2-diagnostic-q-12-d12","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"single-choice","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"format":"application/json","text":"```json\n{\n  \"weekNumber\": 6,\n  \"sessionNumber\": 1,\n  \"estimatedMinutes\": 20,\n  \"formativeNote\": \"This diagnostic is formative only. It helps you identify revision priorities. It is not an official grade.\",\n  \"topicLabels\": {\n    \"threats\": \"Threats\",\n    \"vulnerabilities\": \"Vulnerabilities\",\n    \"attackerTypes\": \"Attacker types\",\n    \"motivations\": \"Motivations\",\n    \"targets\": \"Targets\",\n    \"methods\": \"Methods\",\n    \"impacts\": \"Impacts\",\n    \"ethical\": \"Ethical considerations\",\n    \"legal\": \"Legal considerations\",\n    \"operational\": \"Operational considerations\"\n  }\n}\n```"},"id":"week6-lo2-diagnostic-source-remainder","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"markdown","version":"0.1.0"}],"id":"week6-lo2-diagnostic","metadata":{"activityType":"Diagnostic quiz","href":null,"runtimeGlobal":"Week6Lo2Diagnostic","status":"available","summary":"LO2 Diagnostic Retrieval","title":"LO2 Diagnostic Retrieval"},"relationships":{"assets":[],"assignment":"formative-practice","learningOutcomes":["LO1"],"questions":[]},"schema":"lp.content.activity","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","version":"1.0.0"},{"blocks":[{"content":{"level":2,"text":"Ethical Considerations Learning"},"id":"week6-ethical-learning-title","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"heading","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"level":3,"text":"Responsible disclosure"},"id":"week6-ethical-learning-disclosure-h","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"heading","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"level":3,"text":"Employee monitoring"},"id":"week6-ethical-learning-monitoring-h","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"heading","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"level":3,"text":"Ethical hacking and the authorisation boundary"},"id":"week6-ethical-learning-auth-h","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"heading","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"level":3,"text":"Ethics versus law"},"id":"week6-ethical-learning-ethics-law-h","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"heading","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"correctOptionId":"b","feedback":{"correct":"The goal is safer remediation, not publicity or replacing legal frameworks.","incorrect":"The goal is safer remediation, not publicity or replacing legal frameworks."},"formative":true,"options":[{"id":"a","label":"Maximise publicity for the researcher"},{"id":"b","label":"Allow organisations to fix flaws before wider exploitation"},{"id":"c","label":"Replace data protection legislation"},{"id":"d","label":"Eliminate the need for penetration testing"}],"prompt":"Responsible disclosure mainly aims to:","questionId":"week6-ethical-learning:ek1","sourceQuestionId":"ek1","sourceType":"single"},"id":"week6-ethical-learning-q-1-ek1","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"single-choice","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"correctOptionId":"a","feedback":{"correct":"Rules of engagement, with permission and scope, define authorised testing boundaries.","incorrect":"Rules of engagement, with permission and scope, define authorised testing boundaries."},"formative":true,"options":[{"id":"a","label":"Rules of engagement"},{"id":"b","label":"Lost productivity"},{"id":"c","label":"Cyber Essentials Scheme"},{"id":"d","label":"Safety impact only"}],"prompt":"Which Week 3 idea limits what an ethical tester may do?","questionId":"week6-ethical-learning:ek2","sourceQuestionId":"ek2","sourceType":"single"},"id":"week6-ethical-learning-q-2-ek2","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"single-choice","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"format":"application/json","text":"```json\n{\n  \"weekNumber\": 6,\n  \"sessionNumber\": 1,\n  \"estimatedMinutes\": 30,\n  \"overviewNote\": \"Ethical considerations ask what is right or fair, even when the law may not clearly forbid an action. Week 6 builds on earlier LO2 topics and connects to Week 3 penetration testing ideas: permission, scope and rules of engagement.\"\n}\n```"},"id":"week6-ethical-learning-source-remainder","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"markdown","version":"0.1.0"}],"id":"week6-ethical-learning","metadata":{"activityType":"Guided learning","href":null,"runtimeGlobal":"Week6EthicalLearning","status":"available","summary":"Ethical Considerations Learning","title":"Ethical Considerations Learning"},"relationships":{"assets":[],"assignment":"formative-practice","learningOutcomes":["LO1"],"questions":[]},"schema":"lp.content.activity","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","version":"1.0.0"},{"blocks":[{"content":{"level":2,"text":"Ethical, Unlawful, Both or Neither"},"id":"week6-ethical-classification-title","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"heading","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"format":"application/json","text":"```json\n{\n  \"weekNumber\": 6,\n  \"sessionNumber\": 1,\n  \"estimatedMinutes\": 25,\n  \"categories\": [\n    \"Unethical\",\n    \"Unlawful\",\n    \"Both unethical and unlawful\",\n    \"Neither unethical nor unlawful\"\n  ],\n  \"instructions\": [\n    \"Classify each scenario using the four categories.\",\n    \"Ethics and law are related but not identical.\",\n    \"Some scenarios need more facts before a firm legal conclusion.\",\n    \"Feedback explains the ethical and legal dimensions separately.\"\n  ],\n  \"items\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"e1\",\n      \"statement\": \"A Northbank receptionist reads a celebrity patient record out of curiosity, with no clinical need and no permission.\",\n      \"accepted\": [\n        \"Unethical\",\n        \"Both unethical and unlawful\"\n      ],\n      \"feedback\": \"Ethically, this breaches trust and confidentiality expectations. Legally, unauthorised access to personal data may engage current United Kingdom data protection legislation and possibly Computer Misuse Act 1990, depending on authorisation and intent. More facts may be needed for a firm legal conclusion.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"e2\",\n      \"statement\": \"An authorised penetration tester runs agreed tests only on systems listed in the signed scope during the agreed window.\",\n      \"accepted\": [\n        \"Neither unethical nor unlawful\"\n      ],\n      \"feedback\": \"With permission, scope and rules of engagement, this is authorised security testing. It is not unethical hacking and is not unlawful in that context.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"e3\",\n      \"statement\": \"A student downloads a password-cracking tool from the internet to try on a friend home router without the friend knowledge.\",\n      \"accepted\": [\n        \"Both unethical and unlawful\"\n      ],\n      \"feedback\": \"Ethically, this violates consent and privacy. Unauthorised access attempts may breach Computer Misuse Act 1990. Supplying or preparing tools for misuse may also engage Police and Justice Act 2006 amendments in some circumstances.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"e4\",\n      \"statement\": \"Northbank publishes a clear fair-processing notice explaining that access logs may be reviewed after a suspected insider breach.\",\n      \"accepted\": [\n        \"Neither unethical nor unlawful\"\n      ],\n      \"feedback\": \"Transparent, proportionate monitoring communication supports ethical practice and aligns with data protection expectations. This is not inherently unethical or unlawful.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"e5\",\n      \"statement\": \"A manager secretly installs keylogging software on all staff machines indefinitely, including break rooms, with no security incident reason.\",\n      \"accepted\": [\n        \"Unethical\",\n        \"Both unethical and unlawful\"\n      ],\n      \"feedback\": \"Ethically, this is disproportionate and invasive. Legally, covert excessive monitoring may engage data protection and employment law issues. More organisational context may be needed for a precise legal label.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"e6\",\n      \"statement\": \"A researcher publicly releases a Northbank exploit with no prior warning one hour after discovery.\",\n      \"accepted\": [\n        \"Unethical\"\n      ],\n      \"feedback\": \"This fails responsible disclosure ethics and may harm patients and staff. Whether it is unlawful depends on what was accessed and how. Do not assume ethics and law always align without facts.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"e7\",\n      \"statement\": \"An employee uses their own credentials to export patient lists they are not permitted to access, then sells the data.\",\n      \"accepted\": [\n        \"Both unethical and unlawful\"\n      ],\n      \"feedback\": \"Clearly unethical misuse of trust. Unauthorised access and misuse of personal data likely engages Computer Misuse Act 1990 and current United Kingdom data protection legislation.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"e8\",\n      \"statement\": \"Northbank requires staff to complete annual cyber security awareness training during paid working time.\",\n      \"accepted\": [\n        \"Neither unethical nor unlawful\"\n      ],\n      \"feedback\": \"Training during paid time is a reasonable organisational expectation. It is not unethical and is not unlawful merely because staff must attend.\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```"},"id":"week6-ethical-classification-source-remainder","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"markdown","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"formative":true,"prompt":"Complete this activity on the learner hub page, then write a short note to confirm you have finished.","questionId":"week6-ethical-classification:learner-note","sourceQuestionId":"learner-note"},"id":"week6-ethical-classification-learner-note","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"reflection","version":"0.1.0"}],"id":"week6-ethical-classification","metadata":{"activityType":"Classification","href":null,"runtimeGlobal":"Week6EthicalClassification","status":"available","summary":"Ethical, Unlawful, Both or Neither","title":"Ethical, Unlawful, Both or Neither"},"relationships":{"assets":[],"assignment":"formative-practice","learningOutcomes":["LO1"],"questions":[]},"schema":"lp.content.activity","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","version":"1.0.0"},{"blocks":[{"content":{"level":2,"text":"United Kingdom Legislation Learning"},"id":"week6-legislation-learning-title","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"heading","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"correctOptionId":"b","feedback":{"correct":"Name legislation and the relevant duty or offence. Guidance schemes are not statutes.","incorrect":"Name legislation and the relevant duty or offence. Guidance schemes are not statutes."},"formative":true,"options":[{"id":"a","label":"Computer Misuse Act 1990: lawful basis for marketing emails"},{"id":"b","label":"Current United Kingdom data protection legislation: duties when processing personal data"},{"id":"c","label":"Cyber Essentials Scheme: criminal offence for hacking"},{"id":"d","label":"Cyber Streetwise: statute for unauthorised access"}],"prompt":"Which pairing is most accurate for examination answers?","questionId":"week6-legislation-learning:lk1","sourceQuestionId":"lk1","sourceType":"single"},"id":"week6-legislation-learning-q-1-lk1","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"single-choice","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"correctOptionId":"b","feedback":{"correct":"Unauthorised access offences sit under Computer Misuse Act 1990, not guidance documents.","incorrect":"Unauthorised access offences sit under Computer Misuse Act 1990, not guidance documents."},"formative":true,"options":[{"id":"a","label":"Cyber Streetwise"},{"id":"b","label":"Computer Misuse Act 1990"},{"id":"c","label":"10 Steps to Cyber Security"},{"id":"d","label":"Operational downtime"}],"prompt":"Unauthorised access to Northbank servers without permission is mainly linked to:","questionId":"week6-legislation-learning:lk2","sourceQuestionId":"lk2","sourceType":"single"},"id":"week6-legislation-learning-q-2-lk2","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"single-choice","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"correctOptionId":"a","feedback":{"correct":"Tool supply offences were strengthened through Police and Justice Act 2006 amendments.","incorrect":"Tool supply offences were strengthened through Police and Justice Act 2006 amendments."},"formative":true,"options":[{"id":"a","label":"Police and Justice Act 2006 amendments (supplying tools for misuse)"},{"id":"b","label":"United Kingdom Cyber Security Strategy only"},{"id":"c","label":"Responsible disclosure only"},{"id":"d","label":"Lost productivity"}],"prompt":"Supplying a hacking tool knowing it will likely be used for unauthorised access relates to:","questionId":"week6-legislation-learning:lk3","sourceQuestionId":"lk3","sourceType":"single"},"id":"week6-legislation-learning-q-3-lk3","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"single-choice","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"correctOptionId":"b","feedback":{"correct":"Examiners expect the law plus the duty or offence, applied to the scenario where appropriate.","incorrect":"Examiners expect the law plus the duty or offence, applied to the scenario where appropriate."},"formative":true,"options":[{"id":"a","label":"Always sufficient on its own"},{"id":"b","label":"Insufficient without naming the relevant duty or offence"},{"id":"c","label":"Better than explaining Northbank context"},{"id":"d","label":"Only needed for ethical questions"}],"prompt":"A bare statute name in an examination answer is:","questionId":"week6-legislation-learning:lk4","sourceQuestionId":"lk4","sourceType":"single"},"id":"week6-legislation-learning-q-4-lk4","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"single-choice","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"correctOptionId":"b","feedback":{"correct":"Personal data handling duties are under data protection legislation. Computer misuse may also apply to unauthorised access.","incorrect":"Personal data handling duties are under data protection legislation. Computer misuse may also apply to unauthorised access."},"formative":true,"options":[{"id":"a","label":"Computer Misuse Act 1990 alone"},{"id":"b","label":"Current United Kingdom data protection legislation"},{"id":"c","label":"Cyber Essentials Scheme"},{"id":"d","label":"Rules of engagement"}],"prompt":"After an insider data breach at Northbank, personal data duties mainly come from:","questionId":"week6-legislation-learning:lk5","sourceQuestionId":"lk5","sourceType":"single"},"id":"week6-legislation-learning-q-5-lk5","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"single-choice","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"correctOptionId":"b","feedback":{"correct":"Use current United Kingdom legislation names and accurate duties. Follow tutor and official sources.","incorrect":"Use current United Kingdom legislation names and accurate duties. Follow tutor and official sources."},"formative":true,"options":[{"id":"a","label":"Because ethics never change"},{"id":"b","label":"Because law and guidance evolve and outdated names or duties lose marks"},{"id":"c","label":"Because operational costs are statutes"},{"id":"d","label":"Because NCSC exercises replace legislation"}],"prompt":"Why must learners keep legislation current?","questionId":"week6-legislation-learning:lk6","sourceQuestionId":"lk6","sourceType":"single"},"id":"week6-legislation-learning-q-6-lk6","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"single-choice","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"format":"application/json","text":"```json\n{\n  \"weekNumber\": 6,\n  \"sessionNumber\": 1,\n  \"estimatedMinutes\": 30,\n  \"teachingNote\": \"Examination answers must name the law and the relevant duty or offence. A bare statute name alone is insufficient. Keep legislation current: use official sources and tutor guidance rather than outdated summaries.\",\n  \"laws\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"cma\",\n      \"formalName\": \"Computer Misuse Act 1990\",\n      \"purpose\": \"Creates criminal offences for unauthorised access to computer material, unauthorised access with intent, and unauthorised modification of computer material.\",\n      \"dutyOffence\": \"Relevant offences include unauthorised access to computer material and unauthorised acts with intent to impair operation of a computer.\",\n      \"northbankApplication\": \"If an insider accesses patient records without permission, or an external attacker breaks into Northbank systems, Computer Misuse Act 1990 offences may apply depending on authorisation and intent.\",\n      \"misconception\": \"Misconception: Computer Misuse Act 1990 is not the main statute for lawful processing of personal data. Data protection is addressed separately under current United Kingdom data protection legislation.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"dp\",\n      \"formalName\": \"Current United Kingdom data protection legislation\",\n      \"purpose\": \"Sets duties for organisations that process personal data, including lawful basis, fairness, security and accountability expectations.\",\n      \"dutyOffence\": \"Relevant duties include processing personal data lawfully, securely and transparently, and handling personal data breaches appropriately under the current framework.\",\n      \"northbankApplication\": \"Northbank must protect patient personal data, limit access to what is necessary and respond properly if an insider causes a data breach affecting records.\",\n      \"misconception\": \"Misconception: do not invent section numbers, notification periods or penalty amounts in examination answers. Name the legislation and the relevant duty or offence in plain language.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"pja\",\n      \"formalName\": \"Police and Justice Act 2006 amendments (supplying tools for misuse)\",\n      \"purpose\": \"Amended computer misuse law to address making, supplying or obtaining articles for use in computer misuse offences.\",\n      \"dutyOffence\": \"Relevant offence area: supplying or making available tools knowing they are likely to be used to commit unauthorised access or related misuse.\",\n      \"northbankApplication\": \"If someone distributes a bespoke credential-stealing kit aimed at Northbank staff, supply-of-tools offences may be relevant alongside direct misuse offences.\",\n      \"misconception\": \"Misconception: possessing security testing tools is not automatically illegal. Context, authorisation and intent matter, especially for legitimate security work.\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```"},"id":"week6-legislation-learning-source-remainder","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"markdown","version":"0.1.0"}],"id":"week6-legislation-learning","metadata":{"activityType":"Guided learning","href":null,"runtimeGlobal":"Week6LegislationLearning","status":"available","summary":"United Kingdom Legislation Learning","title":"United Kingdom Legislation Learning"},"relationships":{"assets":[],"assignment":"formative-practice","learningOutcomes":["LO1"],"questions":[]},"schema":"lp.content.activity","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","version":"1.0.0"},{"blocks":[{"content":{"level":2,"text":"Legislation Scenario Matching"},"id":"week6-legislation-matching-title","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"heading","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"format":"application/json","text":"```json\n{\n  \"weekNumber\": 6,\n  \"sessionNumber\": 1,\n  \"estimatedMinutes\": 25,\n  \"legislationOptions\": [\n    \"Computer Misuse Act 1990\",\n    \"Current United Kingdom data protection legislation\",\n    \"Police and Justice Act 2006 amendments (supplying tools for misuse)\",\n    \"Not primarily a criminal statute scenario\"\n  ],\n  \"dutyOptions\": [\n    \"Unauthorised access to computer material\",\n    \"Unauthorised modification of computer material\",\n    \"Processing personal data without appropriate security or lawful basis\",\n    \"Handling a personal data breach under current duties\",\n    \"Supplying tools knowing they are likely to be used for computer misuse\",\n    \"Not primarily a criminal statute scenario\"\n  ],\n  \"scenarios\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"m1\",\n      \"text\": \"An attacker in another country uses stolen credentials to enter Northbank patient record system without permission.\",\n      \"legislation\": \"Computer Misuse Act 1990\",\n      \"duty\": \"Unauthorised access to computer material\",\n      \"feedback\": \"Unauthorised access to systems is a Computer Misuse Act 1990 concern. Personal data duties may also apply separately, but do not label this as data protection alone.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"m2\",\n      \"text\": \"An insider exports thousands of patient details they are not permitted to use and shares them with a third party.\",\n      \"legislation\": \"Current United Kingdom data protection legislation\",\n      \"duty\": \"Processing personal data without appropriate security or lawful basis\",\n      \"feedback\": \"Misuse of personal data engages data protection duties. Computer Misuse Act 1990 may also apply to unauthorised access, but the core personal data duty is under current United Kingdom data protection legislation.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"m3\",\n      \"text\": \"A forum seller offers a ready-made phishing kit advertised for breaking into GP partnerships.\",\n      \"legislation\": \"Police and Justice Act 2006 amendments (supplying tools for misuse)\",\n      \"duty\": \"Supplying tools knowing they are likely to be used for computer misuse\",\n      \"feedback\": \"Supplying tools for misuse is not the same as the Computer Misuse Act 1990 access offence itself. Name the supply offence under the Police and Justice Act 2006 amendments.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"m4\",\n      \"text\": \"Malware encrypts Northbank servers and deletes backups without authorisation.\",\n      \"legislation\": \"Computer Misuse Act 1990\",\n      \"duty\": \"Unauthorised modification of computer material\",\n      \"feedback\": \"Encrypting or deleting data without permission may be unauthorised modification. Do not assume every incident is only a data protection matter.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"m5\",\n      \"text\": \"After discovering an insider breach, Northbank must assess harm and respond under its data protection responsibilities.\",\n      \"legislation\": \"Current United Kingdom data protection legislation\",\n      \"duty\": \"Handling a personal data breach under current duties\",\n      \"feedback\": \"Breaches involving personal data engage current United Kingdom data protection legislation. Do not invent notification periods or section numbers in answers.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"m6\",\n      \"text\": \"A tutor explains the United Kingdom Cyber Security Strategy themes in class without accessing any system.\",\n      \"legislation\": \"Not primarily a criminal statute scenario\",\n      \"duty\": \"Not primarily a criminal statute scenario\",\n      \"feedback\": \"Government strategy is guidance, not a criminal statute. The CMA-for-data-protection misconception: strategy documents do not create criminal offences.\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```"},"id":"week6-legislation-matching-source-remainder","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"markdown","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"formative":true,"prompt":"Complete this activity on the learner hub page, then write a short note to confirm you have finished.","questionId":"week6-legislation-matching:learner-note","sourceQuestionId":"learner-note"},"id":"week6-legislation-matching-learner-note","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"reflection","version":"0.1.0"}],"id":"week6-legislation-matching","metadata":{"activityType":"Matching","href":null,"runtimeGlobal":"Week6LegislationMatching","status":"available","summary":"Legislation Scenario Matching","title":"Legislation Scenario Matching"},"relationships":{"assets":[],"assignment":"formative-practice","learningOutcomes":["LO1"],"questions":[]},"schema":"lp.content.activity","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","version":"1.0.0"},{"blocks":[{"content":{"level":2,"text":"Operational Considerations"},"id":"week6-operational-considerations-title","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"heading","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"text":"Operational considerations ask whether a security control is practical to run day to day. A control that is legally allowed and ethically desirable may still fail if staff cannot use it effectively."},"id":"week6-operational-considerations-intro","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"paragraph","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"format":"application/json","text":"```json\n{\n  \"weekNumber\": 6,\n  \"sessionNumber\": 1,\n  \"estimatedMinutes\": 30,\n  \"intro\": \"Operational considerations ask whether a security control is practical to run day to day. A control that is legally allowed and ethically desirable may still fail if staff cannot use it effectively.\",\n  \"factors\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"financial\",\n      \"label\": \"Financial cost\",\n      \"description\": \"Direct spending on licences, hardware, consultants and ongoing subscriptions.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"staffTime\",\n      \"label\": \"Staff time\",\n      \"description\": \"Hours spent configuring, monitoring, approving access and responding to alerts.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"downtime\",\n      \"label\": \"System downtime\",\n      \"description\": \"Planned or unplanned outages while patching, testing or recovering systems.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"usability\",\n      \"label\": \"Usability\",\n      \"description\": \"Whether staff can follow the control without excessive friction or confusion.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"productivity\",\n      \"label\": \"Lost productivity\",\n      \"description\": \"Work slowed or deferred because security steps add delay or complexity.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"measurePrompt\": \"Northbank is considering mandatory hardware security keys for all remote access to patient systems after an insider threat exercise.\",\n  \"formFields\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"measure\",\n      \"label\": \"Security measure being considered\",\n      \"required\": true,\n      \"rows\": 2\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"financial\",\n      \"label\": \"Financial cost: what would Northbank pay or save?\",\n      \"required\": true,\n      \"rows\": 2\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"staffTime\",\n      \"label\": \"Staff time: who spends time and on what?\",\n      \"required\": true,\n      \"rows\": 2\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"downtime\",\n      \"label\": \"System downtime: when might services be unavailable?\",\n      \"required\": true,\n      \"rows\": 2\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"usability\",\n      \"label\": \"Usability: how easy is the control for clinic and remote staff?\",\n      \"required\": true,\n      \"rows\": 2\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"productivity\",\n      \"label\": \"Lost productivity: where might work slow down?\",\n      \"required\": true,\n      \"rows\": 2\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"workaround\",\n      \"label\": \"Which operational cost most encourages unsafe workarounds?\",\n      \"required\": true,\n      \"rows\": 2\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"proportionate\",\n      \"label\": \"Is the measure proportionate for Northbank? Justify briefly.\",\n      \"required\": true,\n      \"rows\": 3\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```"},"id":"week6-operational-considerations-source-remainder","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"markdown","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"formative":true,"prompt":"Complete this activity on the learner hub page, then write a short note to confirm you have finished.","questionId":"week6-operational-considerations:learner-note","sourceQuestionId":"learner-note"},"id":"week6-operational-considerations-learner-note","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"reflection","version":"0.1.0"}],"id":"week6-operational-considerations","metadata":{"activityType":"Scenario analysis","href":null,"runtimeGlobal":"Week6OperationalConsiderations","status":"available","summary":"Operational Considerations","title":"Operational Considerations"},"relationships":{"assets":[],"assignment":"formative-practice","learningOutcomes":["LO1"],"questions":[]},"schema":"lp.content.activity","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","version":"1.0.0"},{"blocks":[{"content":{"level":2,"text":"Government Cyber Security Initiatives"},"id":"week6-government-initiatives-title","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"heading","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"format":"application/json","text":"```json\n{\n  \"weekNumber\": 6,\n  \"sessionNumber\": 1,\n  \"estimatedMinutes\": 20,\n  \"teachingNote\": \"These initiatives are United Kingdom government guidance or programmes. Describe their purpose in examination answers. Do not invent unsupported claims about current certification status or funding.\",\n  \"initiatives\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"strategy\",\n      \"name\": \"United Kingdom Cyber Security Strategy\",\n      \"purpose\": \"Sets national direction for improving cyber resilience across government, industry and society, prioritising threats and coordinated response.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"essentials\",\n      \"name\": \"Cyber Essentials Scheme\",\n      \"purpose\": \"Provides a baseline set of technical controls and a certification route to help organisations reduce common internet-facing risks.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"tenSteps\",\n      \"name\": \"10 Steps to Cyber Security\",\n      \"purpose\": \"Offers board-level and organisational guidance on essential security areas such as risk management, asset protection and incident response planning.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"streetwise\",\n      \"name\": \"Cyber Streetwise\",\n      \"purpose\": \"A public awareness campaign helping individuals and small organisations adopt safer everyday online habits.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"comparisonQuiz\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"gi1\",\n      \"prompt\": \"Which initiative is mainly aimed at baseline organisational controls and certification?\",\n      \"options\": [\n        \"Cyber Essentials Scheme\",\n        \"Cyber Streetwise\",\n        \"Police and Justice Act 2006 amendments\",\n        \"Computer Misuse Act 1990\"\n      ],\n      \"correctIndex\": 0,\n      \"explanation\": \"Cyber Essentials Scheme focuses on baseline controls and certification. It is not criminal legislation.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"gi2\",\n      \"prompt\": \"Which initiative sets broad national direction rather than day-to-day staff habits alone?\",\n      \"options\": [\n        \"United Kingdom Cyber Security Strategy\",\n        \"Cyber Streetwise only\",\n        \"Responsible disclosure\",\n        \"Rules of engagement\"\n      ],\n      \"correctIndex\": 0,\n      \"explanation\": \"The national strategy sets direction across society. Cyber Streetwise targets public awareness at a smaller scale.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"gi3\",\n      \"prompt\": \"10 Steps to Cyber Security is best described as:\",\n      \"options\": [\n        \"Organisational guidance for leaders on essential security areas\",\n        \"A statute creating hacking offences\",\n        \"A Northbank patient record system\",\n        \"Mandatory hardware key standard\"\n      ],\n      \"correctIndex\": 0,\n      \"explanation\": \"10 Steps to Cyber Security is guidance for organisations, not a statute.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"gi4\",\n      \"prompt\": \"Cyber Streetwise primarily supports:\",\n      \"options\": [\n        \"Public and small organisation awareness of safer online behaviour\",\n        \"Prosecution of computer misuse offences\",\n        \"Penetration testing scope documents\",\n        \"Insider decision recording during NCSC exercises\"\n      ],\n      \"correctIndex\": 0,\n      \"explanation\": \"Cyber Streetwise is an awareness campaign for everyday safer behaviour.\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```"},"id":"week6-government-initiatives-source-remainder","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"markdown","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"formative":true,"prompt":"Complete this activity on the learner hub page, then write a short note to confirm you have finished.","questionId":"week6-government-initiatives:learner-note","sourceQuestionId":"learner-note"},"id":"week6-government-initiatives-learner-note","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"reflection","version":"0.1.0"}],"id":"week6-government-initiatives","metadata":{"activityType":"Guided learning","href":null,"runtimeGlobal":"Week6GovernmentInitiatives","status":"available","summary":"Government Cyber Security Initiatives","title":"Government Cyber Security Initiatives"},"relationships":{"assets":[],"assignment":"formative-practice","learningOutcomes":["LO1"],"questions":[]},"schema":"lp.content.activity","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","version":"1.0.0"},{"blocks":[{"content":{"level":2,"text":"NCSC Exercise in a Box Guidance"},"id":"week6-ncsc-guidance-title","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"heading","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"text":"This page is a tutor-facilitated classroom companion only. Follow your tutor and the official NCSC Exercise in a Box materials. Do not invent staged exercise prompts here."},"id":"week6-ncsc-guidance-intro","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"paragraph","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"format":"application/json","text":"```json\n{\n  \"weekNumber\": 6,\n  \"sessionNumber\": 1,\n  \"estimatedMinutes\": 15,\n  \"organisation\": \"Northbank Community Health Partnership\",\n  \"exerciseTitle\": \"Insider threat resulting in a data breach\",\n  \"ncscOverviewUrl\": \"https://www.ncsc.gov.uk/section/exercise-in-a-box/overview\",\n  \"intro\": \"This page is a tutor-facilitated classroom companion only. Follow your tutor and the official NCSC Exercise in a Box materials. Do not invent staged exercise prompts here.\",\n  \"completionNote\": \"Opening the NCSC website does not automatically complete this activity. Completion requires working through the facilitated exercise with your tutor and recording decisions in the companion decision record.\",\n  \"checklist\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"role\",\n      \"label\": \"I am acting as a Northbank stakeholder role assigned by my tutor during the exercise.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"briefing\",\n      \"label\": \"I used the tutor briefing and official NCSC materials rather than invented prompts.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"containment\",\n      \"label\": \"I considered containment steps and who must be informed during the insider threat data breach scenario.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"dimensions\",\n      \"label\": \"I separated legal obligations, ethical choices and operational practicality when discussing responses.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"guidanceSections\": [\n    {\n      \"title\": \"Act as Northbank\",\n      \"text\": \"Use the Northbank Community Health Partnership context. Patient trust and continuity of care should inform decisions.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"Use the briefing\",\n      \"text\": \"Your tutor will provide the exercise briefing. Record only what was discussed in class, not invented incident timelines.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"Containment and notification\",\n      \"text\": \"Consider how Northbank would contain an insider data breach, which roles decide next steps and which stakeholders may need informing under current United Kingdom data protection legislation.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"Legal versus ethical\",\n      \"text\": \"Some actions may be legally required, others ethically desirable but not mandatory, and others operationally difficult. Keep these dimensions separate in discussion.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"Record the basis\",\n      \"text\": \"After the exercise, capture decisions, reasons and evidence still needed in the Exercise Decision Record activity.\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```"},"id":"week6-ncsc-guidance-source-remainder","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"markdown","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"formative":true,"prompt":"Complete this activity on the learner hub page, then write a short note to confirm you have finished.","questionId":"week6-ncsc-guidance:learner-note","sourceQuestionId":"learner-note"},"id":"week6-ncsc-guidance-learner-note","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"reflection","version":"0.1.0"}],"id":"week6-ncsc-guidance","metadata":{"activityType":"Facilitated companion","href":null,"runtimeGlobal":"Week6NcscGuidance","status":"available","summary":"NCSC Exercise in a Box Guidance","title":"NCSC Exercise in a Box Guidance"},"relationships":{"assets":[],"assignment":"formative-practice","learningOutcomes":["LO1"],"questions":[]},"schema":"lp.content.activity","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","version":"1.0.0"},{"blocks":[{"content":{"level":2,"text":"Exercise Decision Record"},"id":"week6-exercise-decision-record-title","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"heading","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"text":"Record decisions made during the tutor-facilitated NCSC Exercise in a Box session. Do not invent exercise prompts or outcomes. Capture what your group actually discussed."},"id":"week6-exercise-decision-record-intro","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"paragraph","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"format":"application/json","text":"```json\n{\n  \"weekNumber\": 6,\n  \"sessionNumber\": 1,\n  \"estimatedMinutes\": 35,\n  \"organisation\": \"Northbank Community Health Partnership\",\n  \"exerciseTitle\": \"Insider threat resulting in a data breach\",\n  \"intro\": \"Record decisions made during the tutor-facilitated NCSC Exercise in a Box session. Do not invent exercise prompts or outcomes. Capture what your group actually discussed.\",\n  \"reviseNote\": \"You may revise entries after the debrief. Update ethical, legal and operational notes as your tutor clarifies the scenario.\",\n  \"decisionTypes\": [\n    \"Legal obligation\",\n    \"Ethical choice\",\n    \"Operational judgement\",\n    \"Combination\"\n  ],\n  \"minDecisions\": 2,\n  \"entryFields\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"title\",\n      \"label\": \"Decision title (short)\",\n      \"rows\": 1\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"decision\",\n      \"label\": \"Decision taken or proposed\",\n      \"rows\": 2\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"reason\",\n      \"label\": \"Reason for the decision\",\n      \"rows\": 2\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"stakeholder\",\n      \"label\": \"Stakeholder affected or responsible\",\n      \"rows\": 1\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"ethical\",\n      \"label\": \"Ethical consideration\",\n      \"rows\": 2\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"legal\",\n      \"label\": \"Legal consideration (name law and duty where relevant)\",\n      \"rows\": 2\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"operational\",\n      \"label\": \"Operational consideration\",\n      \"rows\": 2\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"type\",\n      \"label\": \"Decision type\",\n      \"type\": \"select\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"evidenceNeeded\",\n      \"label\": \"Evidence still needed\",\n      \"rows\": 2\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"reflection\",\n      \"label\": \"Reflection after debrief (optional until debrief)\",\n      \"rows\": 2\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```"},"id":"week6-exercise-decision-record-source-remainder","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"markdown","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"formative":true,"prompt":"Complete this activity on the learner hub page, then write a short note to confirm you have finished.","questionId":"week6-exercise-decision-record:learner-note","sourceQuestionId":"learner-note"},"id":"week6-exercise-decision-record-learner-note","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"reflection","version":"0.1.0"}],"id":"week6-exercise-decision-record","metadata":{"activityType":"Facilitated companion","href":null,"runtimeGlobal":"Week6ExerciseDecisionRecord","status":"available","summary":"Exercise Decision Record","title":"Exercise Decision Record"},"relationships":{"assets":[],"assignment":"formative-practice","learningOutcomes":["LO1"],"questions":[]},"schema":"lp.content.activity","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","version":"1.0.0"},{"blocks":[{"content":{"level":2,"text":"Session 1 Review"},"id":"week6-session1-review-title","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"heading","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"text":"Review Session 1 by distinguishing what the law required, what was ethically appropriate and what was operationally practical during the insider threat exercise and related activities."},"id":"week6-session1-review-intro","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"paragraph","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"correctOptionId":"a","feedback":{"correct":"Statutory data protection duties create legal obligations. Ethics and operations may shape how Northbank meets them, but the duty itself is legal.","incorrect":"Statutory data protection duties create legal obligations. Ethics and operations may shape how Northbank meets them, but the duty itself is legal."},"formative":true,"options":[{"id":"a","label":"Legal obligation"},{"id":"b","label":"Ethical choice only"},{"id":"c","label":"Operational judgement only"},{"id":"d","label":"Neither legal nor operational"}],"prompt":"Northbank must assess and respond to a personal data breach under current United Kingdom data protection legislation. This decision is best classified as:","questionId":"week6-session1-review:r1","sourceQuestionId":"r1","sourceType":"single"},"id":"week6-session1-review-q-1-r1","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"single-choice","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"correctOptionId":"a","feedback":{"correct":"Transparent communication supports ethical practice and operational acceptance. It does not replace legal duties.","incorrect":"Transparent communication supports ethical practice and operational acceptance. It does not replace legal duties."},"formative":true,"options":[{"id":"a","label":"An ethical and operational choice about trust and proportionality"},{"id":"b","label":"A replacement for data protection legislation"},{"id":"c","label":"Unlawful in all circumstances"},{"id":"d","label":"Defined by Cyber Streetwise as a statute"}],"prompt":"Choosing to warn staff about monitoring in a transparent, proportionate way after an insider incident is mainly:","questionId":"week6-session1-review:r2","sourceQuestionId":"r2","sourceType":"single"},"id":"week6-session1-review-q-2-r2","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"single-choice","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"correctOptionId":"a","feedback":{"correct":"Service delay and staff workflow effects are operational considerations, even when the underlying trigger may involve legal or ethical issues.","incorrect":"Service delay and staff workflow effects are operational considerations, even when the underlying trigger may involve legal or ethical issues."},"formative":true,"options":[{"id":"a","label":"Operational practicality and service impact"},{"id":"b","label":"Nation-state motivation"},{"id":"c","label":"Cyber Essentials certification status"},{"id":"d","label":"Responsible disclosure to a vendor"}],"prompt":"Delaying clinic access while Northbank resets compromised accounts reflects which dimension most directly?","questionId":"week6-session1-review:r3","sourceQuestionId":"r3","sourceType":"single"},"id":"week6-session1-review-q-3-r3","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"single-choice","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"format":"application/json","text":"```json\n{\n  \"weekNumber\": 6,\n  \"sessionNumber\": 1,\n  \"estimatedMinutes\": 15,\n  \"intro\": \"Review Session 1 by distinguishing what the law required, what was ethically appropriate and what was operationally practical during the insider threat exercise and related activities.\"\n}\n```"},"id":"week6-session1-review-source-remainder","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"markdown","version":"0.1.0"}],"id":"week6-session1-review","metadata":{"activityType":"Reflection","href":null,"runtimeGlobal":"Week6Session1Review","status":"available","summary":"Session 1 Review","title":"Session 1 Review"},"relationships":{"assets":[],"assignment":"formative-practice","learningOutcomes":["LO1"],"questions":[]},"schema":"lp.content.activity","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","version":"1.0.0"},{"blocks":[{"content":{"level":2,"text":"Legislation Retrieval Quiz"},"id":"week6-legislation-retrieval-title","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"heading","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"correctOptionId":"a","feedback":{"correct":"Unauthorised access to computer material is primarily addressed under the Computer Misuse Act 1990.","incorrect":"Unauthorised access to computer material is primarily addressed under the Computer Misuse Act 1990."},"formative":true,"options":[{"id":"a","label":"Computer Misuse Act 1990"},{"id":"b","label":"Current United Kingdom data protection legislation only"},{"id":"c","label":"Police and Justice Act 2006 only"},{"id":"d","label":"Cyber Essentials certification scheme"}],"prompt":"Which United Kingdom statute creates the main unauthorised access offence for computer systems?","questionId":"week6-legislation-retrieval:lrq1","sourceQuestionId":"lrq1","sourceType":"single"},"id":"week6-legislation-retrieval-q-1-lrq1","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"single-choice","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"correctOptionId":"a","feedback":{"correct":"Processing personal data must comply with current United Kingdom data protection legislation, including lawful purpose and security expectations.","incorrect":"Processing personal data must comply with current United Kingdom data protection legislation, including lawful purpose and security expectations."},"formative":true,"options":[{"id":"a","label":"Current United Kingdom data protection legislation"},{"id":"b","label":"Computer Misuse Act 1990 only, with no data protection role"},{"id":"c","label":"Police and Justice Act 2006 amendments only"},{"id":"d","label":"Ethical codes with no legal force"}],"prompt":"Northbank must explain why patient contact details were accessed without a proper purpose. Which legislation is most directly relevant to that duty?","questionId":"week6-legislation-retrieval:lrq2","sourceQuestionId":"lrq2","sourceType":"single"},"id":"week6-legislation-retrieval-q-2-lrq2","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"single-choice","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"correctOptionId":"a","feedback":{"correct":"The Police and Justice Act 2006 amendments address making, supplying or obtaining articles for use in Computer Misuse Act offences.","incorrect":"The Police and Justice Act 2006 amendments address making, supplying or obtaining articles for use in Computer Misuse Act offences."},"formative":true,"options":[{"id":"a","label":"Police and Justice Act 2006 amendments on supplying tools for misuse"},{"id":"b","label":"Current United Kingdom data protection legislation only"},{"id":"c","label":"Computer Misuse Act 1990 section on patient confidentiality"},{"id":"d","label":"Operational downtime guidance only"}],"prompt":"A supplier offers Northbank a ready-made credential-testing tool marketed for \"checking weak passwords\" without clear authorisation rules. Which amendment area is most relevant?","questionId":"week6-legislation-retrieval:lrq3","sourceQuestionId":"lrq3","sourceType":"single"},"id":"week6-legislation-retrieval-q-3-lrq3","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"single-choice","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"correctOptionId":"a","feedback":{"correct":"Name the statute and the relevant duty or offence together. Unauthorised access fits the Computer Misuse Act 1990.","incorrect":"Name the statute and the relevant duty or offence together. Unauthorised access fits the Computer Misuse Act 1990."},"formative":true,"options":[{"id":"a","label":"Computer Misuse Act 1990: unauthorised access to computer material"},{"id":"b","label":"Current United Kingdom data protection legislation: only marketing consent"},{"id":"c","label":"Police and Justice Act 2006: only physical break-ins"},{"id":"d","label":"Ethics policy: criminal prosecution without further detail"}],"prompt":"Which pairing best links statute to duty for an insider who accesses records they are not authorised to view?","questionId":"week6-legislation-retrieval:lrq4","sourceQuestionId":"lrq4","sourceType":"single"},"id":"week6-legislation-retrieval-q-4-lrq4","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"single-choice","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"correctOptionId":"a","feedback":{"correct":"Security of personal data and accountability sit under current United Kingdom data protection legislation.","incorrect":"Security of personal data and accountability sit under current United Kingdom data protection legislation."},"formative":true,"options":[{"id":"a","label":"Current United Kingdom data protection legislation: appropriate security and accountability for personal data"},{"id":"b","label":"Computer Misuse Act 1990: only external hackers"},{"id":"c","label":"Police and Justice Act 2006: only copyright infringement"},{"id":"d","label":"Operational policy: replaces all legal duties"}],"prompt":"Which pairing best links statute to duty when Northbank fails to protect personal data by inadequate access controls after an insider breach?","questionId":"week6-legislation-retrieval:lrq5","sourceQuestionId":"lrq5","sourceType":"single"},"id":"week6-legislation-retrieval-q-5-lrq5","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"single-choice","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"correctOptionId":"a","feedback":{"correct":"Week 6 requires you to separate moral judgement from legal requirements and from operational constraints.","incorrect":"Week 6 requires you to separate moral judgement from legal requirements and from operational constraints."},"formative":true,"options":[{"id":"a","label":"Ethics and law are related but not identical; legal compliance does not automatically mean an action is ethical"},{"id":"b","label":"If something is legal it is always ethical in a healthcare setting"},{"id":"c","label":"Ethical behaviour never needs to consider operational practicality"},{"id":"d","label":"Only the Computer Misuse Act 1990 defines ethics for Northbank"}],"prompt":"An action may be unethical but still lawful, or unlawful but argued as well-intentioned. Which statement is most accurate?","questionId":"week6-legislation-retrieval:lrq6","sourceQuestionId":"lrq6","sourceType":"single"},"id":"week6-legislation-retrieval-q-6-lrq6","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"single-choice","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"correctOptionId":"a","feedback":{"correct":"Operational considerations include cost, staff time, downtime, usability and productivity trade-offs.","incorrect":"Operational considerations include cost, staff time, downtime, usability and productivity trade-offs."},"formative":true,"options":[{"id":"a","label":"Staff time, usability, trust and lost productivity if controls are disproportionate"},{"id":"b","label":"Only the colour of the monitoring dashboard"},{"id":"c","label":"Whether the attacker used ransomware encryption"},{"id":"d","label":"Replacing all legislation with a single policy sentence"}],"prompt":"Northbank considers continuous keystroke monitoring for all staff after an insider data breach. Which operational consideration is most relevant?","questionId":"week6-legislation-retrieval:lrq7","sourceQuestionId":"lrq7","sourceType":"single"},"id":"week6-legislation-retrieval-q-7-lrq7","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"single-choice","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"correctOptionId":"a","feedback":{"correct":"Different statutes address different duties. Personal data handling also falls under current United Kingdom data protection legislation.","incorrect":"Different statutes address different duties. Personal data handling also falls under current United Kingdom data protection legislation."},"formative":true,"options":[{"id":"a","label":"Data protection duties also apply to how personal data is processed, secured and explained to individuals"},{"id":"b","label":"The Computer Misuse Act 1990 removes all data protection duties"},{"id":"c","label":"Patient contact details are never personal data"},{"id":"d","label":"Operational cost always overrides both statutes"}],"prompt":"Why should Northbank not rely on the Computer Misuse Act 1990 alone when deciding how to handle exposed patient contact details?","questionId":"week6-legislation-retrieval:lrq8","sourceQuestionId":"lrq8","sourceType":"single"},"id":"week6-legislation-retrieval-q-8-lrq8","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"single-choice","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"correctOptionId":"a","feedback":{"correct":"Strong Week 6 answers name legal duties separately from ethical judgement and operational practicality.","incorrect":"Strong Week 6 answers name legal duties separately from ethical judgement and operational practicality."},"formative":true,"options":[{"id":"a","label":"Law sets minimum requirements that can be enforced; ethics asks whether monitoring is fair, proportionate and respectful even where law allows it"},{"id":"b","label":"Ethics and law are identical, so proportionality never matters"},{"id":"c","label":"Legal duties apply only to external attackers"},{"id":"d","label":"Ethical expectations replace the need to name any statute"}],"prompt":"Which answer best distinguishes a legal duty from an ethical expectation for employee monitoring?","questionId":"week6-legislation-retrieval:lrq9","sourceQuestionId":"lrq9","sourceType":"single"},"id":"week6-legislation-retrieval-q-9-lrq9","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"single-choice","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"correctOptionId":"a","feedback":{"correct":"Exam-style answers need statute linked to duty, ethical proportionality and operational trade-offs, not vague fear-based conclusions.","incorrect":"Exam-style answers need statute linked to duty, ethical proportionality and operational trade-offs, not vague fear-based conclusions."},"formative":true,"options":[{"id":"a","label":"It jumps to an operational choice without linking statute, duty, ethics or stakeholder impact"},{"id":"b","label":"It names the Computer Misuse Act 1990 too precisely"},{"id":"c","label":"It includes too much evidence from the insider breach scenario"},{"id":"d","label":"It balances competing considerations before concluding"}],"prompt":"A learner writes: \"Northbank should monitor everyone heavily because hackers exist.\" What is the main weakness?","questionId":"week6-legislation-retrieval:lrq10","sourceQuestionId":"lrq10","sourceType":"single"},"id":"week6-legislation-retrieval-q-10-lrq10","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"single-choice","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"format":"application/json","text":"```json\n{\n  \"weekNumber\": 6,\n  \"sessionNumber\": 2,\n  \"estimatedMinutes\": 15\n}\n```"},"id":"week6-legislation-retrieval-source-remainder","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"markdown","version":"0.1.0"}],"id":"week6-legislation-retrieval","metadata":{"activityType":"Retrieval quiz","href":null,"runtimeGlobal":"Week6LegislationRetrieval","status":"available","summary":"Legislation Retrieval Quiz","title":"Legislation Retrieval Quiz"},"relationships":{"assets":[],"assignment":"formative-practice","learningOutcomes":["LO1"],"questions":[]},"schema":"lp.content.activity","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","version":"1.0.0"},{"blocks":[{"content":{"level":2,"text":"Northbank Employee Monitoring Scenario"},"id":"week6-employee-monitoring-title","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"heading","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"format":"application/json","text":"```json\n{\n  \"weekNumber\": 6,\n  \"sessionNumber\": 2,\n  \"estimatedMinutes\": 30,\n  \"scenario\": \"Northbank Community Health Partnership discovers that a member of staff copied patient contact details to a personal device before leaving the organisation. The breach is contained, but senior managers ask how far Northbank should monitor employees to prevent repeat insider misuse. Options discussed include enhanced log review, mailbox auditing, workstation monitoring and clearer acceptable-use rules. No decision is made in this activity: you prepare one stakeholder position for debate.\",\n  \"instructions\": \"Select one stakeholder role and prepare a position for classroom debate. Use the ethical, legal and operational prompts. Do not treat your answer as the final organisational decision.\",\n  \"stakeholderRoles\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"employees\",\n      \"label\": \"Employees\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"managers\",\n      \"label\": \"Managers\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"customers\",\n      \"label\": \"Customers\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"regulator\",\n      \"label\": \"The data protection regulator\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"shareholders\",\n      \"label\": \"Shareholders\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"promptGroups\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"ethical\",\n      \"label\": \"Ethical prompts\",\n      \"questions\": [\n        \"Is the proposed monitoring fair and proportionate for this stakeholder?\",\n        \"What trust or dignity concerns arise?\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"legal\",\n      \"label\": \"Legal prompts\",\n      \"questions\": [\n        \"Which statute and duty are most relevant (Computer Misuse Act 1990, current United Kingdom data protection legislation, or Police and Justice Act 2006 amendments where tools are supplied)?\",\n        \"What lawful basis or transparency might employees and customers expect?\"\n      ]\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"operational\",\n      \"label\": \"Operational prompts\",\n      \"questions\": [\n        \"What staff time, usability or productivity effects could monitoring create?\",\n        \"Could monitoring reduce repeat insider risk without harming day-to-day care delivery?\"\n      ]\n    }\n  ],\n  \"fields\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"mainArgument\",\n      \"label\": \"Main argument from your stakeholder role\",\n      \"minLength\": 30\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"evidence\",\n      \"label\": \"Evidence from the Northbank insider breach scenario\",\n      \"minLength\": 20\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"opposingArgument\",\n      \"label\": \"Strongest opposing argument another stakeholder might raise\",\n      \"minLength\": 20\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"hardestOpposing\",\n      \"label\": \"Hardest opposing point for your role to answer\",\n      \"minLength\": 15\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"recommendation\",\n      \"label\": \"Recommendation your role would advance in debate (not the final Northbank decision)\",\n      \"minLength\": 25\n    }\n  ],\n  \"sentenceStarters\": [\n    \"From the perspective of [stakeholder]\u2026\",\n    \"The scenario shows that\u2026\",\n    \"Under current United Kingdom data protection legislation\u2026\",\n    \"Ethically, the concern is\u2026\",\n    \"Operationally, Northbank would need to\u2026\"\n  ]\n}\n```"},"id":"week6-employee-monitoring-source-remainder","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"markdown","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"formative":true,"prompt":"Complete this activity on the learner hub page, then write a short note to confirm you have finished.","questionId":"week6-employee-monitoring:learner-note","sourceQuestionId":"learner-note"},"id":"week6-employee-monitoring-learner-note","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"reflection","version":"0.1.0"}],"id":"week6-employee-monitoring","metadata":{"activityType":"Scenario analysis","href":null,"runtimeGlobal":"Week6EmployeeMonitoring","status":"available","summary":"Northbank Employee Monitoring Scenario","title":"Northbank Employee Monitoring Scenario"},"relationships":{"assets":[],"assignment":"formative-practice","learningOutcomes":["LO1"],"questions":[]},"schema":"lp.content.activity","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","version":"1.0.0"},{"blocks":[{"content":{"level":2,"text":"Stakeholder Debate Preparation"},"id":"week6-stakeholder-debate-title","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"heading","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"format":"application/json","text":"```json\n{\n  \"weekNumber\": 6,\n  \"sessionNumber\": 2,\n  \"estimatedMinutes\": 35,\n  \"scenario\": \"Northbank Community Health Partnership is debating how far to monitor staff after an insider copied patient contact details. Your group prepares structured arguments for a classroom debate. Completion checks field presence, not automatic quality scoring.\",\n  \"participationRoles\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"speaker\",\n      \"label\": \"Speaker\",\n      \"description\": \"Presents the opening position and responds to challenges.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"recorder\",\n      \"label\": \"Recorder\",\n      \"description\": \"Captures arguments, evidence and concessions accurately.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"evidence-checker\",\n      \"label\": \"Evidence checker\",\n      \"description\": \"Checks that claims link to the scenario and named legislation where relevant.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"stakeholderRoles\": [\n    \"Employees\",\n    \"Managers\",\n    \"Customers\",\n    \"The data protection regulator\",\n    \"Shareholders\"\n  ],\n  \"fields\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"role\",\n      \"label\": \"Stakeholder role you are representing\",\n      \"minLength\": 3\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"opening\",\n      \"label\": \"Opening position\",\n      \"minLength\": 20\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"ethical\",\n      \"label\": \"Ethical argument (what ought to be done)\",\n      \"minLength\": 20\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"legal\",\n      \"label\": \"Legal argument (name legislation and the relevant duty or offence where you can)\",\n      \"minLength\": 20\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"operational\",\n      \"label\": \"Operational argument (cost, staff time, usability or productivity)\",\n      \"minLength\": 20\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"opposing\",\n      \"label\": \"Opposing argument you expect from another stakeholder\",\n      \"minLength\": 15\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"response\",\n      \"label\": \"Response to the opposing argument\",\n      \"minLength\": 15\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"concession\",\n      \"label\": \"Concession: one fair point from the other side\",\n      \"minLength\": 12\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"recommendation\",\n      \"label\": \"Final recommendation your role would advance (debate outcome, not hub decision)\",\n      \"minLength\": 20\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```"},"id":"week6-stakeholder-debate-source-remainder","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"markdown","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"formative":true,"prompt":"Complete this activity on the learner hub page, then write a short note to confirm you have finished.","questionId":"week6-stakeholder-debate:learner-note","sourceQuestionId":"learner-note"},"id":"week6-stakeholder-debate-learner-note","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"reflection","version":"0.1.0"}],"id":"week6-stakeholder-debate","metadata":{"activityType":"Debate preparation","href":null,"runtimeGlobal":"Week6StakeholderDebate","status":"available","summary":"Stakeholder Debate Preparation","title":"Stakeholder Debate Preparation"},"relationships":{"assets":[],"assignment":"formative-practice","learningOutcomes":["LO1"],"questions":[]},"schema":"lp.content.activity","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","version":"1.0.0"},{"blocks":[{"content":{"level":2,"text":"Balanced Discuss Response Learning"},"id":"week6-discuss-learning-title","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"heading","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"format":"application/json","text":"```json\n{\n  \"weekNumber\": 6,\n  \"sessionNumber\": 2,\n  \"estimatedMinutes\": 25,\n  \"structure\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"issue\",\n      \"label\": \"Issue\",\n      \"description\": \"State the decision or tension clearly.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"supported\",\n      \"label\": \"Supported consideration\",\n      \"description\": \"One reason or evidence supporting a position, linked to the scenario.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"competing\",\n      \"label\": \"Competing consideration\",\n      \"description\": \"A credible counterpoint from another stakeholder or duty.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"concession\",\n      \"label\": \"Concession\",\n      \"description\": \"A fair point accepted from the other side before concluding.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"conclusion\",\n      \"label\": \"Justified conclusion\",\n      \"description\": \"A balanced judgement that follows from both sides, not a one-sided slogan.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"scenario\": \"Northbank Community Health Partnership must decide how far to monitor employees after an insider copied patient contact details. A Discuss question asks whether enhanced monitoring is justified.\",\n  \"weakResponse\": {\n    \"label\": \"Weaker Discuss-style response\",\n    \"text\": \"Northbank should monitor everyone all the time because insiders are dangerous and the law probably requires it. Monitoring is always ethical if it stops breaches. Any staff who object are hiding something.\",\n    \"problems\": [\n      \"Does not state the issue as a balanced decision\",\n      \"Treats legal, ethical and operational points as one vague claim\",\n      \"No competing consideration or concession\",\n      \"Conclusion is one-sided and not justified from evidence\"\n    ]\n  },\n  \"strongResponse\": {\n    \"label\": \"Stronger balanced response\",\n    \"text\": \"The issue is how far Northbank should monitor staff after an insider copied patient contact details. Enhanced log review may be supported because it could deter repeat misuse and show accountability to customers and the data protection regulator under current United Kingdom data protection legislation. However, employees may argue that continuous monitoring damages trust and adds operational burden if clinic staff fear excessive scrutiny during busy appointments. I accept that some targeted auditing of access to sensitive records is more proportionate than blanket surveillance. Overall, Northbank should favour targeted, transparent monitoring with clear rules rather than unlimited observation, because this balances security with ethical respect for staff and workable day-to-day care delivery.\",\n    \"strengths\": [\n      \"States the issue clearly\",\n      \"Develops a supported consideration with scenario and legal link\",\n      \"Includes a competing stakeholder view\",\n      \"Makes an explicit concession\",\n      \"Concludes with a justified, balanced judgement rather than length alone\"\n    ]\n  },\n  \"knowledgeChecks\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"kc1\",\n      \"prompt\": \"Which element is missing from the weaker response?\",\n      \"options\": [\n        \"A competing consideration and concession\",\n        \"The word Northbank\",\n        \"Any mention of employees\",\n        \"A longer conclusion only\"\n      ],\n      \"correctIndex\": 0,\n      \"explanation\": \"Balanced Discuss answers need a credible counterpoint and a concession, not just a longer one-sided paragraph.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"kc2\",\n      \"prompt\": \"Why is the stronger response better even though both mention monitoring?\",\n      \"options\": [\n        \"It balances supported and competing points before a justified conclusion\",\n        \"It avoids naming any stakeholder\",\n        \"It claims legal compliance removes all ethical doubt\",\n        \"It is better only because it is longer\"\n      ],\n      \"correctIndex\": 0,\n      \"explanation\": \"Balance and structure earn credit, not word count alone.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"kc3\",\n      \"prompt\": \"Where does the stronger response link statute to duty?\",\n      \"options\": [\n        \"Accountability to customers and the data protection regulator under current United Kingdom data protection legislation\",\n        \"Police and Justice Act 2006 amendments on marketing emails only\",\n        \"Computer Misuse Act 1990 removing all privacy rights\",\n        \"It does not mention law at all\"\n      ],\n      \"correctIndex\": 0,\n      \"explanation\": \"Name the statute and the relevant duty or expectation together.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"kc4\",\n      \"prompt\": \"Which line best shows a concession?\",\n      \"options\": [\n        \"I accept that some targeted auditing of access to sensitive records is more proportionate than blanket surveillance.\",\n        \"Monitoring is always right and opponents are wrong.\",\n        \"The law is irrelevant to Northbank.\",\n        \"Operational costs never matter.\"\n      ],\n      \"correctIndex\": 0,\n      \"explanation\": \"A concession fairly accepts a point from the other side.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"kc5\",\n      \"prompt\": \"What should a justified conclusion do?\",\n      \"options\": [\n        \"Follow from both sides of the argument and state a reasoned overall judgement\",\n        \"Repeat the supported point only\",\n        \"Introduce a new unrelated statute\",\n        \"Ignore operational practicality entirely\"\n      ],\n      \"correctIndex\": 0,\n      \"explanation\": \"The conclusion should weigh the supported and competing considerations after the concession.\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```"},"id":"week6-discuss-learning-source-remainder","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"markdown","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"formative":true,"prompt":"Complete this activity on the learner hub page, then write a short note to confirm you have finished.","questionId":"week6-discuss-learning:learner-note","sourceQuestionId":"learner-note"},"id":"week6-discuss-learning-learner-note","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"reflection","version":"0.1.0"}],"id":"week6-discuss-learning","metadata":{"activityType":"Exam skills","href":null,"runtimeGlobal":"Week6DiscussLearning","status":"available","summary":"Balanced Discuss Response Learning","title":"Balanced Discuss Response Learning"},"relationships":{"assets":[],"assignment":"formative-practice","learningOutcomes":["LO1"],"questions":[]},"schema":"lp.content.activity","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","version":"1.0.0"},{"blocks":[{"content":{"level":2,"text":"Discuss Response Planner"},"id":"week6-discuss-planner-title","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"heading","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"format":"application/json","text":"```json\n{\n  \"weekNumber\": 6,\n  \"sessionNumber\": 2,\n  \"estimatedMinutes\": 25,\n  \"scenario\": \"Plan a balanced Discuss answer on how far Northbank Community Health Partnership should monitor employees after an insider copied patient contact details.\",\n  \"issuePrompt\": \"State the issue: what decision or tension must Northbank address?\",\n  \"columns\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"supporting\",\n      \"label\": \"Supporting argument\",\n      \"description\": \"Reasons, evidence or duties supporting one side of the monitoring debate.\",\n      \"minLength\": 30\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"competing\",\n      \"label\": \"Competing consideration\",\n      \"description\": \"Credible counterarguments from another stakeholder or operational concern.\",\n      \"minLength\": 30\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"concessionConclusion\",\n      \"label\": \"Concession and justified conclusion\",\n      \"description\": \"Start with a clearly labelled concession, then state your balanced overall judgement.\",\n      \"minLength\": 40,\n      \"requiresConcessionLabel\": true\n    }\n  ],\n  \"concessionLabel\": \"Concession:\",\n  \"sentenceStarters\": [\n    \"The issue is whether\u2026\",\n    \"One supported reason is\u2026\",\n    \"However, from the perspective of employees/customers\u2026\",\n    \"Concession: I accept that\u2026\",\n    \"Overall, Northbank should\u2026 because\u2026\"\n  ]\n}\n```"},"id":"week6-discuss-planner-source-remainder","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"markdown","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"formative":true,"prompt":"Complete this activity on the learner hub page, then write a short note to confirm you have finished.","questionId":"week6-discuss-planner:learner-note","sourceQuestionId":"learner-note"},"id":"week6-discuss-planner-learner-note","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"reflection","version":"0.1.0"}],"id":"week6-discuss-planner","metadata":{"activityType":"Exam skills","href":null,"runtimeGlobal":"Week6DiscussPlanner","status":"available","summary":"Discuss Response Planner","title":"Discuss Response Planner"},"relationships":{"assets":[],"assignment":"formative-practice","learningOutcomes":["LO1"],"questions":[]},"schema":"lp.content.activity","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","version":"1.0.0"},{"blocks":[{"content":{"level":2,"text":"OCR-Style Timed Questions"},"id":"week6-ocr-question-practice-title","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"heading","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"commandWord":"Identify","correctOptionId":"a","feedback":{"correct":"","incorrect":""},"formative":true,"marks":1,"options":[{"id":"a","label":"Computer Misuse Act 1990"},{"id":"b","label":"Current United Kingdom data protection legislation only"},{"id":"c","label":"Police and Justice Act 2006 amendments only"},{"id":"d","label":"Cyber Essentials"}],"prompt":"Identify which United Kingdom statute is most directly associated with unauthorised access to computer material.","questionId":"week6-ocr-question-practice:ocr6-1","sourceQuestionId":"ocr6-1","sourceType":"single"},"id":"week6-ocr-question-practice-q-1-ocr6-1","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"single-choice","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"commandWord":"Identify","correctOptionId":"a","feedback":{"correct":"","incorrect":""},"formative":true,"marks":1,"options":[{"id":"a","label":"Current United Kingdom data protection legislation"},{"id":"b","label":"Computer Misuse Act 1990 only"},{"id":"c","label":"Police and Justice Act 2006 amendments only"},{"id":"d","label":"No legislation applies to contact details"}],"prompt":"Identify which legislation is most directly relevant to securing patient contact details after an insider breach.","questionId":"week6-ocr-question-practice:ocr6-2","sourceQuestionId":"ocr6-2","sourceType":"single"},"id":"week6-ocr-question-practice-q-2-ocr6-2","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"single-choice","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"commandWord":"Describe","correctOptionId":"","feedback":{"correct":"","incorrect":""},"formative":true,"marks":2,"options":[],"prompt":"Describe one ethical concern employees might raise about enhanced monitoring at Northbank.","questionId":"week6-ocr-question-practice:ocr6-3","sourceQuestionId":"ocr6-3","sourceType":"single"},"id":"week6-ocr-question-practice-q-3-ocr6-3","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"single-choice","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"commandWord":"Describe","correctOptionId":"","feedback":{"correct":"","incorrect":""},"formative":true,"marks":2,"options":[],"prompt":"Describe one operational consideration Northbank must weigh before expanding monitoring.","questionId":"week6-ocr-question-practice:ocr6-4","sourceQuestionId":"ocr6-4","sourceType":"single"},"id":"week6-ocr-question-practice-q-4-ocr6-4","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"single-choice","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"commandWord":"Explain","correctOptionId":"","feedback":{"correct":"","incorrect":""},"formative":true,"marks":3,"options":[],"prompt":"Explain why the insider copying patient contact details may engage both the Computer Misuse Act 1990 and current United Kingdom data protection legislation.","questionId":"week6-ocr-question-practice:ocr6-5","sourceQuestionId":"ocr6-5","sourceType":"single"},"id":"week6-ocr-question-practice-q-5-ocr6-5","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"single-choice","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"commandWord":"Explain","correctOptionId":"","feedback":{"correct":"","incorrect":""},"formative":true,"marks":4,"options":[],"prompt":"Explain why legal compliance alone may not settle whether enhanced employee monitoring is ethical at Northbank.","questionId":"week6-ocr-question-practice:ocr6-6","sourceQuestionId":"ocr6-6","sourceType":"single"},"id":"week6-ocr-question-practice-q-6-ocr6-6","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"single-choice","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"commandWord":"Discuss","correctOptionId":"","feedback":{"correct":"","incorrect":""},"formative":true,"marks":7,"options":[],"prompt":"Discuss how far Northbank Community Health Partnership should monitor employees after the insider data breach.","questionId":"week6-ocr-question-practice:ocr6-7","sourceQuestionId":"ocr6-7","sourceType":"single"},"id":"week6-ocr-question-practice-q-7-ocr6-7","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"single-choice","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"format":"application/json","text":"```json\n{\n  \"weekNumber\": 6,\n  \"sessionNumber\": 2,\n  \"suggestedMinutes\": 25,\n  \"timingGuidance\": \"Use approximately one minute per mark where this helps you manage time. These are OCR-style practice questions, not official OCR examination questions.\",\n  \"beforeReminders\": [\n    \"Name statutes with duties or offences together where law is required.\",\n    \"Separate ethical, legal and operational points.\",\n    \"Use Northbank scenario evidence - do not import unrelated incidents.\",\n    \"Discuss questions need a competing consideration, concession and justified conclusion.\",\n    \"Mark schemes stay hidden until you submit.\"\n  ],\n  \"northbankScenario\": \"Northbank Community Health Partnership discovers that a member of staff copied patient contact details to a personal device before leaving. Managers consider enhanced log review, mailbox auditing and workstation monitoring. Patients ask what is being done to protect their data. The data protection regulator expects a clear explanation. Staff worry about trust and extra workload. Shareholders want assurance that repeat insider misuse is unlikely without harming care delivery.\"\n}\n```"},"id":"week6-ocr-question-practice-source-remainder","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"markdown","version":"0.1.0"}],"id":"week6-ocr-question-practice","metadata":{"activityType":"Exam skills","href":null,"runtimeGlobal":"Week6OcrPractice","status":"available","summary":"OCR-Style Timed Questions","title":"OCR-Style Timed Questions"},"relationships":{"assets":[],"assignment":"formative-practice","learningOutcomes":["LO1"],"questions":[]},"schema":"lp.content.activity","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","version":"1.0.0"},{"blocks":[{"content":{"level":2,"text":"Marking and Answer Improvement"},"id":"week6-answer-improvement-title","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"heading","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"format":"application/json","text":"```json\n{\n  \"weekNumber\": 6,\n  \"sessionNumber\": 2,\n  \"estimatedMinutes\": 25,\n  \"commonError\": \"Treating ethical language as if it were the same as legal duty, or naming a statute without the relevant duty or offence.\",\n  \"question\": {\n    \"commandWord\": \"Discuss\",\n    \"marks\": 7,\n    \"prompt\": \"Discuss how far Northbank Community Health Partnership should monitor employees after an insider copied patient contact details.\"\n  },\n  \"sampleResponse\": {\n    \"text\": \"Monitoring is ethical because staff should be honest. The Computer Misuse Act 1990 means Northbank can do whatever monitoring it wants. Customers might worry but monitoring fixes everything. Therefore Northbank should monitor all staff heavily.\"\n  },\n  \"dominantIssues\": [\n    \"Uses moral language without separating ethics from law\",\n    \"Names the Computer Misuse Act 1990 without linking a specific duty or offence\",\n    \"No competing consideration from employees or other stakeholders\",\n    \"No concession before the conclusion\",\n    \"Conclusion is one-sided and not justified from the argument\"\n  ],\n  \"markSchemePoints\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"c1\",\n      \"label\": \"Responds to the command word (Discuss: balanced argument)\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"c2\",\n      \"label\": \"Names statute and duty together where law is used\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"c3\",\n      \"label\": \"Separates moral judgement from legal requirement\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"c4\",\n      \"label\": \"Includes a competing consideration\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"c5\",\n      \"label\": \"Includes a justified conclusion after weighing both sides\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"rewritePrompt\": \"Rewrite the weakest sentence so it separates ethical and legal points and links any statute to a duty or offence.\",\n  \"improvePrompt\": \"Improve the full response: add a competing consideration, a labelled concession and a balanced conclusion using Northbank scenario evidence.\",\n  \"nextActionPrompt\": \"One next-exam action you will take when you see a Discuss question on ethical, legal and operational considerations.\",\n  \"modelAfterSubmit\": \"Stronger answers state the issue, link current United Kingdom data protection legislation to security and accountability, treat the Computer Misuse Act 1990 as relevant to unauthorised access, accept that employees may raise proportionality concerns, and conclude with targeted transparent monitoring rather than unlimited surveillance.\"\n}\n```"},"id":"week6-answer-improvement-source-remainder","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"markdown","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"formative":true,"prompt":"Complete this activity on the learner hub page, then write a short note to confirm you have finished.","questionId":"week6-answer-improvement:learner-note","sourceQuestionId":"learner-note"},"id":"week6-answer-improvement-learner-note","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"reflection","version":"0.1.0"}],"id":"week6-answer-improvement","metadata":{"activityType":"Self marking","href":null,"runtimeGlobal":"Week6AnswerImprovement","status":"available","summary":"Marking and Answer Improvement","title":"Marking and Answer Improvement"},"relationships":{"assets":[],"assignment":"formative-practice","learningOutcomes":["LO1"],"questions":[]},"schema":"lp.content.activity","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","version":"1.0.0"},{"blocks":[{"content":{"level":2,"text":"LO2 Revision Organiser"},"id":"week6-revision-organiser-title","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"heading","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"level":3,"text":"Threats"},"id":"week6-revision-organiser-2-1-h","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"heading","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"level":3,"text":"Vulnerabilities and types of attackers"},"id":"week6-revision-organiser-2-2-h","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"heading","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"level":3,"text":"Motivations"},"id":"week6-revision-organiser-2-3-h","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"heading","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"level":3,"text":"Targets"},"id":"week6-revision-organiser-2-4-h","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"heading","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"level":3,"text":"Impacts"},"id":"week6-revision-organiser-2-5-h","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"heading","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"level":3,"text":"Other considerations (ethical, legal, operational, government initiatives)"},"id":"week6-revision-organiser-2-6-h","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"heading","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"format":"application/json","text":"```json\n{\n  \"weekNumber\": 6,\n  \"sessionNumber\": 2,\n  \"estimatedMinutes\": 30,\n  \"diagnosticDraftKey\": \"lo2-diagnostic\",\n  \"weakestFields\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"weakest1\",\n      \"label\": \"Weakest LO2 topic 1 (from diagnostic if available)\",\n      \"minLength\": 5\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"weakest2\",\n      \"label\": \"Weakest LO2 topic 2 (from diagnostic if available)\",\n      \"minLength\": 5\n    }\n  ],\n  \"priorityFields\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"priority1\",\n      \"label\": \"Revision priority 1 for the next study session\",\n      \"minLength\": 15\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"priority2\",\n      \"label\": \"Revision priority 2 for the next study session\",\n      \"minLength\": 15\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```"},"id":"week6-revision-organiser-source-remainder","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"markdown","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"formative":true,"prompt":"Complete this activity on the learner hub page, then write a short note to confirm you have finished.","questionId":"week6-revision-organiser:learner-note","sourceQuestionId":"learner-note"},"id":"week6-revision-organiser-learner-note","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"reflection","version":"0.1.0"}],"id":"week6-revision-organiser","metadata":{"activityType":"Revision","href":null,"runtimeGlobal":"Week6RevisionOrganiser","status":"available","summary":"LO2 Revision Organiser","title":"LO2 Revision Organiser"},"relationships":{"assets":[],"assignment":"formative-practice","learningOutcomes":["LO1"],"questions":[]},"schema":"lp.content.activity","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","version":"1.0.0"},{"blocks":[{"content":{"level":2,"text":"Session 1 Retrieval and Prior Learning"},"id":"week7-session1-retrieval-title","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"heading","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"text":"Recall Cyber Essentials from Week 6, separate threat from vulnerability, and think about how Northbank should prioritise funding. Risk is not the same as threat, and threat is not the same as vulnerability."},"id":"week7-session1-retrieval-intro","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"paragraph","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"correctOptionId":"a","feedback":{"correct":"Cyber Essentials is a government-backed assurance scheme focused on basic technical controls. It is not a criminal statute.","incorrect":"Cyber Essentials is a government-backed assurance scheme focused on basic technical controls. It is not a criminal statute."},"formative":true,"options":[{"id":"a","label":"A government assurance scheme that helps organisations implement basic technical controls against common cyber attacks"},{"id":"b","label":"A United Kingdom criminal statute that creates hacking offences"},{"id":"c","label":"An NCSC exercise pack that replaces risk assessment"},{"id":"d","label":"A penetration testing methodology required by law for all NHS partners"}],"prompt":"What is the main purpose of Cyber Essentials?","questionId":"week7-session1-retrieval:s1r-1","sourceQuestionId":"s1r-1","sourceType":"single"},"id":"week7-session1-retrieval-q-1-s1r-1","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"single-choice","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"correctOptionId":"a","feedback":{"correct":"Threats are potential causes of harm. Vulnerabilities are weaknesses. Risk then weighs likelihood and impact if a threat exploits a vulnerability.","incorrect":"Threats are potential causes of harm. Vulnerabilities are weaknesses. Risk then weighs likelihood and impact if a threat exploits a vulnerability."},"formative":true,"options":[{"id":"a","label":"A threat is a potential cause of harm; a vulnerability is a weakness that could be exploited"},{"id":"b","label":"A threat and a vulnerability are the same thing described in different words"},{"id":"c","label":"A vulnerability is always an external attacker; a threat is always a software bug"},{"id":"d","label":"Risk, threat and vulnerability all mean the chance that an attack will succeed"}],"prompt":"Which statement correctly separates threat and vulnerability?","questionId":"week7-session1-retrieval:s1r-2","sourceQuestionId":"s1r-2","sourceType":"single"},"id":"week7-session1-retrieval-q-2-s1r-2","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"single-choice","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"correctOptionId":"a","feedback":{"correct":"Risk combines likelihood and impact. Naming a threat alone is not a full risk assessment.","incorrect":"Risk combines likelihood and impact. Naming a threat alone is not a full risk assessment."},"formative":true,"options":[{"id":"a","label":"Risk is an assessment of likelihood and impact if a threat exploits a vulnerability"},{"id":"b","label":"Risk is another word for an attacker"},{"id":"c","label":"Risk only means the financial cost of buying a firewall"},{"id":"d","label":"Risk is identical to listing every possible threat name"}],"prompt":"Which statement about risk is most accurate?","questionId":"week7-session1-retrieval:s1r-3","sourceQuestionId":"s1r-3","sourceType":"single"},"id":"week7-session1-retrieval-q-3-s1r-3","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"single-choice","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"correctOptionId":"a","feedback":{"correct":"Prioritise where likelihood and impact are both high, especially for systems that hold or affect patient care data.","incorrect":"Prioritise where likelihood and impact are both high, especially for systems that hold or affect patient care data."},"formative":true,"options":[{"id":"a","label":"A high-likelihood, high-impact weakness affecting patient appointment and clinical records systems"},{"id":"b","label":"A purely cosmetic interface issue on a public leaflet PDF with no data exposure"},{"id":"c","label":"Any vulnerability that is easiest to describe in one sentence, regardless of impact"},{"id":"d","label":"Only vulnerabilities that have already caused a confirmed breach elsewhere in the country"}],"prompt":"Northbank has limited funding. Which vulnerability should usually be considered for funding first?","questionId":"week7-session1-retrieval:s1r-4","sourceQuestionId":"s1r-4","sourceType":"single"},"id":"week7-session1-retrieval-q-4-s1r-4","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"single-choice","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"format":"application/json","text":"```json\n{\n  \"weekNumber\": 7,\n  \"sessionNumber\": 1,\n  \"estimatedMinutes\": 15,\n  \"intro\": \"Recall Cyber Essentials from Week 6, separate threat from vulnerability, and think about how Northbank should prioritise funding. Risk is not the same as threat, and threat is not the same as vulnerability.\",\n  \"misconceptions\": [\n    \"Risk is not the same as threat. Risk combines likelihood and impact for a vulnerability exploited by a threat.\",\n    \"Threat is not the same as vulnerability. A threat is a potential cause of harm; a vulnerability is a weakness that can be exploited.\"\n  ],\n  \"reflections\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"fund-reason\",\n      \"label\": \"In your own words, explain briefly why the vulnerability you would fund first deserves priority at Northbank.\",\n      \"minChars\": 40,\n      \"marks\": 1,\n      \"starter\": \"I would fund this first because the likelihood and impact are\u2026 and patient care could be affected if\u2026\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"threat-vuln\",\n      \"label\": \"Give one Northbank example that shows the difference between a threat and a vulnerability (do not treat them as the same term).\",\n      \"minChars\": 40,\n      \"marks\": 1,\n      \"starter\": \"Threat: \u2026 could try to\u2026 Vulnerability: \u2026 is weak because\u2026\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```"},"id":"week7-session1-retrieval-source-remainder","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"markdown","version":"0.1.0"}],"id":"week7-session1-retrieval","metadata":{"activityType":"Retrieval","href":null,"runtimeGlobal":"Week7Session1Retrieval","status":"available","summary":"Session 1 Retrieval and Prior Learning","title":"Session 1 Retrieval and Prior Learning"},"relationships":{"assets":[],"assignment":"formative-practice","learningOutcomes":["LO1"],"questions":[]},"schema":"lp.content.activity","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","version":"1.0.0"},{"blocks":[{"content":{"level":2,"text":"Cyber Security Risk Management Learning"},"id":"week7-risk-management-learning-title","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"heading","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"correctOptionId":"a","feedback":{"correct":"Start by identifying assets so later judgements are anchored to what matters.","incorrect":"Start by identifying assets so later judgements are anchored to what matters."},"formative":true,"options":[{"id":"a","label":"Identify assets"},{"id":"b","label":"Decide treatment"},{"id":"c","label":"Review effectiveness measure"},{"id":"d","label":"Analyse impact before naming any asset"}],"prompt":"Which stage comes first in the risk-management sequence used here?","questionId":"week7-risk-management-learning:rm-1","sourceQuestionId":"rm-1","sourceType":"single"},"id":"week7-risk-management-learning-q-1-rm-1","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"single-choice","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"correctOptionId":"a","feedback":{"correct":"Phishing is a threat. Weak passwords or missing MFA would be related vulnerabilities.","incorrect":"Phishing is a threat. Weak passwords or missing MFA would be related vulnerabilities."},"formative":true,"options":[{"id":"a","label":"Threat (potential cause of harm)"},{"id":"b","label":"Vulnerability (the weakness itself)"},{"id":"c","label":"Risk score without likelihood or impact"},{"id":"d","label":"Effectiveness measure"}],"prompt":"Phishing emails targeting Northbank staff are best described as a:","questionId":"week7-risk-management-learning:rm-2","sourceQuestionId":"rm-2","sourceType":"single"},"id":"week7-risk-management-learning-q-2-rm-2","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"single-choice","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"correctOptionId":"a","feedback":{"correct":"Accept is a reasoned choice when further spend is disproportionate, typically for lower impact or lower overall risk.","incorrect":"Accept is a reasoned choice when further spend is disproportionate, typically for lower impact or lower overall risk."},"formative":true,"options":[{"id":"a","label":"When the cost of further control is disproportionate to a lower-rated risk"},{"id":"b","label":"Whenever a risk sounds technical"},{"id":"c","label":"Only when the organisation wants to ignore patient confidentiality"},{"id":"d","label":"Never; every risk must be fully mitigated"}],"prompt":"When is Accept an appropriate treatment in this unit?","questionId":"week7-risk-management-learning:rm-3","sourceQuestionId":"rm-3","sourceType":"single"},"id":"week7-risk-management-learning-q-3-rm-3","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"single-choice","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"correctOptionId":"a","feedback":{"correct":"Low-impact information-only disruption can be accepted when mitigation cost is disproportionate.","incorrect":"Low-impact information-only disruption can be accepted when mitigation cost is disproportionate."},"formative":true,"options":[{"id":"a","label":"Temporary unavailability of a public leaflet PDF with no effect on care systems"},{"id":"b","label":"High-likelihood exposure of clinical notes with no compensating control"},{"id":"c","label":"Confirmed ransomware on the appointment system"},{"id":"d","label":"Any risk labelled High on the register"}],"prompt":"Which Northbank example is a rational candidate for Accept?","questionId":"week7-risk-management-learning:rm-4","sourceQuestionId":"rm-4","sourceType":"single"},"id":"week7-risk-management-learning-q-4-rm-4","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"single-choice","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"correctOptionId":"a","feedback":{"correct":"Effectiveness needs an observable indicator of reduced likelihood or impact, not only installation.","incorrect":"Effectiveness needs an observable indicator of reduced likelihood or impact, not only installation."},"formative":true,"options":[{"id":"a","label":"It does not show whether risk actually reduced"},{"id":"b","label":"Antivirus can never be mentioned in cyber security"},{"id":"c","label":"Installation always proves High risk remains"},{"id":"d","label":"Effectiveness measures are illegal to record"}],"prompt":"\u201cWe installed antivirus\u201d alone is a weak effectiveness measure because:","questionId":"week7-risk-management-learning:rm-5","sourceQuestionId":"rm-5","sourceType":"single"},"id":"week7-risk-management-learning-q-5-rm-5","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"single-choice","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"correctOptionId":"a","feedback":{"correct":"Prioritise later is an ordered decision with a recorded reason, not denial of the risk.","incorrect":"Prioritise later is an ordered decision with a recorded reason, not denial of the risk."},"formative":true,"options":[{"id":"a","label":"The risk is recognised but higher-priority risks are treated first"},{"id":"b","label":"The risk does not exist"},{"id":"c","label":"The organisation transfers all legal duty to a supplier automatically"},{"id":"d","label":"Impact is ignored forever"}],"prompt":"Prioritise later means:","questionId":"week7-risk-management-learning:rm-6","sourceQuestionId":"rm-6","sourceType":"single"},"id":"week7-risk-management-learning-q-6-rm-6","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"single-choice","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"correctOptionId":"a","feedback":{"correct":"Proportionate recommendations consider cost and benefit in the organisation\u2019s context.","incorrect":"Proportionate recommendations consider cost and benefit in the organisation\u2019s context."},"formative":true,"options":[{"id":"a","label":"Weigh control cost against expected risk reduction for Northbank\u2019s size"},{"id":"b","label":"Always choose the most expensive product"},{"id":"c","label":"Ignore staff time entirely"},{"id":"d","label":"Replace likelihood and impact scoring"}],"prompt":"Cost-benefit consideration should:","questionId":"week7-risk-management-learning:rm-7","sourceQuestionId":"rm-7","sourceType":"single"},"id":"week7-risk-management-learning-q-7-rm-7","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"single-choice","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"correctOptionId":"a","feedback":{"correct":"This unit\u2019s register decisions use Mitigate, Accept and Prioritise. Transfer may appear as a quiz distractor only.","incorrect":"This unit\u2019s register decisions use Mitigate, Accept and Prioritise. Transfer may appear as a quiz distractor only."},"formative":true,"options":[{"id":"a","label":"Transfer (as a required register option)"},{"id":"b","label":"Mitigate"},{"id":"c","label":"Accept"},{"id":"d","label":"Prioritise later"}],"prompt":"Which distractor treatment is not required as a Northbank register decision in this unit?","questionId":"week7-risk-management-learning:rm-8","sourceQuestionId":"rm-8","sourceType":"single"},"id":"week7-risk-management-learning-q-8-rm-8","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"single-choice","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"format":"application/json","text":"```json\n{\n  \"weekNumber\": 7,\n  \"sessionNumber\": 1,\n  \"estimatedMinutes\": 30,\n  \"teachingNote\": \"Work through the risk-management stages in order. Treatments used in this unit are Mitigate, Accept (when cost is disproportionate) and Prioritise. Transfer and Avoid may appear as distractors in quizzes but are not required treatment options for the Northbank register.\",\n  \"stages\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"identify-assets\",\n      \"title\": \"Identify assets\",\n      \"summary\": \"List what matters to the organisation: systems, data, people, premises and services that support care.\",\n      \"northbankExample\": \"Northbank identifies the patient appointment system, staff laptops, the shared clinical notes store and the public website as assets that support day-to-day care.\",\n      \"teachingPoint\": \"Without a clear asset list, later likelihood and impact judgements have no organisational anchor.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"identify-threats-vulns\",\n      \"title\": \"Identify threats and vulnerabilities\",\n      \"summary\": \"For each asset, name plausible threats and the weaknesses that could be exploited. Keep the terms separate.\",\n      \"northbankExample\": \"Threat: phishing that steals staff credentials. Vulnerability: weak or reused passwords on the appointment system. Do not label phishing itself as the vulnerability.\",\n      \"teachingPoint\": \"Threat is the potential cause of harm; vulnerability is the weakness. Mixing them confuses the register.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"analyse-likelihood\",\n      \"title\": \"Analyse likelihood\",\n      \"summary\": \"Judge how likely it is that a threat will successfully exploit the vulnerability in this organisation.\",\n      \"northbankExample\": \"If many staff reuse passwords and phishing emails are common, likelihood of credential theft against the appointment system may be High.\",\n      \"teachingPoint\": \"Likelihood is contextual. A theoretical attack that is hard to deliver may still be Low likelihood for Northbank.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"analyse-impact\",\n      \"title\": \"Analyse impact\",\n      \"summary\": \"Judge the harm if the risk materialises: care disruption, confidentiality loss, financial cost, reputation and regulatory consequences.\",\n      \"northbankExample\": \"Unauthorised access to clinical notes could have High impact because patient confidentiality and care continuity are affected.\",\n      \"teachingPoint\": \"Impact is about consequence, not how impressive the attack sounds.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"determine-risk\",\n      \"title\": \"Determine risk level or score\",\n      \"summary\": \"Combine likelihood and impact using the Week 7 hub scoring guide to produce a Low, Medium or High risk rating.\",\n      \"northbankExample\": \"High likelihood and High impact for stolen appointment-system credentials produces a High risk rating that should be addressed early.\",\n      \"teachingPoint\": \"The score supports prioritisation. It is not a substitute for a justified decision.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"decide-treatment\",\n      \"title\": \"Decide treatment\",\n      \"summary\": \"Choose Mitigate, Accept or Prioritise later. Accept is valid when the cost of control is disproportionate to the risk.\",\n      \"northbankExample\": \"Northbank may Accept a Low-impact risk that the public leaflet PDF is briefly unavailable during a content update, because care systems are unaffected and mitigation spend would be disproportionate.\",\n      \"teachingPoint\": \"Accept is a reasoned decision, not ignoring the risk. Mitigate means reducing likelihood or impact. Prioritise later means the risk is recognised but other risks come first.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"cost-benefit\",\n      \"title\": \"Consider cost and benefit\",\n      \"summary\": \"Compare the cost or consequence of a control with the expected benefit in risk reduction for an organisation of Northbank\u2019s size.\",\n      \"northbankExample\": \"Mandatory multi-factor authentication for remote access to clinical systems has a staff-training cost but a clear benefit: fewer successful credential-theft incidents.\",\n      \"teachingPoint\": \"A perfect control that Northbank cannot afford or staff cannot use is a weak recommendation.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"review-effectiveness\",\n      \"title\": \"Review effectiveness measure\",\n      \"summary\": \"State how you will know the treatment worked. Avoid empty claims such as \u201cinstalled\u201d with no evidence of reduced risk.\",\n      \"northbankExample\": \"Effectiveness for MFA might be measured by a fall in successful password-reset phishing incidents and successful login attempts without a second factor over three months.\",\n      \"teachingPoint\": \"Effectiveness should be observable. \u201cWe installed the tool\u201d alone does not show risk reduction.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"treatments\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"mitigate\",\n      \"name\": \"Mitigate\",\n      \"meaning\": \"Reduce likelihood and/or impact with a proportionate control.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"accept\",\n      \"name\": \"Accept\",\n      \"meaning\": \"Consciously accept the risk when the cost of further control is disproportionate, usually for lower-rated risks.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"prioritise\",\n      \"name\": \"Prioritise later\",\n      \"meaning\": \"Recognise the risk but schedule treatment after higher-priority risks, with a reason recorded.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"acceptWorkedExample\": {\n    \"title\": \"Worked accept example (Low impact)\",\n    \"text\": \"Asset: public health leaflet PDF on the website. Threat: temporary link breakage during a routine content update. Vulnerability: single file publish process without a staging check. Likelihood: Low to Medium. Impact: Low (public information delayed; no patient records affected). Decision: Accept. Justification: the care impact is minimal and paying for a complex publishing platform would be disproportionate for Northbank\u2019s size.\"\n  }\n}\n```"},"id":"week7-risk-management-learning-source-remainder","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"markdown","version":"0.1.0"}],"id":"week7-risk-management-learning","metadata":{"activityType":"Guided learning","href":null,"runtimeGlobal":"Week7RiskManagementLearning","status":"available","summary":"Cyber Security Risk Management Learning","title":"Cyber Security Risk Management Learning"},"relationships":{"assets":[],"assignment":"formative-practice","learningOutcomes":["LO1"],"questions":[]},"schema":"lp.content.activity","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","version":"1.0.0"},{"blocks":[{"content":{"level":2,"text":"Northbank Risk Register"},"id":"week7-northbank-risk-register-title","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"heading","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"text":"Convert Week 2 vulnerabilities into a Week 7 risk register. Score likelihood and impact with the hub guide, then justify Mitigate, Accept or Prioritise later decisions with cost-benefit and effectiveness thinking."},"id":"week7-northbank-risk-register-intro","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"paragraph","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"format":"application/json","text":"```json\n{\n  \"weekNumber\": 7,\n  \"sessionNumber\": 1,\n  \"estimatedMinutes\": 45,\n  \"organisation\": \"Northbank Community Health Partnership\",\n  \"entryCount\": 5,\n  \"intro\": \"Convert Week 2 vulnerabilities into a Week 7 risk register. Score likelihood and impact with the hub guide, then justify Mitigate, Accept or Prioritise later decisions with cost-benefit and effectiveness thinking.\",\n  \"week2UnavailableNote\": \"No Week 2 vulnerability register was found in this browser. Enter five assets and related fields yourself. Do not invent previous learner answers from another device.\",\n  \"decisions\": [\n    \"Mitigate\",\n    \"Accept\",\n    \"Prioritise later\"\n  ],\n  \"levels\": [\n    \"Low\",\n    \"Medium\",\n    \"High\"\n  ],\n  \"scoringGuide\": {\n    \"title\": \"Week 7 hub scoring guide\",\n    \"likelihood\": {\n      \"Low\": \"Unlikely in normal Northbank operations in the near term.\",\n      \"Medium\": \"Plausible given current practices, tooling or staff behaviour.\",\n      \"High\": \"Likely without further control, or already nearly occurring.\"\n    },\n    \"impact\": {\n      \"Low\": \"Limited disruption; little or no effect on patient care or confidential data.\",\n      \"Medium\": \"Noticeable disruption, partial data exposure risk, or recovery effort required.\",\n      \"High\": \"Serious harm to care continuity, confidentiality, regulatory standing or trust.\"\n    },\n    \"matrix\": [\n      {\n        \"likelihood\": \"Low\",\n        \"impact\": \"Low\",\n        \"risk\": \"Low\",\n        \"numeric\": \"1\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"likelihood\": \"Low\",\n        \"impact\": \"Medium\",\n        \"risk\": \"Low\",\n        \"numeric\": \"2\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"likelihood\": \"Low\",\n        \"impact\": \"High\",\n        \"risk\": \"Medium\",\n        \"numeric\": \"3\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"likelihood\": \"Medium\",\n        \"impact\": \"Low\",\n        \"risk\": \"Low\",\n        \"numeric\": \"2\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"likelihood\": \"Medium\",\n        \"impact\": \"Medium\",\n        \"risk\": \"Medium\",\n        \"numeric\": \"4\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"likelihood\": \"Medium\",\n        \"impact\": \"High\",\n        \"risk\": \"High\",\n        \"numeric\": \"6\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"likelihood\": \"High\",\n        \"impact\": \"Low\",\n        \"risk\": \"Medium\",\n        \"numeric\": \"3\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"likelihood\": \"High\",\n        \"impact\": \"Medium\",\n        \"risk\": \"High\",\n        \"numeric\": \"6\"\n      },\n      {\n        \"likelihood\": \"High\",\n        \"impact\": \"High\",\n        \"risk\": \"High\",\n        \"numeric\": \"9\"\n      }\n    ],\n    \"note\": \"Risk ratings use text labels (Low, Medium, High). Colour is optional and never the only indicator. Numeric helpers are for discussion only.\"\n  },\n  \"sampleRows\": [\n    {\n      \"asset\": \"Patient appointment system\",\n      \"threat\": \"Credential-theft phishing against reception and clinical staff\",\n      \"vulnerability\": \"Single-factor passwords with limited monitoring of unusual logins\",\n      \"likelihood\": \"High\",\n      \"impact\": \"High\",\n      \"riskScore\": \"High\",\n      \"mitigation\": \"Require multi-factor authentication for remote and privileged access\",\n      \"costConsequence\": \"Staff setup time and occasional login friction during busy clinics\",\n      \"expectedBenefit\": \"Fewer successful account takeovers affecting bookings and records access\",\n      \"decision\": \"Mitigate\",\n      \"effectivenessMeasure\": \"Track successful phishing-driven password resets and MFA challenge failures over 90 days\",\n      \"justification\": \"High likelihood and High impact on care coordination justify mitigation before lower-rated risks.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"asset\": \"Public health leaflet PDF on website\",\n      \"threat\": \"Temporary broken link during a routine content update\",\n      \"vulnerability\": \"Single-step publish process without a staging check\",\n      \"likelihood\": \"Low\",\n      \"impact\": \"Low\",\n      \"riskScore\": \"Low\",\n      \"mitigation\": \"Optional dual-person publish check (not funded this quarter)\",\n      \"costConsequence\": \"Extra staff time on every leaflet update for low care impact\",\n      \"expectedBenefit\": \"Slightly fewer public information delays\",\n      \"decision\": \"Accept\",\n      \"effectivenessMeasure\": \"Quarterly review of public content downtime minutes; escalate if care advice pages are affected\",\n      \"justification\": \"Low impact on patient care; further control cost is disproportionate for Northbank\u2019s size.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"sentenceStarters\": [\n    \"This asset matters because\u2026\",\n    \"The threat could\u2026 while the vulnerability is\u2026\",\n    \"Likelihood is\u2026 because\u2026\",\n    \"Impact is\u2026 because patient care / data\u2026\",\n    \"I choose Mitigate / Accept / Prioritise later because\u2026\",\n    \"Cost is acceptable / disproportionate because\u2026\",\n    \"I will judge effectiveness by measuring\u2026\"\n  ],\n  \"addressFirstPrompt\": \"Which risk will you address first, and why? Link likelihood, impact and organisational context.\",\n  \"fields\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"asset\",\n      \"label\": \"Asset\",\n      \"rows\": 1,\n      \"required\": true\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"threat\",\n      \"label\": \"Threat\",\n      \"rows\": 2,\n      \"required\": true\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"vulnerability\",\n      \"label\": \"Vulnerability\",\n      \"rows\": 2,\n      \"required\": true\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"likelihood\",\n      \"label\": \"Likelihood (Low / Medium / High)\",\n      \"type\": \"select\",\n      \"required\": true\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"impact\",\n      \"label\": \"Impact (Low / Medium / High)\",\n      \"type\": \"select\",\n      \"required\": true\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"riskScore\",\n      \"label\": \"Risk rating (auto from guide, editable)\",\n      \"type\": \"select\",\n      \"required\": true\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"mitigation\",\n      \"label\": \"Mitigation or treatment idea\",\n      \"rows\": 2,\n      \"required\": true\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"costConsequence\",\n      \"label\": \"Cost or consequence of treatment / of accepting\",\n      \"rows\": 2,\n      \"required\": true\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"expectedBenefit\",\n      \"label\": \"Expected benefit\",\n      \"rows\": 2,\n      \"required\": true\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"decision\",\n      \"label\": \"Decision\",\n      \"type\": \"decision\",\n      \"required\": true\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"effectivenessMeasure\",\n      \"label\": \"Effectiveness measure\",\n      \"rows\": 2,\n      \"required\": true\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"justification\",\n      \"label\": \"Justification\",\n      \"rows\": 3,\n      \"required\": true\n    }\n  ],\n  \"validationMessages\": {\n    \"asset\": \"Each entry needs a named asset.\",\n    \"threatVuln\": \"Threat and vulnerability text should not be identical. Keep the cause of harm separate from the weakness.\",\n    \"allHigh\": \"Warning: every entry is rated High. Check whether some risks are genuinely lower so prioritisation remains meaningful.\",\n    \"mitigationRelate\": \"Mitigation should clearly relate to the named vulnerability or threat.\",\n    \"decisionReason\": \"Each decision needs a justification.\",\n    \"effectivenessInstalled\": \"Effectiveness should not be only \u201cinstalled\u201d. Say what you will measure.\",\n    \"costMitigate\": \"Mitigate decisions need a cost or consequence note.\",\n    \"addressFirst\": \"Select which risk to address first and justify it.\",\n    \"acceptNeeded\": \"Include at least one Accept decision with justification.\",\n    \"costBenefitOne\": \"Complete cost and expected benefit for at least one mitigation.\",\n    \"effectivenessOne\": \"Provide a measurable effectiveness statement for at least one entry.\"\n  }\n}\n```"},"id":"week7-northbank-risk-register-source-remainder","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"markdown","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"formative":true,"prompt":"Complete this activity on the learner hub page, then write a short note to confirm you have finished.","questionId":"week7-northbank-risk-register:learner-note","sourceQuestionId":"learner-note"},"id":"week7-northbank-risk-register-learner-note","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"reflection","version":"0.1.0"}],"id":"week7-northbank-risk-register","metadata":{"activityType":"Structured register","href":null,"runtimeGlobal":"Week7RiskRegister","status":"available","summary":"Northbank Risk Register","title":"Northbank Risk Register"},"relationships":{"assets":[],"assignment":"formative-practice","learningOutcomes":["LO1"],"questions":[]},"schema":"lp.content.activity","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","version":"1.0.0"},{"blocks":[{"content":{"level":2,"text":"Vulnerability Testing Methods"},"id":"week7-testing-methods-title","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"heading","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"text":"Compare four authorised testing methods. Penetration testing is not the same as automated vulnerability scanning."},"id":"week7-testing-methods-intro","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"paragraph","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"correctOptionId":"a","feedback":{"correct":"Pentesting is authorised and scoped. It is not identical to automated scanning.","incorrect":"Pentesting is authorised and scoped. It is not identical to automated scanning."},"formative":true,"options":[{"id":"a","label":"An authorised simulated attack within an agreed scope"},{"id":"b","label":"Any automated vulnerability scan run overnight"},{"id":"c","label":"Unrestricted hacking without permission"},{"id":"d","label":"Only checking that a password field accepts input"}],"prompt":"Penetration testing is best described as:","questionId":"week7-testing-methods:tm-1","sourceQuestionId":"tm-1","sourceType":"single"},"id":"week7-testing-methods-q-1-tm-1","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"single-choice","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"correctOptionId":"a","feedback":{"correct":"Fuzzing stresses software with unexpected or invalid input.","incorrect":"Fuzzing stresses software with unexpected or invalid input."},"formative":true,"options":[{"id":"a","label":"Unexpected, invalid or unusual input"},{"id":"b","label":"Only perfectly valid clinical workflows"},{"id":"c","label":"Physical lock picking"},{"id":"d","label":"Public relations statements"}],"prompt":"Fuzzing mainly uses:","questionId":"week7-testing-methods:tm-2","sourceQuestionId":"tm-2","sourceType":"single"},"id":"week7-testing-methods-q-2-tm-2","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"single-choice","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"correctOptionId":"a","feedback":{"correct":"SFT verifies specified security control behaviour.","incorrect":"SFT verifies specified security control behaviour."},"formative":true,"options":[{"id":"a","label":"A control behaves as specified"},{"id":"b","label":"Every possible zero-day is impossible"},{"id":"c","label":"Staff morale is high"},{"id":"d","label":"The organisation has transferred all risk"}],"prompt":"Security functionality testing checks that:","questionId":"week7-testing-methods:tm-3","sourceQuestionId":"tm-3","sourceType":"single"},"id":"week7-testing-methods-q-3-tm-3","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"single-choice","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"correctOptionId":"a","feedback":{"correct":"Sandboxing isolates untrusted content for safer observation.","incorrect":"Sandboxing isolates untrusted content for safer observation."},"formative":true,"options":[{"id":"a","label":"Untrusted code or files need isolation for observation"},{"id":"b","label":"You want to email malware to patients for realism"},{"id":"c","label":"You need to replace penetration testing forever"},{"id":"d","label":"You only want to rename a vulnerability as a threat"}],"prompt":"Sandboxing is appropriate when:","questionId":"week7-testing-methods:tm-4","sourceQuestionId":"tm-4","sourceType":"single"},"id":"week7-testing-methods-q-4-tm-4","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"single-choice","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"correctOptionId":"a","feedback":{"correct":"Scanning and penetration testing answer related but different questions.","incorrect":"Scanning and penetration testing answer related but different questions."},"formative":true,"options":[{"id":"a","label":"Known signature issues may be absent, but not that a pentest-style attack path is impossible"},{"id":"b","label":"Northbank can never be breached"},{"id":"c","label":"Fuzzing is unnecessary forever"},{"id":"d","label":"Sandboxing is illegal"}],"prompt":"A clean vulnerability scan alone proves:","questionId":"week7-testing-methods:tm-5","sourceQuestionId":"tm-5","sourceType":"single"},"id":"week7-testing-methods-q-5-tm-5","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"single-choice","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"correctOptionId":"a","feedback":{"correct":"SFT checks that the control behaves as specified.","incorrect":"SFT checks that the control behaves as specified."},"formative":true,"options":[{"id":"a","label":"Security functionality testing"},{"id":"b","label":"Fuzzing alone"},{"id":"c","label":"Sandboxing a PDF"},{"id":"d","label":"Accepting the risk without testing"}],"prompt":"Which method is most focused on whether MFA enforces the intended policy?","questionId":"week7-testing-methods:tm-6","sourceQuestionId":"tm-6","sourceType":"single"},"id":"week7-testing-methods-q-6-tm-6","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"single-choice","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"correctOptionId":"a","feedback":{"correct":"Sandbox evasion and environment differences limit what can be concluded.","incorrect":"Sandbox evasion and environment differences limit what can be concluded."},"formative":true,"options":[{"id":"a","label":"Some malicious samples detect sandboxes and stay quiet"},{"id":"b","label":"Isolation always makes every file safe for clinical PCs"},{"id":"c","label":"It replaces the need for any access control"},{"id":"d","label":"It is identical to penetration testing"}],"prompt":"A limitation of sandboxing is that:","questionId":"week7-testing-methods:tm-7","sourceQuestionId":"tm-7","sourceType":"single"},"id":"week7-testing-methods-q-7-tm-7","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"single-choice","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"correctOptionId":"a","feedback":{"correct":"Keep purpose distinctions clear for examination answers.","incorrect":"Keep purpose distinctions clear for examination answers."},"formative":true,"options":[{"id":"a","label":"Fuzzing \u2192 unusual input; Pentest \u2192 authorised simulated attack"},{"id":"b","label":"Fuzzing \u2192 authorised simulated attack; Pentest \u2192 only PDF isolation"},{"id":"c","label":"SFT \u2192 untrusted file isolation; Sandboxing \u2192 password policy wording only"},{"id":"d","label":"All four methods are identical"}],"prompt":"Which pairing is correct?","questionId":"week7-testing-methods:tm-8","sourceQuestionId":"tm-8","sourceType":"single"},"id":"week7-testing-methods-q-8-tm-8","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"single-choice","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"format":"application/json","text":"```json\n{\n  \"weekNumber\": 7,\n  \"sessionNumber\": 1,\n  \"estimatedMinutes\": 30,\n  \"intro\": \"Compare four authorised testing methods. Penetration testing is not the same as automated vulnerability scanning.\",\n  \"methods\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"pentest\",\n      \"name\": \"Penetration testing\",\n      \"purpose\": \"An authorised simulated attack that tries to exploit weaknesses the way an attacker might, within an agreed scope.\",\n      \"mayReveal\": \"Chained weaknesses, weak access control, and realistic attack paths that scanners alone may not prove.\",\n      \"mayMiss\": \"Issues outside the agreed scope, zero-day flaws unknown to the tester, or social-engineering paths excluded from the rules of engagement.\",\n      \"appropriate\": \"When Northbank needs assurance that critical care systems can withstand a skilled, authorised attempt after controls are in place.\",\n      \"limitation\": \"Time-boxed and scoped; a clean report does not prove the organisation is permanently secure. It is not the same as running an automated vulnerability scan.\",\n      \"misconception\": \"Penetration testing is not just automated vulnerability scanning. Scanning finds known issues; a pentest attempts exploitation under authorisation.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"fuzzing\",\n      \"name\": \"Fuzzing\",\n      \"purpose\": \"Send unexpected, invalid or unusual input to software to see whether it crashes, corrupts data or behaves unsafely.\",\n      \"mayReveal\": \"Input-handling bugs, crashes and edge-case failures in applications or parsers.\",\n      \"mayMiss\": \"Logic flaws that need valid business workflows, misconfigurations, or human-process weaknesses.\",\n      \"appropriate\": \"When testing how Northbank-facing forms, upload handlers or APIs cope with malformed input before wider release.\",\n      \"limitation\": \"Fuzzing does not replace architectural review or access-control testing; crashes need triage to become actionable fixes.\",\n      \"misconception\": \"Fuzzing is about unusual input behaviour, not a full simulated attacker campaign.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"sft\",\n      \"name\": \"Security functionality testing\",\n      \"purpose\": \"Check that a security control behaves as specified: authentication, authorisation, logging, encryption or similar controls.\",\n      \"mayReveal\": \"Controls that are misconfigured, incomplete, or do not enforce the intended policy.\",\n      \"mayMiss\": \"Novel attack techniques or weaknesses in components that were never specified as security functions under test.\",\n      \"appropriate\": \"After Northbank deploys MFA or role-based access, to confirm the control works as designed for staff roles.\",\n      \"limitation\": \"Passing functional checks does not prove there are no other vulnerabilities elsewhere in the estate.\",\n      \"misconception\": \"Security functionality testing checks specified control behaviour; it is not a full penetration test.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"sandbox\",\n      \"name\": \"Sandboxing\",\n      \"purpose\": \"Run untrusted code or files in isolation so behaviour can be observed without exposing the live network or endpoints.\",\n      \"mayReveal\": \"Suspicious network calls, file changes or process behaviour from an untrusted attachment or installer.\",\n      \"mayMiss\": \"Malware that detects sandboxes and stays quiet, or threats that only trigger on production systems.\",\n      \"appropriate\": \"When Northbank staff receive an unexpected attachment and need a safe, tutor-led way to observe behaviour before any live use.\",\n      \"limitation\": \"Isolation reduces risk but does not prove a file is safe for unrestricted use on clinical devices.\",\n      \"misconception\": \"Sandboxing is observation in isolation, not permission to execute unknown malware on personal or clinical devices.\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```"},"id":"week7-testing-methods-source-remainder","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"markdown","version":"0.1.0"}],"id":"week7-testing-methods","metadata":{"activityType":"Guided learning","href":null,"runtimeGlobal":"Week7TestingMethods","status":"available","summary":"Vulnerability Testing Methods","title":"Vulnerability Testing Methods"},"relationships":{"assets":[],"assignment":"formative-practice","learningOutcomes":["LO1"],"questions":[]},"schema":"lp.content.activity","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","version":"1.0.0"},{"blocks":[{"content":{"level":2,"text":"Safe Sandboxing Demonstration Record"},"id":"week7-sandbox-observation-title","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"heading","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"format":"application/json","text":"```json\n{\n  \"weekNumber\": 7,\n  \"sessionNumber\": 1,\n  \"estimatedMinutes\": 20,\n  \"executesFiles\": false,\n  \"safetyNotice\": \"This hub does not upload, execute or analyse malware. There is no file upload and no malware analysis service. Record only what you observe in the tutor-led demonstration.\",\n  \"demoNotes\": [\n    \"Your tutor will demonstrate placing an untrusted sample into an isolated environment.\",\n    \"Watch for process, file or network behaviour that appears without running anything on your own device.\",\n    \"Discuss what the demonstration can and cannot prove about safety on clinical systems.\"\n  ],\n  \"fields\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"whatPlaced\",\n      \"label\": \"What was placed in the sandbox (as described by the tutor)?\",\n      \"minChars\": 20,\n      \"marks\": 0.5\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"whyIsolation\",\n      \"label\": \"Why was isolation used?\",\n      \"minChars\": 25,\n      \"marks\": 0.5\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"behaviourObserved\",\n      \"label\": \"What behaviour was observed?\",\n      \"minChars\": 25,\n      \"marks\": 1\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"analysisRevealed\",\n      \"label\": \"What did the analysis reveal (or suggest)?\",\n      \"minChars\": 25,\n      \"marks\": 0.5\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"couldNotProve\",\n      \"label\": \"What could the sandbox demonstration not prove?\",\n      \"minChars\": 25,\n      \"marks\": 0.5\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"whyUnsafeDirect\",\n      \"label\": \"Why would it be unsafe to open the sample directly on a clinical or personal device?\",\n      \"minChars\": 30,\n      \"marks\": 1\n    }\n  ],\n  \"completionNote\": \"Score is based on field completeness. Empty or one-word answers do not earn marks.\"\n}\n```"},"id":"week7-sandbox-observation-source-remainder","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"markdown","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"formative":true,"prompt":"Complete this activity on the learner hub page, then write a short note to confirm you have finished.","questionId":"week7-sandbox-observation:learner-note","sourceQuestionId":"learner-note"},"id":"week7-sandbox-observation-learner-note","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"reflection","version":"0.1.0"}],"id":"week7-sandbox-observation","metadata":{"activityType":"Observation record","href":null,"runtimeGlobal":"Week7SandboxObservation","status":"available","summary":"Safe Sandboxing Demonstration Record","title":"Safe Sandboxing Demonstration Record"},"relationships":{"assets":[],"assignment":"formative-practice","learningOutcomes":["LO1"],"questions":[]},"schema":"lp.content.activity","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","version":"1.0.0"},{"blocks":[{"content":{"level":2,"text":"Detection and Prevention Comparison"},"id":"week7-detection-prevention-title","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"heading","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"text":"Detection alerts; prevention acts. Learn NIDS, HIDS, DIDS, anomaly-based and signature-based detection, and honeypots in a Northbank context."},"id":"week7-detection-prevention-intro","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"paragraph","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"correctOptionId":"a","feedback":{"correct":"Detection alerts; prevention is what acts to block.","incorrect":"Detection alerts; prevention is what acts to block."},"formative":true,"options":[{"id":"a","label":"Alerts on suspicious activity"},{"id":"b","label":"Always blocks every packet automatically"},{"id":"c","label":"Replaces the need for any firewall"},{"id":"d","label":"Is identical to a honeypot"}],"prompt":"Intrusion detection mainly:","questionId":"week7-detection-prevention:dp-1","sourceQuestionId":"dp-1","sourceType":"single"},"id":"week7-detection-prevention-q-1-dp-1","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"single-choice","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"correctOptionId":"a","feedback":{"correct":"Prevention systems can take automated protective action.","incorrect":"Prevention systems can take automated protective action."},"formative":true,"options":[{"id":"a","label":"Can act to block or disrupt suspicious activity"},{"id":"b","label":"Only stores leaflets as PDFs"},{"id":"c","label":"Never generates alerts"},{"id":"d","label":"Means accepting every High risk"}],"prompt":"Intrusion prevention mainly:","questionId":"week7-detection-prevention:dp-2","sourceQuestionId":"dp-2","sourceType":"single"},"id":"week7-detection-prevention-q-2-dp-2","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"single-choice","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"correctOptionId":"a","feedback":{"correct":"NIDS is network-based.","incorrect":"NIDS is network-based."},"formative":true,"options":[{"id":"a","label":"Network traffic"},{"id":"b","label":"Only one host\u2019s local files"},{"id":"c","label":"Paper visitor badges"},{"id":"d","label":"Staff appraisal scores"}],"prompt":"NIDS focuses on:","questionId":"week7-detection-prevention:dp-3","sourceQuestionId":"dp-3","sourceType":"single"},"id":"week7-detection-prevention-q-3-dp-3","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"single-choice","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"correctOptionId":"a","feedback":{"correct":"HIDS is host-based.","incorrect":"HIDS is host-based."},"formative":true,"options":[{"id":"a","label":"Activity on a specific host"},{"id":"b","label":"Only internet backbone links worldwide"},{"id":"c","label":"Public relations wording"},{"id":"d","label":"Transferring risk by renaming it"}],"prompt":"HIDS focuses on:","questionId":"week7-detection-prevention:dp-4","sourceQuestionId":"dp-4","sourceType":"single"},"id":"week7-detection-prevention-q-4-dp-4","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"single-choice","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"correctOptionId":"a","feedback":{"correct":"Distributed IDS coordinates multiple detection points.","incorrect":"Distributed IDS coordinates multiple detection points."},"formative":true,"options":[{"id":"a","label":"Coordinated detection across multiple sensors or sites"},{"id":"b","label":"A single unused password"},{"id":"c","label":"Only signature matching on one laptop"},{"id":"d","label":"A type of fuzzing input"}],"prompt":"DIDS is best described as:","questionId":"week7-detection-prevention:dp-5","sourceQuestionId":"dp-5","sourceType":"single"},"id":"week7-detection-prevention-q-5-dp-5","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"single-choice","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"correctOptionId":"a","feedback":{"correct":"Signatures match known patterns and may miss novel attacks.","incorrect":"Signatures match known patterns and may miss novel attacks."},"formative":true,"options":[{"id":"a","label":"Known patterns already in the signature set"},{"id":"b","label":"Brand-new techniques with no matching signature"},{"id":"c","label":"Every possible future attack forever"},{"id":"d","label":"Only printer paper jams"}],"prompt":"Signature-based detection is strongest against:","questionId":"week7-detection-prevention:dp-6","sourceQuestionId":"dp-6","sourceType":"single"},"id":"week7-detection-prevention-q-6-dp-6","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"single-choice","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"correctOptionId":"a","feedback":{"correct":"Anomaly detection looks for deviation from normal.","incorrect":"Anomaly detection looks for deviation from normal."},"formative":true,"options":[{"id":"a","label":"Differs from an established baseline"},{"id":"b","label":"Exactly matches one old virus name only"},{"id":"c","label":"Is always harmless by definition"},{"id":"d","label":"Cannot be reviewed by analysts"}],"prompt":"Anomaly-based detection flags activity that:","questionId":"week7-detection-prevention:dp-7","sourceQuestionId":"dp-7","sourceType":"single"},"id":"week7-detection-prevention-q-7-dp-7","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"single-choice","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"correctOptionId":"a","feedback":{"correct":"Honeypots are decoys, not production care systems.","incorrect":"Honeypots are decoys, not production care systems."},"formative":true,"options":[{"id":"a","label":"A decoy designed to attract and reveal attacker methods"},{"id":"b","label":"The live clinical notes database"},{"id":"c","label":"Another word for NIDS only"},{"id":"d","label":"A legal statute"}],"prompt":"A honeypot is:","questionId":"week7-detection-prevention:dp-8","sourceQuestionId":"dp-8","sourceType":"single"},"id":"week7-detection-prevention-q-8-dp-8","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"single-choice","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"format":"application/json","text":"```json\n{\n  \"weekNumber\": 7,\n  \"sessionNumber\": 1,\n  \"estimatedMinutes\": 35,\n  \"intro\": \"Detection alerts; prevention acts. Learn NIDS, HIDS, DIDS, anomaly-based and signature-based detection, and honeypots in a Northbank context.\",\n  \"concepts\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"ids\",\n      \"name\": \"Intrusion detection\",\n      \"summary\": \"Monitors activity and raises alerts when suspicious behaviour is found. It does not by itself block the activity.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"ips\",\n      \"name\": \"Intrusion prevention\",\n      \"summary\": \"Monitors activity and can take automated action to block or disrupt suspicious traffic or behaviour.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"nids\",\n      \"name\": \"NIDS (Network-based IDS)\",\n      \"summary\": \"Watches network traffic for suspicious patterns across links and segments.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"hids\",\n      \"name\": \"HIDS (Host-based IDS)\",\n      \"summary\": \"Watches activity on a specific host, such as logs, file integrity or process behaviour.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"dids\",\n      \"name\": \"DIDS (Distributed IDS)\",\n      \"summary\": \"Coordinates detection across multiple sensors or sites so analysts see a wider picture.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"signature\",\n      \"name\": \"Signature-based detection\",\n      \"summary\": \"Matches activity against known attack patterns or signatures.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"anomaly\",\n      \"name\": \"Anomaly-based detection\",\n      \"summary\": \"Flags activity that differs from an established normal baseline.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"honeypot\",\n      \"name\": \"Honeypot\",\n      \"summary\": \"A decoy system or service designed to attract attackers and reveal methods without exposing real assets.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"novelAttackScenario\": \"A new phishing kit uses previously unseen command-and-control domains and slightly altered email templates that do not match any signature in Northbank\u2019s current detection set. Signature-based tools may miss the first wave until signatures are updated, while anomaly-based monitoring might notice unusual outbound connections from a reception PC after a staff member opens the message.\",\n  \"comparisonFields\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"canDetect\",\n      \"label\": \"What it can detect well\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"mayMiss\",\n      \"label\": \"What it may miss\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"advantage\",\n      \"label\": \"Main advantage\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"limitation\",\n      \"label\": \"Main limitation\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"scenario\",\n      \"label\": \"Suitable Northbank scenario\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"comparisonTargets\": [\n    \"anomaly\",\n    \"signature\"\n  ]\n}\n```"},"id":"week7-detection-prevention-source-remainder","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"markdown","version":"0.1.0"}],"id":"week7-detection-prevention","metadata":{"activityType":"Guided learning","href":null,"runtimeGlobal":"Week7DetectionPrevention","status":"available","summary":"Detection and Prevention Comparison","title":"Detection and Prevention Comparison"},"relationships":{"assets":[],"assignment":"formative-practice","learningOutcomes":["LO1"],"questions":[]},"schema":"lp.content.activity","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","version":"1.0.0"},{"blocks":[{"content":{"level":2,"text":"NCSC Heightened Cyber Threat Decision Log"},"id":"week7-heightened-threat-title","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"heading","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"text":"Use this page as a facilitated companion while your tutor runs NCSC Exercise in a Box: Heightened cyber threat. Do not invent exercise prompts. Record the decisions your group actually makes and link each action to a risk register entry."},"id":"week7-heightened-threat-intro","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"paragraph","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"format":"application/json","text":"```json\n{\n  \"weekNumber\": 7,\n  \"sessionNumber\": 1,\n  \"estimatedMinutes\": 40,\n  \"organisation\": \"Northbank Community Health Partnership\",\n  \"ncscUrl\": \"https://www.ncsc.gov.uk/section/exercise-in-a-box/heightened-cyber-threat\",\n  \"intro\": \"Use this page as a facilitated companion while your tutor runs NCSC Exercise in a Box: Heightened cyber threat. Do not invent exercise prompts. Record the decisions your group actually makes and link each action to a risk register entry.\",\n  \"collaborationNote\": \"If your group uses different devices, share a short group code and paste agreed notes here so you do not need one shared browser session.\",\n  \"minDecisionsWithCostBenefit\": 2,\n  \"entryFields\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"riskRegisterRef\",\n      \"label\": \"Risk register reference\",\n      \"type\": \"ref\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"proposedAction\",\n      \"label\": \"Proposed action\",\n      \"rows\": 2\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"riskAddressed\",\n      \"label\": \"Risk addressed (what reduces?)\",\n      \"rows\": 2\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"additionalMonitoring\",\n      \"label\": \"Additional monitoring (if any)\",\n      \"rows\": 2\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"costAccepted\",\n      \"label\": \"Cost accepted\",\n      \"rows\": 2\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"benefitGained\",\n      \"label\": \"Benefit gained\",\n      \"rows\": 2\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"stopDelayReduce\",\n      \"label\": \"Stop, delay or reduce? (and why)\",\n      \"rows\": 2\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"groupJustification\",\n      \"label\": \"Group justification\",\n      \"rows\": 3\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"debriefNotes\",\n      \"label\": \"Debrief notes\",\n      \"rows\": 2\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```"},"id":"week7-heightened-threat-source-remainder","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"markdown","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"formative":true,"prompt":"Complete this activity on the learner hub page, then write a short note to confirm you have finished.","questionId":"week7-heightened-threat:learner-note","sourceQuestionId":"learner-note"},"id":"week7-heightened-threat-learner-note","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"reflection","version":"0.1.0"}],"id":"week7-heightened-threat","metadata":{"activityType":"Facilitated companion","href":null,"runtimeGlobal":"Week7HeightenedThreat","status":"available","summary":"NCSC Heightened Cyber Threat Decision Log","title":"NCSC Heightened Cyber Threat Decision Log"},"relationships":{"assets":[],"assignment":"formative-practice","learningOutcomes":["LO1"],"questions":[]},"schema":"lp.content.activity","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","version":"1.0.0"},{"blocks":[{"content":{"level":2,"text":"Session 2 Retrieval Quiz"},"id":"week7-session2-retrieval-title","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"heading","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"text":"Low-stakes retrieval on detection versus prevention, testing methods, risk terminology and monitoring placements."},"id":"week7-session2-retrieval-intro","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"paragraph","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"correctOptionId":"a","feedback":{"correct":"Keep the alert-versus-act distinction clear.","incorrect":"Keep the alert-versus-act distinction clear."},"formative":true,"options":[{"id":"a","label":"Detection alerts on suspicious activity; prevention can act to block or disrupt it"},{"id":"b","label":"Detection always blocks traffic; prevention only writes reports"},{"id":"c","label":"They are identical terms with no practical difference"},{"id":"d","label":"Prevention means accepting every High risk without controls"}],"prompt":"Detection versus prevention: which statement is accurate?","questionId":"week7-session2-retrieval:s2-1","sourceQuestionId":"s2-1","sourceType":"single"},"id":"week7-session2-retrieval-q-1-s2-1","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"single-choice","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"correctOptionId":"a","feedback":{"correct":"Anomaly detection compares behaviour with a normal baseline.","incorrect":"Anomaly detection compares behaviour with a normal baseline."},"formative":true,"options":[{"id":"a","label":"Differs from an established baseline"},{"id":"b","label":"Exactly matches one known malware hash only"},{"id":"c","label":"Is approved in a staff handbook paragraph"},{"id":"d","label":"Cannot generate false positives ever"}],"prompt":"Anomaly-based detection mainly looks for activity that:","questionId":"week7-session2-retrieval:s2-2","sourceQuestionId":"s2-2","sourceType":"single"},"id":"week7-session2-retrieval-q-2-s2-2","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"single-choice","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"correctOptionId":"a","feedback":{"correct":"New techniques can arrive before signatures are updated.","incorrect":"New techniques can arrive before signatures are updated."},"formative":true,"options":[{"id":"a","label":"There may be no matching known pattern yet"},{"id":"b","label":"Signatures always include every future attack"},{"id":"c","label":"Novel attacks cannot use the network"},{"id":"d","label":"Honeypots delete all signatures daily"}],"prompt":"Signature-based detection may miss a novel attack because:","questionId":"week7-session2-retrieval:s2-3","sourceQuestionId":"s2-3","sourceType":"single"},"id":"week7-session2-retrieval-q-3-s2-3","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"single-choice","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"correctOptionId":"a","feedback":{"correct":"Network versus host placement is the core distinction.","incorrect":"Network versus host placement is the core distinction."},"formative":true,"options":[{"id":"a","label":"NIDS watches network traffic; HIDS watches a specific host"},{"id":"b","label":"NIDS watches one laptop only; HIDS watches only internet backbones"},{"id":"c","label":"Both only mean honeypots"},{"id":"d","label":"HIDS is a criminal statute"}],"prompt":"NIDS versus HIDS: which pairing is correct?","questionId":"week7-session2-retrieval:s2-4","sourceQuestionId":"s2-4","sourceType":"single"},"id":"week7-session2-retrieval-q-4-s2-4","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"single-choice","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"correctOptionId":"a","feedback":{"correct":"Risk is not a synonym for threat.","incorrect":"Risk is not a synonym for threat."},"formative":true,"options":[{"id":"a","label":"Risk assesses likelihood and impact; a threat is a potential cause of harm"},{"id":"b","label":"Risk and threat are always the same word"},{"id":"c","label":"Threat is the numeric score only"},{"id":"d","label":"Risk means any software update"}],"prompt":"Risk versus threat: which is correct?","questionId":"week7-session2-retrieval:s2-5","sourceQuestionId":"s2-5","sourceType":"single"},"id":"week7-session2-retrieval-q-5-s2-5","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"single-choice","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"correctOptionId":"a","feedback":{"correct":"Do not collapse pentest into automated scanning.","incorrect":"Do not collapse pentest into automated scanning."},"formative":true,"options":[{"id":"a","label":"A pentest is an authorised simulated attack; scanning mainly finds known issues without full exploitation"},{"id":"b","label":"They are legally identical in every case"},{"id":"c","label":"Scanning always includes physical break-in"},{"id":"d","label":"Pentesting never needs authorisation"}],"prompt":"Penetration testing versus vulnerability scanning:","questionId":"week7-session2-retrieval:s2-6","sourceQuestionId":"s2-6","sourceType":"single"},"id":"week7-session2-retrieval-q-6-s2-6","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"single-choice","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"correctOptionId":"a","feedback":{"correct":"Fuzzing stresses input handling with unusual data.","incorrect":"Fuzzing stresses input handling with unusual data."},"formative":true,"options":[{"id":"a","label":"Test software with unexpected, invalid or unusual input"},{"id":"b","label":"Replace all staff training"},{"id":"c","label":"Accept Low risks automatically"},{"id":"d","label":"Coordinate DIDS sensors only"}],"prompt":"The main purpose of fuzzing is to:","questionId":"week7-session2-retrieval:s2-7","sourceQuestionId":"s2-7","sourceType":"single"},"id":"week7-session2-retrieval-q-7-s2-7","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"single-choice","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"correctOptionId":"a","feedback":{"correct":"Sandboxing isolates untrusted content for safer observation.","incorrect":"Sandboxing isolates untrusted content for safer observation."},"formative":true,"options":[{"id":"a","label":"Observe untrusted code or files in isolation"},{"id":"b","label":"Publish patient records to the public website"},{"id":"c","label":"Prove a file is permanently safe on every clinical PC"},{"id":"d","label":"Rename vulnerabilities as threats"}],"prompt":"Sandboxing is used to:","questionId":"week7-session2-retrieval:s2-8","sourceQuestionId":"s2-8","sourceType":"single"},"id":"week7-session2-retrieval-q-8-s2-8","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"single-choice","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"correctOptionId":"a","feedback":{"correct":"Honeypots are decoys, not production care systems.","incorrect":"Honeypots are decoys, not production care systems."},"formative":true,"options":[{"id":"a","label":"A decoy that can reveal attacker methods"},{"id":"b","label":"The live appointment database"},{"id":"c","label":"Another name for impact scoring"},{"id":"d","label":"Automated fuzzing of clinical forms only"}],"prompt":"A honeypot is best described as:","questionId":"week7-session2-retrieval:s2-9","sourceQuestionId":"s2-9","sourceType":"single"},"id":"week7-session2-retrieval-q-9-s2-9","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"single-choice","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"correctOptionId":"a","feedback":{"correct":"Distributed IDS aggregates and coordinates detection points.","incorrect":"Distributed IDS aggregates and coordinates detection points."},"formative":true,"options":[{"id":"a","label":"Coordinates detection across multiple sensors or sites"},{"id":"b","label":"Means a single unused firewall rule"},{"id":"c","label":"Is identical to Accept on the risk register"},{"id":"d","label":"Replaces the need for any host logging"}],"prompt":"DIDS mainly:","questionId":"week7-session2-retrieval:s2-10","sourceQuestionId":"s2-10","sourceType":"single"},"id":"week7-session2-retrieval-q-10-s2-10","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"single-choice","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"format":"application/json","text":"```json\n{\n  \"weekNumber\": 7,\n  \"sessionNumber\": 2,\n  \"estimatedMinutes\": 15,\n  \"intro\": \"Low-stakes retrieval on detection versus prevention, testing methods, risk terminology and monitoring placements.\",\n  \"completionLinks\": [\n    {\n      \"label\": \"Risk management learning\",\n      \"path\": \"../risk-management-learning/\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"label\": \"Northbank risk register\",\n      \"path\": \"../risk-register/\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"label\": \"Testing methods\",\n      \"path\": \"../testing-methods/\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"label\": \"Detection and prevention\",\n      \"path\": \"../detection-prevention/\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"insecureTermsSummary\": [\n    \"Do not treat risk, threat and vulnerability as synonyms.\",\n    \"Do not treat penetration testing as identical to automated vulnerability scanning.\",\n    \"Do not claim \u201cinstalled\u201d alone proves effectiveness.\",\n    \"Detection alerts; prevention acts.\"\n  ]\n}\n```"},"id":"week7-session2-retrieval-source-remainder","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"markdown","version":"0.1.0"}],"id":"week7-session2-retrieval","metadata":{"activityType":"Retrieval quiz","href":null,"runtimeGlobal":"Week7Session2Retrieval","status":"available","summary":"Session 2 Retrieval Quiz","title":"Session 2 Retrieval Quiz"},"relationships":{"assets":[],"assignment":"formative-practice","learningOutcomes":["LO1"],"questions":[]},"schema":"lp.content.activity","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","version":"1.0.0"},{"blocks":[{"content":{"level":2,"text":"Testing and Monitoring Matching"},"id":"week7-testing-matching-title","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"heading","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"text":"Match each Northbank situation to the most suitable testing or monitoring measure. Use the accessible select lists (not drag-and-drop only). Justify every choice. Some scenarios allow a defensible alternative."},"id":"week7-testing-matching-intro","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"paragraph","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"format":"application/json","text":"```json\n{\n  \"weekNumber\": 7,\n  \"sessionNumber\": 2,\n  \"estimatedMinutes\": 25,\n  \"intro\": \"Match each Northbank situation to the most suitable testing or monitoring measure. Use the accessible select lists (not drag-and-drop only). Justify every choice. Some scenarios allow a defensible alternative.\",\n  \"measureOptions\": [\n    \"Penetration testing\",\n    \"Fuzzing\",\n    \"Security functionality testing\",\n    \"Sandboxing\",\n    \"NIDS\",\n    \"HIDS\",\n    \"DIDS\",\n    \"Anomaly-based detection\",\n    \"Signature-based detection\",\n    \"Honeypot\"\n  ],\n  \"scenarios\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"m1\",\n      \"text\": \"Northbank wants an authorised attempt to chain weaknesses in the remote-access path to clinical systems after MFA is deployed.\",\n      \"preferred\": \"Penetration testing\",\n      \"alternativeAnswers\": [],\n      \"altFullCredit\": false,\n      \"justificationMin\": 25,\n      \"preferredWhy\": \"An authorised simulated attack best tests realistic exploitation paths after controls are in place.\",\n      \"alternativeWhy\": \"\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"m2\",\n      \"text\": \"Developers changed an online referral form and need to see how it behaves with malformed and unexpected input.\",\n      \"preferred\": \"Fuzzing\",\n      \"alternativeAnswers\": [],\n      \"altFullCredit\": false,\n      \"justificationMin\": 25,\n      \"preferredWhy\": \"Fuzzing targets unexpected, invalid or unusual input handling.\",\n      \"alternativeWhy\": \"\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"m3\",\n      \"text\": \"Managers need evidence that the new role-based access rules block reception staff from clinical admin functions as specified.\",\n      \"preferred\": \"Security functionality testing\",\n      \"alternativeAnswers\": [\n        \"Penetration testing\"\n      ],\n      \"altFullCredit\": false,\n      \"justificationMin\": 25,\n      \"preferredWhy\": \"Security functionality testing directly checks that the control behaves as specified.\",\n      \"alternativeWhy\": \"A pentest might discover related access issues, but it is broader and less focused on proving the specified control behaviour.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"m4\",\n      \"text\": \"An unexpected email attachment arrives. The tutor will demonstrate observing it without running it on a clinical PC.\",\n      \"preferred\": \"Sandboxing\",\n      \"alternativeAnswers\": [],\n      \"altFullCredit\": false,\n      \"justificationMin\": 25,\n      \"preferredWhy\": \"Sandboxing isolates untrusted files for safer observation.\",\n      \"alternativeWhy\": \"\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"m5\",\n      \"text\": \"Analysts want visibility of suspicious traffic patterns moving across Northbank\u2019s internal network segments.\",\n      \"preferred\": \"NIDS\",\n      \"alternativeAnswers\": [\n        \"DIDS\"\n      ],\n      \"altFullCredit\": false,\n      \"justificationMin\": 25,\n      \"preferredWhy\": \"NIDS is placed to watch network traffic.\",\n      \"alternativeWhy\": \"DIDS can help if multiple sites must be coordinated, but the core need described is network traffic visibility, which NIDS addresses directly.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"m6\",\n      \"text\": \"A critical server that stores appointment data needs monitoring of local file integrity and unusual process activity on that host.\",\n      \"preferred\": \"HIDS\",\n      \"alternativeAnswers\": [],\n      \"altFullCredit\": false,\n      \"justificationMin\": 25,\n      \"preferredWhy\": \"HIDS watches activity on a specific host.\",\n      \"alternativeWhy\": \"\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"m7\",\n      \"text\": \"After hours, a reception PC starts making unusual outbound connections that do not match Northbank\u2019s normal clinic baseline, and no known malware name has been matched yet.\",\n      \"preferred\": \"Anomaly-based detection\",\n      \"alternativeAnswers\": [\n        \"NIDS\",\n        \"HIDS\"\n      ],\n      \"altFullCredit\": false,\n      \"justificationMin\": 25,\n      \"preferredWhy\": \"Anomaly-based detection is suited to behaviour that differs from baseline, including novel activity without a known signature.\",\n      \"alternativeWhy\": \"NIDS or HIDS may surface the traffic or host events, but the key requirement is recognising deviation from normal rather than matching a known pattern.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"m8\",\n      \"text\": \"Northbank\u2019s tools hold up-to-date indicators for a widely known ransomware family, and managers want alerts when those exact known patterns appear.\",\n      \"preferred\": \"Signature-based detection\",\n      \"alternativeAnswers\": [\n        \"Honeypot\",\n        \"NIDS\"\n      ],\n      \"altFullCredit\": false,\n      \"justificationMin\": 25,\n      \"preferredWhy\": \"Signature-based detection matches known attack patterns already in the signature set.\",\n      \"alternativeWhy\": \"A honeypot or NIDS can support monitoring, but they are less direct answers when the requirement is matching known signatures.\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```"},"id":"week7-testing-matching-source-remainder","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"markdown","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"formative":true,"prompt":"Complete this activity on the learner hub page, then write a short note to confirm you have finished.","questionId":"week7-testing-matching:learner-note","sourceQuestionId":"learner-note"},"id":"week7-testing-matching-learner-note","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"reflection","version":"0.1.0"}],"id":"week7-testing-matching","metadata":{"activityType":"Matching","href":null,"runtimeGlobal":"Week7TestingMatching","status":"available","summary":"Testing and Monitoring Matching","title":"Testing and Monitoring Matching"},"relationships":{"assets":[],"assignment":"formative-practice","learningOutcomes":["LO1"],"questions":[]},"schema":"lp.content.activity","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","version":"1.0.0"},{"blocks":[{"content":{"level":2,"text":"Justified Recommendation Practice"},"id":"week7-recommendation-practice-title","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"heading","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"format":"application/json","text":"```json\n{\n  \"weekNumber\": 7,\n  \"sessionNumber\": 2,\n  \"estimatedMinutes\": 25,\n  \"structureNote\": \"Full credit is not awarded for naming a measure alone. Build: (1) name the measure, (2) explain why it suits Northbank, (3) state how effectiveness is judged. Also compare an alternative and state cost or limitation.\",\n  \"scenario\": \"Northbank Community Health Partnership has a Medium-to-High risk that staff credentials for the appointment system could be stolen through phishing. Clinics are busy, budgets are limited, and managers want a recommendation they can justify to partners without claiming that installation alone proves success.\",\n  \"fields\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"measure\",\n      \"label\": \"1. Name the recommended measure\",\n      \"minChars\": 4,\n      \"feedbackKey\": \"named\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"whyOrg\",\n      \"label\": \"2. Why this suits Northbank (organisational context)\",\n      \"minChars\": 40,\n      \"feedbackKey\": \"context\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"effectiveness\",\n      \"label\": \"3. How effectiveness will be judged (measurable)\",\n      \"minChars\": 30,\n      \"feedbackKey\": \"effectiveness\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"registerRef\",\n      \"label\": \"Risk register reference (entry or asset name)\",\n      \"minChars\": 3,\n      \"feedbackKey\": \"named\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"costLimitation\",\n      \"label\": \"Cost or limitation\",\n      \"minChars\": 25,\n      \"feedbackKey\": \"limitation\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"alternative\",\n      \"label\": \"Compare an alternative measure\",\n      \"minChars\": 25,\n      \"feedbackKey\": \"comparison\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"whyAltLess\",\n      \"label\": \"Why the alternative is less effective here\",\n      \"minChars\": 25,\n      \"feedbackKey\": \"comparison\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"feedbackLabels\": {\n    \"named\": \"Named measure\",\n    \"context\": \"Contextual reason for Northbank\",\n    \"effectiveness\": \"Measurable effectiveness\",\n    \"limitation\": \"Cost or limitation\",\n    \"comparison\": \"Comparison with alternative\"\n  },\n  \"weakPatterns\": [\n    \"Naming a product with no Northbank reason\",\n    \"Effectiveness stated only as \u201cinstalled\u201d\",\n    \"No alternative considered\"\n  ]\n}\n```"},"id":"week7-recommendation-practice-source-remainder","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"markdown","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"formative":true,"prompt":"Complete this activity on the learner hub page, then write a short note to confirm you have finished.","questionId":"week7-recommendation-practice:learner-note","sourceQuestionId":"learner-note"},"id":"week7-recommendation-practice-learner-note","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"reflection","version":"0.1.0"}],"id":"week7-recommendation-practice","metadata":{"activityType":"Exam skills","href":null,"runtimeGlobal":"Week7RecommendationPractice","status":"available","summary":"Justified Recommendation Practice","title":"Justified Recommendation Practice"},"relationships":{"assets":[],"assignment":"formative-practice","learningOutcomes":["LO1"],"questions":[]},"schema":"lp.content.activity","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","version":"1.0.0"},{"blocks":[{"content":{"level":2,"text":"OCR-Style Timed Questions"},"id":"week7-ocr-question-practice-title","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"heading","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"commandWord":"Identify","correctOptionId":"a","feedback":{"correct":"","incorrect":""},"formative":true,"marks":1,"options":[{"id":"a","label":"Identify assets"},{"id":"b","label":"Review effectiveness measure"},{"id":"c","label":"Decide treatment with no asset list"},{"id":"d","label":"Install software without analysis"}],"prompt":"Identify the first stage in the risk-management sequence used in this unit.","questionId":"week7-ocr-question-practice:ocr7-1","sourceQuestionId":"ocr7-1","sourceType":"single"},"id":"week7-ocr-question-practice-q-1-ocr7-1","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"single-choice","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"commandWord":"Identify","correctOptionId":"a","feedback":{"correct":"","incorrect":""},"formative":true,"marks":1,"options":[{"id":"a","label":"Threat is a potential cause of harm; vulnerability is a weakness that could be exploited"},{"id":"b","label":"Threat and vulnerability mean the same thing"},{"id":"c","label":"Vulnerability is always an external attacker"},{"id":"d","label":"Risk is only another word for threat"}],"prompt":"Identify which statement correctly separates threat and vulnerability.","questionId":"week7-ocr-question-practice:ocr7-2","sourceQuestionId":"ocr7-2","sourceType":"single"},"id":"week7-ocr-question-practice-q-2-ocr7-2","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"single-choice","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"commandWord":"Describe","correctOptionId":"","feedback":{"correct":"","incorrect":""},"formative":true,"marks":2,"options":[],"prompt":"Describe what penetration testing is and state one limitation for Northbank.","questionId":"week7-ocr-question-practice:ocr7-3","sourceQuestionId":"ocr7-3","sourceType":"single"},"id":"week7-ocr-question-practice-q-3-ocr7-3","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"single-choice","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"commandWord":"Describe","correctOptionId":"","feedback":{"correct":"","incorrect":""},"formative":true,"marks":2,"options":[],"prompt":"Describe the purpose of fuzzing.","questionId":"week7-ocr-question-practice:ocr7-4","sourceQuestionId":"ocr7-4","sourceType":"single"},"id":"week7-ocr-question-practice-q-4-ocr7-4","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"single-choice","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"commandWord":"Explain","correctOptionId":"","feedback":{"correct":"","incorrect":""},"formative":true,"marks":2,"options":[],"prompt":"Explain the purpose of security functionality testing using a Northbank control example.","questionId":"week7-ocr-question-practice:ocr7-5","sourceQuestionId":"ocr7-5","sourceType":"single"},"id":"week7-ocr-question-practice-q-5-ocr7-5","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"single-choice","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"commandWord":"Explain","correctOptionId":"","feedback":{"correct":"","incorrect":""},"formative":true,"marks":2,"options":[],"prompt":"Explain why sandboxing may be used before opening an untrusted file.","questionId":"week7-ocr-question-practice:ocr7-6","sourceQuestionId":"ocr7-6","sourceType":"single"},"id":"week7-ocr-question-practice-q-6-ocr7-6","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"single-choice","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"commandWord":"Compare","correctOptionId":"","feedback":{"correct":"","incorrect":""},"formative":true,"marks":4,"options":[],"prompt":"Compare intrusion detection with intrusion prevention for Northbank.","questionId":"week7-ocr-question-practice:ocr7-7","sourceQuestionId":"ocr7-7","sourceType":"single"},"id":"week7-ocr-question-practice-q-7-ocr7-7","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"single-choice","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"commandWord":"Discuss","correctOptionId":"","feedback":{"correct":"","incorrect":""},"formative":true,"marks":3,"options":[],"prompt":"Discuss whether Northbank should Accept a Low-impact risk that a public leaflet PDF is briefly unavailable during updates.","questionId":"week7-ocr-question-practice:ocr7-8","sourceQuestionId":"ocr7-8","sourceType":"single"},"id":"week7-ocr-question-practice-q-8-ocr7-8","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"single-choice","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"commandWord":"Justify","correctOptionId":"","feedback":{"correct":"","incorrect":""},"formative":true,"marks":3,"options":[],"prompt":"Justify one monitoring or testing recommendation for Northbank\u2019s appointment-system phishing risk. Include how you would judge effectiveness.","questionId":"week7-ocr-question-practice:ocr7-9","sourceQuestionId":"ocr7-9","sourceType":"single"},"id":"week7-ocr-question-practice-q-9-ocr7-9","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"single-choice","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"format":"application/json","text":"```json\n{\n  \"weekNumber\": 7,\n  \"sessionNumber\": 2,\n  \"suggestedMinutes\": 25,\n  \"timingGuidance\": \"Use approximately one minute per mark where this helps you manage time. These are OCR-style practice questions, not official OCR examination questions.\",\n  \"beforeReminders\": [\n    \"Separate risk, threat and vulnerability.\",\n    \"Name testing methods with purpose and limitation where asked.\",\n    \"Detection alerts; prevention acts.\",\n    \"Recommendations need organisational context and measurable effectiveness, not \u201cinstalled\u201d alone.\",\n    \"Mark schemes stay hidden until you submit.\"\n  ],\n  \"northbankScenario\": \"Northbank Community Health Partnership runs community clinics with a shared appointment system, staff laptops and a public website. Partners expect proportionate cyber security. Budget is limited. Staff report phishing attempts. Managers are building a risk register and choosing testing and monitoring measures that they can justify.\"\n}\n```"},"id":"week7-ocr-question-practice-source-remainder","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"markdown","version":"0.1.0"}],"id":"week7-ocr-question-practice","metadata":{"activityType":"Exam skills","href":null,"runtimeGlobal":"Week7OcrPractice","status":"available","summary":"OCR-Style Timed Questions","title":"OCR-Style Timed Questions"},"relationships":{"assets":[],"assignment":"formative-practice","learningOutcomes":["LO1"],"questions":[]},"schema":"lp.content.activity","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","version":"1.0.0"},{"blocks":[{"content":{"level":2,"text":"Marking and Answer Improvement"},"id":"week7-answer-improvement-title","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"heading","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"format":"application/json","text":"```json\n{\n  \"weekNumber\": 7,\n  \"sessionNumber\": 2,\n  \"estimatedMinutes\": 25,\n  \"commonError\": \"Recommending a measure without organisational context, and treating effectiveness as \u201cwe installed it\u201d.\",\n  \"question\": {\n    \"commandWord\": \"Justify\",\n    \"marks\": 6,\n    \"prompt\": \"Justify one testing or monitoring recommendation for Northbank Community Health Partnership after phishing against the appointment system. Explain why it suits the organisation and how effectiveness would be judged.\"\n  },\n  \"sampleResponse\": {\n    \"text\": \"Northbank should use a firewall. It is ethical and stops hackers. Effectiveness is that it is installed. Therefore the risk is gone.\"\n  },\n  \"dominantIssues\": [\n    \"Names a measure with almost no Northbank organisational context\",\n    \"Does not link the recommendation to the phishing / appointment-system risk\",\n    \"Effectiveness is only \u201cinstalled\u201d\",\n    \"No limitation or cost considered\",\n    \"No comparison with an alternative\"\n  ],\n  \"markSchemePoints\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"c1\",\n      \"label\": \"Names a suitable testing or monitoring measure\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"c2\",\n      \"label\": \"Uses Northbank / phishing / appointment context\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"c3\",\n      \"label\": \"States a measurable effectiveness criterion\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"c4\",\n      \"label\": \"States a cost or limitation\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"c5\",\n      \"label\": \"Compares an alternative and why it is less suitable\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"workflowPrompts\": {\n    \"measure\": \"Identify the measure you would recommend instead (or refine the weak one).\",\n    \"evidence\": \"Highlight contextual evidence from Northbank that supports your recommendation.\",\n    \"justification\": \"Add a clear justification linking measure to organisational need.\",\n    \"effectiveness\": \"Add a measurable effectiveness statement (not only that something was installed).\",\n    \"limitation\": \"State one limitation or cost.\",\n    \"improved\": \"Write your improved full answer.\"\n  },\n  \"nextActionPrompt\": \"One next-exam action you will take when a Justify recommendation question appears.\",\n  \"modelAfterSubmit\": \"Stronger answers name a proportionate measure such as MFA with security functionality testing or targeted awareness plus monitoring, link it to Northbank\u2019s phishing exposure on the appointment system, define effectiveness using reduced successful credential theft or MFA challenge metrics, and admit staff-time cost while explaining why a vague \u201cinstall a firewall\u201d claim is weaker.\"\n}\n```"},"id":"week7-answer-improvement-source-remainder","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"markdown","version":"0.1.0"},{"content":{"formative":true,"prompt":"Complete this activity on the learner hub page, then write a short note to confirm you have finished.","questionId":"week7-answer-improvement:learner-note","sourceQuestionId":"learner-note"},"id":"week7-answer-improvement-learner-note","metadata":{},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.block","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","type":"reflection","version":"0.1.0"}],"id":"week7-answer-improvement","metadata":{"activityType":"Self marking","href":null,"runtimeGlobal":"Week7AnswerImprovement","status":"available","summary":"Marking and Answer Improvement","title":"Marking and Answer Improvement"},"relationships":{"assets":[],"assignment":"formative-practice","learningOutcomes":["LO1"],"questions":[]},"schema":"lp.content.activity","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","version":"1.0.0"}],"assets":[],"assignments":[{"id":"formative-practice","metadata":{"status":"available","title":"Formative Unit 3 practice"},"relationships":{},"schema":"lp.content.assignment","schemaVersion":"0.1.0","version":"0.1.0"}],"curriculum":{"id":"unit-3-cyber-security-curriculum","metadata":{"course":"